a-c=\"1D451\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-I-1D451\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(520,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D709\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-I-1D709\"></use></g></g><rect width=\"1189\" height=\"60\" x=\"120\" y=\"220\"></rect></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(3039.6,0) translate(0 -0.5)\"><use data-c=\"29\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-S3-29\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(6765.9,0)\"><use data-c=\"3D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-3D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(7821.7,0)\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"msup\" transform=\"translate(8599.7,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D703\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-I-1D703\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(502,413) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"1D45B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-I-1D45B\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg>','[]','[]','[\"standard-star-27773fe3\",\"star-edge-c61abbbd\",\"radiative-balance-267859a0\",\"quantum-geometry-9998956e\"]'),
(2009392,'hawking-radiation','black-holes','Hawking Radiation','<p>Hawking Radiation is theoretical thermal radiation predicted to be emitted by <strong>Black Holes</strong> due to quantum effects near the <strong>Event Horizon</strong>. Discovered by Stephen Hawking in 1974, it proved that black holes are not truly black but possess a <strong>Temperature</strong> and slowly leak energy into space. In university-level physics, Hawking radiation is the primary mechanism for black hole evaporation and the ultimate source of the <strong>Black Hole Information Paradox</strong>.</p>\n\n                    <h3>1. Vacuum Fluctuations near the Horizon</h3>\n                    <p>The physical origin of Hawking radiation lies in <strong>Quantum Field Theory</strong>. In a vacuum, pairs of virtual particles and anti-particles are constantly created and annihilated. Near an event horizon, it is possible for one member of the pair to fall into the black hole while the other escapes. To an outside observer, the black hole appears to have \"Emitted\" a real particle, while the infalling particle carries <strong>Negative Energy</strong>, reducing the black hole\'s mass.</p>\n\n                    <h3>2. The Hawking Temperature (TH)</h3>\n                    <p>Hawking proved that the emitted radiation has a perfect <strong>Blackbody Spectrum</strong> with a characteristic temperature: \\( T_H = \\frac{\\hbar c^3}{8\\pi G M k_B} \\). Crucially, the temperature is <em>inversely</em> proportional to the mass. Large black holes are extremely cold (colder than the <strong>CMB</strong>), while tiny black holes would be intensely hot and \"Glow\" with high-energy gamma rays before exploding.</p>\n\n                    <h3>3. Black Hole Evaporation</h3>\n                    <p>Because black holes emit radiation, they lose mass over time. The power output is given by the <strong>Stefan-Boltzmann Law</strong> applied to the horizon. As the black hole loses mass, its temperature <em>increases</em>, leading to faster radiation and even faster mass loss. This positive feedback loop results in the eventual <strong>Evaporation</strong> of the black hole in a final, violent burst of energy, a process that takes \\( \\sim 10^{67} \\) years for a solar-mass hole.</p>\n\n                    <h3>4. Information and Unitarity</h3>\n                    <p>Hawking radiation leads to a crisis in physics known as the <strong>Information Paradox</strong>. In quantum mechanics, evolution must be <strong>Unitary</strong> (information cannot be destroyed). However, Hawking\'s original calculation suggested the radiation was purely thermal and carried no information about the matter that formed the black hole. If the black hole disappears, the information appears to be lost, violating the fundamental laws of <strong>Quantum Interpretations</strong>.</p>\n\n                    <h3>5. Firewalls and the Page Curve</h3>\n                    <p>To resolve the paradox, some theorists proposed that the event horizon is actually a <strong>Firewall</strong>—a region of high-energy particles that \"incinerates\" anything falling in to preserve information. Others use the <strong>Page Curve</strong> to show how information might leak out of the black hole via <strong>Quantum Entanglement</strong> in the radiation. These debates are the current frontier of <strong>Quantum Gravity</strong>, searching for a way to reconcile GR with information theory.</p>\n\n                    <h3>6. Primordial Black Holes as a Test</h3>\n                    <p>While Hawking radiation has never been detected for stellar-mass black holes (it is too faint), it could be observable for <strong>Primordial Black Holes</strong> created in the Big Bang. If such tiny holes exist, their final stages of evaporation would be visible as high-energy flashes. Searching for these signals is a primary goal of <strong>Gamma-Ray Astronomy</strong>, as it would provide the first empirical proof the unification of thermodynamics and gravity.</p>','Hawking Radiation is theoretical thermal radiation predicted to be emitted by Black Holes due to quantum effects near the Event Horizon. Discovered by Stephen Hawking in 1974, it proved that black holes are not truly black but possess a Temperature and slowly leak energy into space. In university-level physics, Hawking radiation is the primary mechanism for black hole evaporation and the ultimate source of the Black Hole Information Paradox.','Hawking Radiation is theoretical thermal radiation predicted to be emitted by Black Holes due to quantum effects near the Event Horizon. Discovered by Stephen Hawking in 1974, it proved that black holes are not truly black but possess a Temperature and slowly leak energy into space. In university-level physics, Hawking radiation is the primary mechanism for black hole evaporation and the ultimate source of the Black Hole Information Paradox.','<svg style=\"color: #FFD700; vertical-align: -1.021ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"13.418ex\" height=\"3.245ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -983.2 5930.6 1434.2\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><defs><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-I-1D447\" d=\"M40 437Q21 437 21 445Q21 450 37 501T71 602L88 651Q93 669 101 677H569H659Q691 677 697 676T704 667Q704 661 687 553T668 444Q668 437 649 437Q640 437 637 437T631 442L629 445Q629 451 635 490T641 551Q641 586 628 604T573 629Q568 630 515 631Q469 631 457 630T439 622Q438 621 368 343T298 60Q298 48 386 46Q418 46 427 45T436 36Q436 31 433 22Q429 4 424 1L422 0Q419 0 415 0Q410 0 363 1T228 2Q99 2 64 0H49Q43 6 43 9T45 27Q49 40 55 46H83H94Q174 46 189 55Q190 56 191 56Q196 59 201 76T241 233Q258 301 269 344Q339 619 339 625Q339 630 310 630H279Q212 630 191 624Q146 614 121 583T67 467Q60 445 57 441T43 437H40Z\"></path><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-I-1D43B\" d=\"M228 637Q194 637 192 641Q191 643 191 649Q191 673 202 682Q204 683 219 683Q260 681 355 681Q389 681 418 681T463 682T483 682Q499 682 499 672Q499 670 497 658Q492 