215.6,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"29\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-29\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(422,289) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g></g><rect width=\"5241.2\" height=\"60\" x=\"120\" y=\"220\"></rect></g></g></g></svg>','[]','[]','[\"the-1-r-rule-a546ccff\",\"the-1-r-3-rule-4dd47615\",\"structural-anchor-7103594b\",\"compactness-factor-40f86b24\"]'),
(2009459,'freeze-out','dark-matter','Freeze-out and Relic Abundance','<p><strong>Freeze-out</strong> is the cosmological process that determines the <strong>Cosmic Abundance</strong> of a species of particle that was once in thermal equilibrium in the <strong>Early Universe</strong>. In university-level physics, freeze-out occurs when the expansion rate of the universe (\\( H \\)) exceeds the interaction rate (\\( \\Gamma \\)) of the particle. For <strong>Dark Matter</strong>, this process effectively \"sets\" the amount of invisible mass we see today, providing the physical mechanism for the <strong>WIMP Miracle</strong>.</p>\n\n                    <h3>1. Thermal Equilibrium in the Plasma</h3>\n                    <p>In the first fraction of a second after the <strong>Big Bang</strong>, the universe was hot enough for <strong>WIMPs</strong> to be created and annihilated constantly via weak-force interactions (\\( \\chi\\bar{\\chi} \\leftrightarrow q\\bar{q} \\)). In this state, the number density follows a <strong>Maxwell-Boltzmann</strong> distribution. The particles are in perfect thermal contact with the surrounding 4D plasma, and their density is a simple function of the temperature \\( T \\).</p>\n\n                    <h3>2. The Condition for Decoupling</h3>\n                    <p>As the universe expands, it cools, and the interaction rate \\( \\Gamma = n \\langle \\sigma v \\rangle \\) decreases. Simultaneously, the <strong>Expansion History</strong> is governed by the <strong>Hubble Parameter</strong> (\\( H \\)). When \\( \\Gamma \\lt H \\), the particles can no longer find each other to annihilate before being pulled apart by the stretching of space. this is moment of <strong>Freeze-out</strong>, after which the number of particles in a \"comoving volume\" remains constant.</p>\n\n                    <h3>3. Solving the Boltzmann Equation</h3>\n                    <p>The exact timing and result of freeze-out are found by solving the <strong>Boltzmann Equation</strong>:\n                    \\[ \\frac{dn}{dt} + 3Hn = -\\langle \\sigma v \\rangle (n^2 - n_{eq}^2) \\]\n                    This equation tracks the \"Tug-of-War\" between the annihilation that tries to reach equilibrium and the expansion that dilutes the density. The result is the \"Relic Abundance\"—the leftover density of dark matter that populates the modern .</p>\n\n                    <h3>4. Cross-Section and Density</h3>\n                    <p>A profound university-level result of freeze-out is the <strong>Inverse Relationship</strong>: a particle with a <em>larger</em> annihilation cross-section stays in equilibrium longer and therefore has a <em>smaller</em> final density. This allows physicists to \"Calculate\" the subatomic <strong>Strong Interaction</strong> or weak-force properties of dark matter just by measuring the <strong>Cosmological Density</strong> (\\( \\Omega_{DM} \\)) in the sky.</p>\n\n                    <h3>5. Relativistic vs. Non-Relativistic Freeze-out</h3>\n                    <p>Freeze-out depends on whether the particle is relativistic when it decouples:\n                        <ul>\n                            <li><strong>Cold Dark Matter (CDM):</strong> Freeze-out occurs when \\( T \\lt m_\\chi \\). This leads to a low density.</li>\n                            <li><strong>Hot Dark Matter (HDM):</strong> Freeze-out occurs when \\( T \\gt m_\\chi \\). This leads to a high density (like neutrinos).</li>\n                        </ul>\n                    The observed abundance of 27% suggests that dark matter must be Cold, anchoring the <strong>\\(\\Lambda\\)-CDM</strong> model.</p>\n\n                    <h3>6. Epistemic Status: The Relic Map</h3>\n                    <p>Freeze-out assumes a standard <strong>Expansion History</strong>. If the universe underwent a non-standard phase (like a late <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/cosmic-inflation\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Cosmic Inflation</strong></a>) after dark matter formed, the relic abundance would be changed. This makes freeze-out a sensitive \"Clock\" for the <strong>History of the Universe</strong>, linking the subatomic contents of the vacuum to the global 4D geometry of the Big Bang.</p>','Freeze-out is the cosmological process that determines the Cosmic Abundance of a species of particle that was once in thermal equilibrium in the Early Universe. In university-level physics, freeze-out occurs when the expansion rate of the universe exceeds the interaction rate of the particle. For Dark Matter, this process effectively \"sets\" the amount of invisible mass we see today, providing the physical mechanism for the WIMP Miracle.','Freeze-out is the cosmological process that determines the Cosmic Abundance of a species of particle that was once in thermal equilibrium in the Early Universe. In university-level physics, freeze-out occurs when the expansion rate of the universe (<svg style=\"color: #FFD700; vertical-align: 0;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"2.009ex\" height=\"1.545ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -683 888 683\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><defs><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-I-1D43B\" d=\"M228 637Q194 637 192 641Q191 643 191 649Q191 673 202 682Q204 683 219 683Q260 681 355 681Q389 681 418 681T463 682T483 682Q499 682 499 672Q499 670 497 658Q492 641 487 638H485Q483 638 480 638T473 638T464 637T455 637Q416 636 405 634T387 623Q384 619 355 500Q348 474 340 442T328 395L324 380Q324 378 469 378H614L615 381Q615 384 646 504Q674 619 674 627T617 637Q594 637 587 639T580 648Q580 650 582 660Q586 677 588 679T604 682Q609 682 646 681T740 680Q802 680 835 681T871 682Q888 682 888 672Q888 645 876 638H874Q872 638 869 638T862 638T853 637T844 637Q805 636 794 634T776 623Q773 618 704 340T634 58Q634 51 638 51Q646 48 692 46H723Q729 38 729 37T726 19Q722 6 716 0H701Q664 2 567 2Q533 2 504 2T458 2T437 1Q420 1 420 10Q420 15 423 24Q428 43 433 45Q437 46 448 46H454Q481 46 514 49Q520 50 522 50T528 55T534 64T540 82T547