db2c\",\"radial-shift-0b38f1d1\"]'),
(2009484,'cosmological-redshift','hubbles-law','Cosmological Redshift','<p>Cosmological Redshift (\\( z \\)) is the increase in the wavelength of <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/electromagnetic-radiation\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Electromagnetic Radiation</strong></a> due to the expansion of the  of space. In university-level astrophysics, it is distinguished from the Doppler effect; while Doppler shift arises from motion <em>through</em> space, cosmological redshift is a <strong>Metric Phenomenon</strong> caused by the stretching of space itself during the light\'s time of flight.</p>\n\n                    <h3>1. The Scale Factor Relation</h3>\n                    <p>The redshift is directly related to the <strong>Scale Factor</strong> (\\( a \\)) of the universe. If light is emitted when the universe had scale factor \\( a_{emit} \\) and detected today (\\( a_0 \\)), the redshift is given by:\n                    \\[ 1 + z = \\frac{a_0}{a_{emit}} \\]\n                    This implies that a galaxy with \\( z = 1 \\) is being observed as it was when the universe was half its current linear size. Redshift serves as the \"Cosmic Ruler\" for the <strong>History of the Universe</strong>.</p>\n\n                    <h3>2. Metric Stretching of Waves</h3>\n                    <p>As a photon travels through the expanding 4D <strong>Block Universe</strong>, its wavelength (\\( \\lambda \\)) is \"dragged\" along by the 4D metric. Because the 4D distance between wave crests increases, the energy of the photon (\\( E = hc/\\lambda \\)) decreases. This loss of energy is transferred to the gravitational field of the , a hallmark of <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/general-relativity\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>General Relativity</strong></a> where energy is not globally conserved in expanding space.</p>\n\n                    <h3>3. Redshift as a Measure of Time</h3>\n                    <p>Because the expansion rate is determined by the <strong>Friedmann Equations</strong>, redshift can be mapped to look-back time. High-redshift objects (like the first galaxies at \\( z \\sim 15 \\)) allow astronomers to \"look back in time\" to the era of <strong>Reionization</strong>. The <strong>Cosmic Microwave Background (CMB)</strong>, with \\( z \\approx 1100 \\), represents the ultimate  of observable light.</p>\n\n                    <h3>4. Distinction from Peculiar Velocity</h3>\n                    <p>In the \"Standard Model\" of cosmology, the total observed redshift includes a small contribution from <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/peculiar-velocities\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Peculiar Velocities</strong></a> (Doppler shift).\n                    \\[ (1+z_{obs}) = (1+z_{cosmo})(1+z_{pec}) \\]\n                    For distant galaxies, the cosmological term dominates, allowing for the derivation of the <strong>Hubble-Lemaître Law</strong>. Accounting for this distinction is essential for 4D <strong>Analytical Mechanics</strong> of galaxy clusters.</p>\n\n                    <h3>5. Gravitational Redshift Comparison</h3>\n                    <p>Cosmological redshift is often compared to <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/gravitational-redshift-theory\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Gravitational Redshift</strong></a>. While both are metric effects, gravitational redshift occurs due to <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/proper-time\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Proper Time</strong></a> differences in a static 4D potential (like near a <strong>Black Hole</strong>). Cosmological redshift is dynamic, reflecting the global <strong>Expansion History</strong> of the entire .</p>\n\n                    <h3>6. Epistemic Status: The Primary Observable</h3>\n                    <p>Redshift is the most reliable <strong>Epistemic</strong> tool in cosmology. We do not measure distance directly; we measure the shift in spectral lines. Our <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/scientific-realism\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Scientific Realism</strong></a> about the <strong>Big Bang</strong> is anchored in the precise mapping of these shifts, proving that the 4D <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/spacetime-causal-topology\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Causal Topology</strong></a> of the universe is a expanding, evolving geometric history.</p>','Cosmological Redshift is the increase in the wavelength of Electromagnetic Radiation due to the expansion of the of space. In university-level astrophysics, it is distinguished from the Doppler effect; while Doppler shift arises from motion through space, cosmological redshift is a Metric Phenomenon caused by the stretching of space itself during the light\'s time of flight. The redshift is directly related to the Scale Factor of the universe.','Cosmological Redshift (<svg style=\"color: #FFD700; vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.052ex\" height=\"1.025ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -442 465 453\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><defs><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-I-1D467\" d=\"M347 338Q337 338 294 349T231 360Q211 360 197 356T174 346T162 335T155 324L153 320Q150 317 138 317Q117 317 117 325Q117 330 120 339Q133 378 163 406T229 440Q241 442 246 442Q271 442 291 425T329 392T367 375Q389 375 411 408T434 441Q435 442 449 442H462Q468 436 468 434Q468 430 463 420T449 399T432 377T418 358L411 349Q368 298 275 214T160 106L148 94L163 93Q185 93 227 82T290 71Q328 71 360 90T402 140Q406 149 409 151T424 153Q443 153 443 143Q443 138 442 134Q425 72 376 31T278 -11Q252 -11 232 6T193 40T155 57Q111 57 76 -3Q70 -11 59 -11H54H41Q35 -5 35 -2Q35 13 93 84Q132 129 225 214T340 322Q352 338 347 338Z\"></path></defs><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D467\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-I-1D467\"></use></g></g></g></svg>) is the increase in the wavelength of Electromagnetic Radiation due to the expansion of the  of space. In university-level astrophysics, it is distinguished from the Doppler effect; while Doppler shift arises from motion through space, cosmological redshift is a Metric Phenomenon caused by the stretching of space itself during the light\'s time of flight. The redshift is directly related to the Scale Factor (<svg style=\"color: #FFD700; vertical-align: -0.023ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.197ex\" height=\"1.02ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -441 529 451\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><defs><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-I-1D44E\" d=\"M33 157Q33 258 109 349T280 441Q331 441 370 392Q386 422 416 422Q429 422 439 414T449 394Q449 381 412 234T374 68Q374 43 381 35T402 26Q411 27 422 35Q443 55 463 131Q469 151 473 152Q475 153 483 153H487Q506 153 506 144Q506 138 501 117T481 63T449 13Q436 0 417 -8Q409 -10 393 -10Q359 -10 336 5T306 36L300 51Q299 52 296 50Q294 48 292 46Q233 -10 172 -10Q117 -10 75 30T33 157ZM351 328Q351 334 346 350T323 385T277 405Q242 405 210 374T160 293Q131 214 119 129Q119 126 119 118T118 106Q118 61 136 44T179 26Q217 26 254 59T298 110Q300 114 325 217T351 328Z\"></path></defs><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D44E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-I-1D44E\"></use></g></g></g></svg>) of the universe.','<svg style=\"color: #FFD700; vertical-align: -1.909ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"13.626ex\" height=\"4.436ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -1117 6022.6 1960.8\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><defs><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-N-31\" d=\"M213 578L200 573Q186 568 160 563T102 556H83V602H102Q149 604 189 617T245 641T273 663Q275 666 285 666Q294 666 302 660V361L303 61Q310 54 315 52T339 48T401 46H427V0H416Q395 3 257 3Q121 3 100 0H88V46H114Q136 46 152 46T177 47T193 50T201 52T207 57T213 61V578Z\"></path><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-N-2B\" d=\"M56 237T56 250T70 270H369V420L370 570Q380 583 389 583Q402 583 409 568V