0\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-I-1D450\"></use></g></g></g></g></g></svg>','[]','[]','[\"random-motion-1130c323\",\"gravity-tugs-28945d6c\",\"andromeda-link-dafa7383\",\"map-errors-d89907c4\"]'),
(2009489,'hubble-lemaitre-law','hubbles-law','The Hubble-Lemaître Law','<p>The <strong>Hubble-Lemaître Law</strong> (formerly Hubble\'s Law) is the observation that the recessional velocity of a galaxy is directly proportional to its distance from the observer. In university-level cosmology, this law is the empirical proof the <strong>Metric Expansion</strong> of space. It identifies the  as non-static, providing the <strong>Geometric Origin</strong> for the <strong>Big Bang</strong> theory and the primary method for mapping the 4D <strong>Block Universe</strong>.</p>\n\n                    <h3>1. The Linear Relation: v = H d</h3>\n                    <p>The law is mathematically expressed as:\n                    \\[ v = H_0 d \\]\n                    Where \\( v \\) is the recessional velocity (usually derived from <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/cosmological-redshift\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Cosmological Redshift</strong></a>) and \\( d \\) is the <strong>Proper Distance</strong>. This linear relationship is a direct consequence of a <strong>Homogeneous</strong> and <strong>Isotropic</strong> 4D expansion. It implies that every point in the universe appears to be the center of expansion, a hallmark of the <strong>Principle of Relativity</strong>.</p>\n\n                    <h3>2. History and Lemaître\'s Role</h3>\n                    <p>While Edwin Hubble provided the most robust observational data in 1929, Georges Lemaître had theoretically derived the law from the <strong>Friedmann Equations</strong> in 1927. The 2018 renaming to the \"Hubble-Lemaître Law\" acknowledges this 4D unification of theory and observation. It represents the <strong>Epistemic</strong> shift from a \"Steady State\"  to an evolving, dynamic .</p>\n\n                    <h3>3. The Cosmological Interpretation</h3>\n                    <p>A university-level nuance is that the \"velocity\" in the law is not a traditional Doppler speed. At large distances, galaxies move away from us faster than the <strong>Velocity of Light</strong> (\\( v \\gt c \\)). This does not violate <strong>Special Relativity</strong> because the galaxies are not moving <em>through</em> space; the 4D metric between us is growing. This distinction defines the <strong>observable universe</strong> boundary.</p>\n\n                    <h3>4. Calibration via Standard Candles</h3>\n                    <p>To establish the law, astronomers use the <strong>Cosmic Distance Ladder</strong>. This involves using \"Standard Candles\" like <strong>Cepheid Variables</strong> and <strong>Type Ia Supernovae</strong> to measure \\( d \\) and spectral lines to measure \\( v \\). The slope of the resulting line is the <strong>Hubble Constant</strong> (\\( H_0 \\)), the \"Speedometer\" that sets the scale for the entire <strong>Cosmic Budget</strong>.</p>\n\n                    <h3>5. Deviations and the Hubble Parameter</h3>\n                    <p>The law \\( v = H_0 d \\) is only the \"Low-z\" linear approximation of a deeper 4D law. For distant galaxies, the <strong>Expansion History</strong> is non-linear due to the changing density of matter and <strong>Dark Energy</strong>. \n                    \\[ v \\approx H(z) d(z) \\]\n                    Measuring these deviations allows cosmologists to track the transition from decelerating to <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/accelerated-expansion\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Accelerated Expansion</strong></a>, dictating the <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/total-dynamics\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Total Dynamics</strong></a> of the cosmos.</p>\n\n                    <h3>6. Epistemic Status: The Fundamental Proof</h3>\n                    <p>The Hubble-Lemaître Law is the most important 4D observation in the history of science. It destroyed the <strong>Ontology</strong> of a static, eternal universe. By proving that the  is growing, it forces us to accept a \"Beginning\" (the Big Bang) and an \"End.\" It anchors <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/scientific-realism\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Scientific Realism</strong></a> in the belief that the large-scale structure of the  is a single, unfolding geometric event.</p>','The Hubble-Lemaître Law (formerly Hubble\'s Law) is the observation that the recessional velocity of a galaxy is directly proportional to its distance from the observer. In university-level cosmology, this law is the empirical proof the Metric Expansion of space. It identifies the as non-static, providing the Geometric Origin for the Big Bang theory and the primary method for mapping the 4D Block Universe.','The Hubble-Lemaître Law (formerly Hubble\'s Law) is the observation that the recessional velocity of a galaxy is directly proportional to its distance from the observer. In university-level cosmology, this law is the empirical proof the Metric Expansion of space. It identifies the  as non-static, providing the Geometric Origin for the Big Bang theory and the primary method for mapping the 4D Block Universe.','<svg style=\"color: #FFD700; vertical-align: -0.375ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"8.159ex\" height=\"1.945ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -694 3606.1 859.6\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><defs><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-I-1D463\" d=\"M173 380Q173 405 154 405Q130 405 104 376T61 287Q60 286 59 284T58 281T56 279T53 278T49 278T41 278H27Q21 284 21 287Q21 294 29 316T53 368T97 419T160 441Q202 441 225 417T249 361Q249 344 246 335Q246 329 231 291T200 202T182 113Q182 86 187 69Q200 26 250 26Q287 26 319 60T369 139T398 222T409 277Q409 300 401 317T383 343T365 361T357 383Q357 405 376 424T417 443Q436 443 451 425T467 367Q467 340 455 284T418 159T347 40T241 -11Q177 -11 139 22Q102 54 102 117Q102 148 110 181T151 298Q173 362 173 380Z\"></path><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-N-3D\" d=\"M56 347Q56 360 70 367H707Q722 359 722 347Q722 336 708 328L390 327H72Q56 332 56 347ZM56 153Q56 168 72 173H708Q722 163 722 153Q722 140 707 133H70Q56 140 56 153Z\"></path><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX