(2009490,'redshift-definition','hubbles-law','Redshift Definition and Measurement','<p><strong>Redshift</strong> (\\( z \\)) is defined as the fractional increase in the wavelength of light (or other radiation) relative to its emitted wavelength. In university-level physics, redshift is the primary \"Universal Coordinate\" for the . It quantifies the 4D stretching of the <strong>Block Universe</strong> and provides the raw data for the <strong>Hubble-Lemaître Law</strong>, serving as the definitive link between spectroscopy and <strong>Physical Cosmology</strong>.</p>\n\n                    <h3>1. The Mathematical Definition</h3>\n                    <p>The redshift is calculated from the shift in spectral lines:\n                    \\[ z = \\frac{\\lambda_{obs} - \\lambda_{em}}{\\lambda_{em}} = \\frac{\\Delta \\lambda}{\\lambda} \\]\n                    If \\( z \\gt 0 \\), the light is \"Redshifted\" (longer wavelength). If \\( z \\lt 0 \\), it is \"Blueshifted.\" In the , \\( z \\) is a dimensionless number that tracks the \"Expansion Factor\" (\\( 1+z \\)) of space between two events.</p>\n\n                    <h3>2. Three Types of Redshift</h3>\n                    <p>In 4D <strong>Theoretical Physics</strong>, we distinguish between:\n                        <ul>\n                            <li><strong>Doppler Redshift:</strong> Caused by relative motion <em>through</em> space (Peculiar Velocities).</li>\n                            <li><strong>Cosmological Redshift:</strong> Caused by the <strong>Metric Expansion</strong> of space itself.</li>\n                            <li><strong>Gravitational Redshift:</strong> Caused by light climbing out of a 4D potential well (e.g., near a <strong>White Dwarf</strong>).</li>\n                        </ul>\n                    Untangling these three is the <strong>Epistemic</strong> challenge of modern <strong>Astrophysics</strong>.</p>\n\n                    <h3>3. Measurement via Absorption Lines</h3>\n                    <p>To measure \\( z \\), astronomers look for known \"Fingers\" in the spectrum—absorption or emission lines from the <strong>Standard Model</strong> elements (like Hydrogen alpha or Calcium H&K). By comparing the laboratory wavelength to the observed wavelength, they find the precise 4D shift of the galaxy. This anchors <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/scientific-realism\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Scientific Realism</strong></a> in the subatomic stability of atoms across the .</p>\n\n                    <h3>4. Redshift and Energy Density</h3>\n                    <p>Redshift is coupled to the <strong>Energy Density</strong> of the cosmic fluid. According to the <strong>Friedmann Equations</strong>, the 4D expansion stretches the wavelength of individual photons, causing radiation density to drop as \\( (1+z)^4 \\). This rapid dilution is the physical reason why the <strong>Early Universe</strong> cooled down, dictating the <strong>History of the Universe</strong> after the Big Bang.</p>\n\n                    <h3>5. The Redshift-Distance Relation</h3>\n                    <p>Redshift is the \"Distance\" variable of choice in 4D cosmology. Because we measure \\( z \\) directly, we use it to define \"Redshift Space.\" In this 4D mapping, a galaxy\'s position is given by its \\( z \\) value. Correcting for <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/peculiar-velocities\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Peculiar Velocities</strong></a> is what allows us to translate these 4D maps into the true 3D <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/spacetime-causal-topology\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Causal Topology</strong></a> of the cosmos.</p>\n\n                    <h3>6. Epistemic Status: The Cosmic Clock</h3>\n                    <p>Redshift is the \"Cosmic Clock\" that tracks the 4D aging of the universe. It is our most robust <strong>Ontological</strong> link to the past. By observing high-\\( z \\) objects, we are seeing the <strong>History of the Universe</strong> in real-time. Redshift represents the <strong>Epistemic</strong> limit of our sight, ending at the <strong>CMB</strong> (\\( z \\approx 1100 \\)), where the  first became transparent to light.</p>','Redshift is defined as the fractional increase in the wavelength of light (or other radiation) relative to its emitted wavelength. In university-level physics, redshift is the primary \"Universal Coordinate\" for the. It quantifies the 4D stretching of the Block Universe and provides the raw data for the Hubble-Lemaître Law, serving as the definitive link between spectroscopy and Physical Cosmology.','Redshift (<svg style=\"color: #FFD700; vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.052ex\" height=\"1.025ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -442 465 453\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><defs><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-I-1D467\" d=\"M347 338Q337 338 294 349T231 360Q211 360 197 356T174 346T162 335T155 324L153 320Q150 317 138 317Q117 317 117 325Q117 330 120 339Q133 378 163 406T229 440Q241 442 246 442Q271 442 291 425T329 392T367 375Q389 375 411 408T434 441Q435 442 449 442H462Q468 436 468 434Q468 430 463 420T449 399T432 377T418 358L411 349Q368 298 275 214T160 106L148 94L163 93Q185 93 227 82T290 71Q328 71 360 90T402 140Q406 149 409 151T424 153Q443 153 443 143Q443 138 442 134Q425 72 376 31T278 -11Q252 -11 232 6T193 40T155 57Q111 57 76 -3Q70 -11 59 -11H54H41Q35 -5 35 -2Q35 13 93 84Q132 129 225 214T340 322Q352 338 347 338Z\"></path></defs><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D467\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-I-1D467\"></use></g></g></g></svg>) is defined as the fractional increase in the wavelength of light (or other radiation) relative to its emitted wavelength. In university-level physics, redshift is the primary \"Universal Coordinate\" for the . It quantifies the 4D stretching of the Block Universe and provides the raw data