0Q202 343 195 315T187 232V168V108Q187 78 188 68T191 55T200 49Q221 46 249 46H265V0H257L234 1Q210 2 183 2T145 3Q42 3 33 0H25V46H41Z\"></path></defs><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"3C\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-3C\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(1055.8,0)\"><use data-c=\"30\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-30\"></use><use data-c=\"2E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-2E\" transform=\"translate(500,0)\"></use><use data-c=\"35\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-35\" transform=\"translate(778,0)\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mtext\" transform=\"translate(2333.8,0)\"><use data-c=\"A0\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-A0\"></use><use data-c=\"66\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-66\" transform=\"translate(250,0)\"></use><use data-c=\"6D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-6D\" transform=\"translate(556,0)\"></use></g></g></g></svg>). In the context of Neutron Stars, this short-range repulsion is the vital \"Second Pillar\" of support, preventing gravity from crushing the star even after Neutron Degeneracy Pressure has been overcome. In university-level nuclear physics, the repulsion is modeled as a \"Hard Core\" potential.','<svg style=\"color: #FFD700; vertical-align: 0;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"6.662ex\" height=\"1.595ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -705 2944.8 705\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><defs><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-N-223C\" d=\"M55 166Q55 241 101 304T222 367Q260 367 296 349T362 304T421 252T484 208T554 189Q616 189 655 236T694 338Q694 350 698 358T708 367Q722 367 722 334Q722 260 677 197T562 134H554Q517 134 481 152T414 196T355 248T292 293T223 311Q179 311 145 286Q109 257 96 218T80 156T69 133Q55 133 55 166Z\"></path><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-N-31\" d=\"M213 578L200 573Q186 568 160 563T102 556H83V602H102Q149 604 189 617T245 641T273 663Q275 666 285 666Q294 666 302 660V361L303 61Q310 54 315 52T339 48T401 46H42