sform=\"translate(3471.1,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2F\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-2F\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(3971.1,0)\"><use data-c=\"33\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-33\"></use></g></g></g></svg>','[]','[]','[\"driving-force-8a309e17\",\"energy-loss-44d93e96\",\"relativistic-push-92ee709a\"]'),
(2009512,'matter-domination','physical-cosmology','The Matter-Dominated Era','<p>The <strong>Matter-Dominated Era</strong> followed the radiation epoch, lasting from approximately 50,000 years to 9 billion years after the Big Bang. In university-level 4D <strong>Physical Cosmology</strong>, this era is characterized by the 4D <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/total-dynamics\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Total Dynamics</strong></a> of \"Dust\"—non-relativistic matter whose 4D <strong>Energy Density</strong> is governed purely by the volume expansion of the .</p>\n\n                  <h3>1. Scaling and the Dust Model</h3>\n                  <p>In cosmology, ordinary matter and 4D <strong>Dark Matter</strong> are modeled as a fluid with zero pressure (\\( P=0 \\)). Consequently, the 4D <strong>Energy Density</strong> dilutes exactly as the volume: \\( \\rho_m \\propto a^{-3} \\). This 4D <strong>Logical Basis</strong> allowed the expansion rate to slow down (decelerate) significantly compared to the radiation era, providing the 4D <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/spacetime-causal-topology\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Causal Topology</strong></a> necessary for the growth of structure.</p>\n\n                  <h3>2. Structure Formation (\\( a \\propto t^{2/3} \\))</h3>\n                  <p>During the matter era, the scale factor evolved as \\( a(t) \\propto t^{2/3} \\). Under this slower 4D <strong>Expansion Rate</strong>, small 4D <strong>Density Fluctuations</strong> from the early universe could grow via 4D <strong>Gravitational Instability</strong>. this is era of <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/scientific-realism\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Scientific Realism</strong></a> for galaxies and large-scale structures; the \"Stuff\" of the universe finally clumped together to form the 4D <strong>Cosmic Web</strong> we see today.</p>\n\n                  <h3>3. The Deceleration Phase</h3>\n                  <p>Because matter is attractive and has no opposing pressure, the 4D <strong>Matter Era</strong> was a period of <strong>Decelerated Expansion</strong>. Physicists measure this using the <strong>Deceleration Parameter</strong> (\\( q \\)). For a flat, matter-only universe (Einstein-de Sitter), \\( q = 1/2 \\). This phase lasted until 4D <strong>Dark Energy</strong>—which does not dilute—eventually overtook matter density, triggering the 4D <strong>Current Epoch</strong> of acceleration.</p>','The Matter-Dominated Era followed the radiation epoch, lasting from approximately 50,000 years to 9 billion years after the Big Bang. In university-level 4D Physical Cosmology, this era is characterized by the 4D Total Dynamics of \"Dust\"—non-relativistic matter whose 4D Energy Density is governed purely by the volume expansion of the. In cosmology, ordinary matter and 4D Dark Matter are modeled as a fluid with zero pressure.','The Matter-Dominated Era followed the radiation epoch, lasting from approximately 50,000 years to 9 billion years after the Big Bang. In university-level 4D Physical Cosmology, this era is characterized by the 4D Total Dynamics of \"Dust\"—non-relativistic matter whose 4D Energy Density is governed purely by the volume expansion of the . In cosmology, ordinary matter and 4D Dark Matter are modeled as a fluid with zero pressure (<svg style=\"color: #FFD700; vertical-align: -0.186ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"5.847ex\" height=\"1.731ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -683 2584.6 765\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><defs><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-I-1D443\" d=\"M287 628Q287 635 230 637Q206 637 199 638T192 648Q192 649 194 659Q200 679 203 681T397 683Q587 682 600 680Q664 669 707 631T751 530Q751 453 685 389Q616 321 507 303Q500 302 402 301H307L277 182Q247 66 247 59Q247 55 248 54T255 50T272 48T305 46H336Q342 37 342 35Q342 19 335 5Q330 0 319 0Q316 0 282 1T182 2Q120 2 87 2T51 1Q33 1 33 11Q33 13 36 25Q40 41 44 43T67 46Q94 46 127 49Q141 52 146 61Q149 65 218 339T287 628ZM645 554Q645 567 643 575T634 597T609 619T560 635Q553 636 480 637Q463 637 445 637T416 636T404 636Q391 635 386 627Q384 621 367 550T332 412T314 344Q314 342 395 342H407H430Q542 342 590 392Q617 419 631 471T645 554Z\"></path><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-N-3D\" d=\"M56 347Q56 360 70 367H707Q722 359 722 347Q722 336 708 328L390 327H72Q56 332 56 347ZM56 153Q56 168 72 173H708Q722 163 722 153Q722 140 707 133H70Q56 140 56 153Z\"></path><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-N-30\" d=\"M96 585Q152 666 249 666Q297 666 345 640T423 548Q460 465 460 320Q460 165 417 83Q397 41 362 16T301 -15T250 -22Q224 -22 198 -16T137 16T82 83Q39 165 39 320Q39 494 96 585ZM321 597Q291 629 250 629Q208 629 178 597Q153 571 145 525T137 333Q137 175 145 125T181 46Q209 16 250 16Q290 16 318 46Q347 76 354 130T362 333Q362 478 354 524T321 597Z\"></path></defs><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D443\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-I-1D443\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1028.8,0)\"><use data-c=\"3D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-3D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(2084.6,0)\"><use data-c=\"30\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-30\"></use></g></g></g></svg>).','<svg style=\"color: #FFD700; vertical-align: -0.186ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"5.847ex\" height=\"1.731ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -683 2584.6 765\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><defs><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-I-1D443\" d=\"M287 628Q287 635 230 637Q206 637 199 638T192 648Q192 649 194 659Q200 679 203 681T397 683Q587 682 600 680Q664 669 707 631T751 530Q751 453 685 389Q616 321 507 303Q500 302 402 301H307L277 182Q247 66 247 59Q247 55 248 54T255 50T272 48T305 46H336Q342 37 342 35Q342 19 335 5Q330 0 319 0Q316 0 282 1T182 2Q120 2 87 2T51 1Q33 1 33 11Q33 13 36 25Q40 41 44 43T67 46Q94 46 127 49Q141 52 146 61Q149 65 218 339T287 628ZM645 554Q645 567 643 575T634 597T609 619T560 635Q553 636 480 637Q463 637 445 637T416 636T404 636Q391 635 386 627Q384 621 367 550T332 412T314 344Q314 342 395 342H407H430Q542 342 590 392Q617 419 631 471T645 554Z\"></path><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-N-3D\" d=\"M56 347Q56 360 70 367H707Q722 359 722 347Q722 336 708 328L390 327H72Q56 332 56 347ZM56 153Q56 168 72 173H708Q722 163 722 153Q722 140 707 133H70Q56 140 56 153Z\"></path><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-N-30\" d=\"M96 585Q152 666 249 666Q297 666 345 640T423 548Q460 465 460 320Q460 165 417 83Q397 41 362 16T301 -15T250 -22Q224 -22 198 -16T137 16T82 83Q39 165 39 320Q39 494 96 585ZM321 597Q291 629 250 629Q208 629 178 597Q153 571 145 525T137 333Q137 175 145 125T181 46Q209 16 250 16Q290 16 318 46Q347 76 354 130T362 333Q362 478 354 524T321 597Z\"></path></defs><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D443\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-I-1D443\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1028.8,0)\"><use data-c=\"3D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-3D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(2084.6,0)\"><use data-c=\"30\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-30\"></use></g></g></g></svg>','[]','[]','[\"dust-model-3386642e\",\"structure-seed-99af7e9e\",\"technical-relation-39ff4117\"]'),
(2009513,'dark-energy-cosmology','physical-cosmology','Dark Energy and the Accelerated Expansion','<p><strong>Dark Energy</strong> is the dominant 4D <strong>Ontological Commitment</strong> of the modern universe, accounting for approximately 68% of the total 4D <strong>Energy Density</strong>. In university-level astrophysics, dark energy is defined by its <strong>Negative Pressure</strong>, which acts as a 4D <strong>Cosmic Force</strong> that causes the 4D <strong>Expansion Rate</strong> of the  to accelerate, rather than slow down.</p>\n\n                  <h3>1. The Cosmological Constant (\\( \\Lambda \\))</h3>\n                  <p>The simplest model for dark energy is the <strong>Cosmological Constant</strong>, introduced by Einstein. It represents a 4D <strong>Energy Density</strong> inherent to the 4D <strong>Subatomic Vacuum</strong> itself. Unlike matter or radiation, vacuum energy does not dilute as space expands (\\( \\rho_\\Lambda = \\text{const} \\)). This 4D <strong>Logical Basis</strong> leads to a 4D <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/total-dynamics\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Total Dynamics</strong></a> where expansion eventually becomes exponential, pushing galaxies apart at increasing speeds.</p>\n\n                  <h3>2. Equation of State (\\( w = -1 \\))</h3>\n                  <p>Dark energy is characterized by its <strong>Equation of State</strong> parameter \\( w = P / \\rho c^2 \\). For a cosmological constant, \\( w = -1 \\). This 4D <strong>Negative Pressure</strong> is what drives the 4D <strong>Acceleration Equation</strong>. If \\( w \\) is different from -1 (a model known as <strong>Quintessence</strong>), the 4D <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/spacetime-causal-topology\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Causal Topology</strong></a> of the future universe could lead to a \"Big Rip\" or a \"Big Crunch,\" anchoring 4D <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/scientific-realism\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Scientific Realism</strong></a> in the precise value of vacuum pressure.</p>\n\n                  <h3>3. The Lambda-CDM Paradigm</h3>\n                  <p>The combination of 4D <strong>Dark Energy</strong> (Lambda) and 4D <strong>Cold Dark Matter</strong> (CDM) forms the <strong>Standard Model of Cosmology</strong>. This 4D <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/mathematical-structure\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Mathematical Structure</strong></a> provides a 4D <strong>Holistic</strong> fit for observations of 4D <strong>Type Ia Supernovae</strong>, the 4D <strong>CMB</strong>, and galaxy clusters. It proves that we live in a 4D <strong>Block Universe</strong> that is transitioning from a 4D <strong>Matter</strong> state to a 4D <strong>Vacuum-Dominated</strong> state.</p>','Dark Energy is the dominant 4D Ontological Commitment of the modern universe, accounting for approximately 68% of the total 4D Energy Density. In university-level astrophysics, dark energy is defined by its Negative Pressure, which acts as a 4D Cosmic Force that causes the 4D Expansion Rate of the to accelerate, rather than slow down. The simplest model for dark energy is the Cosmological Constant, introduced by Einstein.','Dark Energy is the dominant 4D Ontological Commitment of the modern universe, accounting for approximately 68% of the total 4D Energy Density. In university-level astrophysics, dark energy is defined by its Negative Pressure, which acts as a 4D Cosmic Force that causes the 4D Expansion Rate of the  to accelerate, rather than slow down. The simplest model for dark energy is the Cosmological Constant, introduced by Einstein.','<svg style=\"color: #FFD700; vertical-align: 0;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.57ex\" height=\"1.62ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -716 694 716\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><defs><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-N-39B\" d=\"M320 708Q326 716 340 716H348H355Q367 716 372 708Q374 706 423 547T523 226T575 62Q581 52 591 50T634 46H661V0H653Q644 3 532 3Q411 3 390 0H379V46H392Q464 46 464 65Q463 70 390 305T316 539L246 316Q177 95 177 84Q177 72 198 59T248 46H253V0H245Q230 3 130 3Q47 3 38 0H32V46H45Q112 51 127 91Q128 92 224 399T320 708Z\"></path></defs><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"39B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-39B\"></use></g></g></g></svg>','[]','[]','[\"repulsive-gravity-3202861e\",\"non-diluting-density-39e76d7d\",\"technical-relation-2d922c62\"]');
INSERT INTO `subtopics` VALUES
(2009514,'recombination-cosmic','physical-cosmology','Recombination and the Last Scattering','<p><strong>Recombination</strong> is the pivotal milestone in the 4D <strong>Block Universe</strong> history (\\( z \\approx 1100 \\)) when the 4D <strong>Subatomic Vacuum</strong> cooled enough for protons and electrons to bind into neutral hydrogen atoms. This 4D <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/ontological-emergence-physics\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Ontological Emergence</strong></a> of neutral matter allowed the universe to become transparent, releasing the <strong>Cosmic Microwave Background (CMB)</strong>.</p>\n\n                  <h3>1. Transition to Transparency</h3>\n                  <p>Before recombination, the universe was a hot, ionized 4D <strong>Plasma</strong> where photons were constantly scattered by free electrons (<strong>Thomson Scattering</strong>). This 4D <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/spacetime-causal-topology\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Causal Topology</strong></a> was an \"Opaque Fog.\" Once atoms formed, the 4D <strong>Mean Free Path</strong> of photons became effectively infinite. This \"Last Scattering\" surface is the 4D <strong>Light Cone Boundary</strong> beyond which we cannot see using electromagnetic radiation.</p>\n\n                  <h3>2. The Saha Equation</h3>\n                  <p>The timing of recombination is determined by the <strong>Saha Equation</strong>, which models the 4D <strong>Statistical Mechanics</strong> of ionization. Although the binding energy of Hydrogen is 13.6 eV, recombination occurred at a much lower temperature (\\( \\sim 3000 \\text{ K} \\) or 0.3 eV) because of the massive 4D <strong>Photon-to-Baryon Ratio</strong>. This 4D <strong>Logical Basis</strong> proves that the 4D <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/total-dynamics\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Total Dynamics</strong></a> was dominated by the radiation field even as matter was clumping.</p>\n\n                  <h3>3. Origin of the CMB</h3>\n                  <p>The photons released during recombination have been traveling through the  for 13.8 billion years, stretched by 4D <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/cosmological-redshift\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Cosmological Redshift</strong></a> into the microwave spectrum. The 4D <strong>Isotropy</strong> and 4D <strong>Homogeneity</strong> of this radiation are the strongest proofs of the 4D <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/cosmological-principle\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Cosmological Principle</strong></a>, anchoring 4D <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/scientific-realism\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Scientific Realism</strong></a> in the \"Afterglow\" of the Big Bang.</p>','Recombination is the pivotal milestone in the 4D Block Universe history when the 4D Subatomic Vacuum cooled enough for protons and electrons to bind into neutral hydrogen atoms. This 4D Ontological Emergence of neutral matter allowed the universe to become transparent, releasing the Cosmic Microwave Background (CMB). Before recombination, the universe was a hot, ionized 4D Plasma where photons were constantly scattered by free electrons (Thomson Scattering).','Recombination is the pivotal milestone in the 4D Block Universe history (<svg style=\"color: #FFD700; vertical-align: -0.05ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"8.594ex\" height=\"1.557ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -666 3798.6 688\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><defs><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-I-1D467\" d=\"M347 338Q337 338 294 349T231 360Q211 360 197 356T174 346T162 335T155 324L153 320Q150 317 138 317Q117 317 117 325Q117 330 120 339Q133 378 163 406T229 440Q241 442 246 442Q271 442 291 425T329 392T367 375Q389 375 411 408T434 441Q435 442 449 442H462Q468 436 468 434Q468 430 463 420T449 399T432 377T418 358L411 349Q368 298 275 214T160 106L148 94L163 93Q185 93 227 82T290 71Q328 71 360 90T402 140Q406 149 409 151T424 153Q443 153 443 143Q443 138 442 134Q425 72 376 31T278 -11Q252 -11 232 6T193 40T15