(1000,0)\"></use><use data-c=\"30\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-30\" transform=\"translate(1500,0)\"></use></g></g></g></svg>) when the 4D Subatomic Vacuum cooled enough for protons and electrons to bind into neutral hydrogen atoms. This 4D Ontological Emergence of neutral matter allowed the universe to become transparent, releasing the Cosmic Microwave Background (CMB). Before recombination, the universe was a hot, ionized 4D Plasma where photons were constantly scattered by free electrons (Thomson Scattering).','<svg style=\"color: #FFD700; vertical-align: -0.05ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"8.594ex\" height=\"1.557ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -666 3798.6 688\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><defs><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-I-1D467\" d=\"M347 338Q337 338 294 349T231 360Q211 360 197 356T174 346T162 335T155 324L153 320Q150 317 138 317Q117 317 117 325Q117 330 120 339Q133 378 163 406T229 440Q241 442 246 442Q271 442 291 425T329 392T367 375Q389 375 411 408T434 441Q435 442 449 442H462Q468 436 468 434Q468 430 463 420T449 399T432 377T418 358L411 349Q368 298 275 214T160 106L148 94L163 93Q185 93 227 82T290 71Q328 71 360 90T402 140Q406 149 409 151T424 153Q443 153 443 143Q443 138 442 134Q425 72 376 31T278 -11Q252 -11 232 6T193 40T155 57Q111 57 76 -3Q70 -11 59 -11H54H41Q35 -5 35 -2Q35 13 93 84Q132 129 225 214T340 322Q352 338 347 338Z\"></path><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-N-2248\" d=\"M55 319Q55 360 72 393T114 444T163 472T205 482Q207 482 213 482T223 483Q262 483 296 468T393 413L443 381Q502 346 553 346Q609 346 649 375T694 454Q694 465 698 474T708 483Q722 483 722 452Q722 386 675 338T555 289Q514 289 468 310T388 357T308 404T224 426Q164 426 125 393T83 318Q81 289 69 289Q55 289 55 319ZM55 85Q55 126 72 159T114 210T163 238T205 248Q207 248 213 248T223 249Q262 249 296 234T393 179L443 147Q502 112 553 112Q609 112 649 141T694 220Q694 249 708 249T722 217Q722 153 675 104T555 55Q514 55 468 76T388 123T308 170T224 192Q164 192 125 159T83 84Q80 55 69 55Q55 55 55 85Z\"></path><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-N-31\" d=\"M213 578L200 573Q186 568 160 563T102 556H83V602H102Q149 604 189 617T245 641T273 663Q275 666 285 666Q294 666 302 660V361L303 61Q310 54 315 52T339 48T401 46H427V0H416Q395 3 257 3Q121 3 100 0H88V46H114Q136 46 152 46T177 47T193 50T201 52T207 57T213 61V578Z\"></path><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-N-30\" d=\"M96 585Q152 666 249 666Q297 666 345 640T423 548Q460 465 460 320Q460 165 417 83Q397 41 362 16T301 -15T250 -22Q224 -22 198 -16T137 16T82 83Q39 165 39 320Q39 494 96 585ZM321 597Q291 629 250 629Q208 629 178 597Q153 571 145 525T137 333Q137 175 145 125T181 46Q209 16 250 16Q290 16 318 46Q347 76 354 130T362 333Q362 478 354 524T321 597Z\"></path></defs><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D467\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-I-1D467\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(742.8,0)\"><use data-c=\"2248\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-2248\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(1798.6,0)\"><use data-c=\"31\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-31\"></use><use data-c=\"31\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-31\" transform=\"translate(500,0)\"></use><use data-c=\"30\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-30\" transform=\"translate(1000,0)\"></use><use data-c=\"30\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-30\" transform=\"translate(1500,0)\"></use></g></g></g></svg>','[]','[]','[\"phase-transition-4426efdd\",\"visual-horizon-5bc13e77\",\"technical-relation-e8ff9b0e\"]'),
(2009515,'equality-epoch','physical-cosmology','The Radiation-Matter Equality Epoch','<p><strong>Radiation-Matter Equality</strong> (\\( z \\approx 3400 \\)) is the 4D <strong>Logical</strong> boundary between the early, radiation-driven universe and the subsequent structure-forming matter era. In university-level 4D <strong>Physical Cosmology</strong>, this epoch marks the point where the 4D <strong>Energy Density</strong> of relativistic particles and non-relativistic matter were exactly equal.</p>\n\n                  <h3>1. Crossing the Density Threshold</h3>\n                  <p>Because 4D <strong>Radiation</strong> density (\\( a^{-4} \\)) falls faster than 4D <strong>Matter</strong> density (\\( a^{-3} \\)), their dominance must eventually swap. The redshift of equality (\\( z_{eq} \\)) depends solely on the ratio of 4D <strong>Density Parameters</strong> (\\( \\Omega_m / \\Omega_r \\)). This 4D <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/total-dynamics\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Total Dynamics</strong></a> event determined the \"Horizon Scale\" at which galaxy formation could begin, anchoring 4D <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/scientific-realism\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Scientific Realism</strong></a> in the competitive scaling of cosmic fluids.</p>\n\n                  <h3>2. <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/jeans-instability\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Jeans Instability</strong></a> and Growth</h3>\n                  <p>During the radiation era, the high 4D <strong>Photon Pressure</strong> prevented matter from collapsing (the <strong>Jeans Length</strong> was huge). At equality, the 4D <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/spacetime-causal-topology\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Causal Topology</strong></a> changed; the expansion rate slowed (\\( a \\propto t^{1/2} \\to t^{2/3} \\)) and gravity began to win. This allowed 4D <strong>Dark Matter</strong> to start clumping into halos, providing the 4D <strong>Logical Basis</strong> for the \"Bottom-Up\" assembly of the 4D <strong>Cosmic Web</strong>.</p>\n\n                  <h3>3. The Horizon at Equality</h3>\n                  <p>The 4D <strong>Cosmological Horizons</strong> at the moment of equality leave a permanent \"Scale\" in the distribution of galaxies, known as the <strong>Peak of the Power Spectrum</strong>. By measuring this scale in modern 4D <strong>Galaxy Surveys</strong>, astronomers can \"Look Back\" to the equality epoch and verify the 4D <strong>Initial Conditions</strong> of the Big Bang, anchoring 4D <strong>Epistemology</strong> in the fossilized remnants of 4D <strong>Subatomic Vacuum</strong> dynamics.</p>','Radiation-Matter Equality is the 4D Logical boundary between the early, radiation-driven universe and the subsequent structure-forming matter era. In university-level 4D Physical Cosmology, this epoch marks the point where the 4D Energy Density of relativistic particles and non-relativistic matter were exactly equal. Because 4D Radiation density falls faster than 4D Matter density, their dominance must eventually swap.','Radiation-Matter Equality (<svg style=\"color: #FFD700; vertical-align: -0.05ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"8.594ex\" height=\"1.581ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -677 3798.6 699\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><defs><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-I-1D467\" d=\"M347 338Q337 338 294 349T231 360Q211 360 197 356T174 346T162 335T155 324L153 320Q150 317 138 317Q117 317 117 325Q117 330 120 339Q133 378 163 406T229 440Q241 442 246 442Q271 442 291 425T329 392T367 375Q389 375 411 408T434 441Q435 442 449 442H462Q468 436 468 434Q468 430 463 420T449 399T432 377T418 358L411 349Q368 298 275 214T160 106L148 94L163 93Q185 93 227 82T290 71Q328 71 360 90T402 140Q406 149 409 151T424 153Q443 153 443 143Q443 138 442 134Q425 72 376 31T278 -11Q252 -11 232 6T193 40T155 57Q111 57 76 -3Q70 -11 59 -11H54H41Q35 -5 35 -2Q35 13 93 84Q132 129 225 214T340 322Q352 338 347 338Z\"></path><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-N-2248\" d=\"M55 