e four Maxwell\'s Equations. It describes how a time-varying magnetic field acts as a \"Source\" of electric vorticity, proving that electric fields are not exclusively generated by charges, but can also be induced by dynamic magnetic environments in the .','<svg style=\"color: #FFD700; vertical-align: -0.566ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"17.498ex\" height=\"2.262ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -750 7734 1000\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><defs><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-N-2207\" d=\"M46 676Q46 679 51 683H781Q786 679 786 676Q786 674 617 326T444 -26Q439 -33 416 -33T388 -26Q385 -22 216 326T46 676ZM697 596Q697 597 445 597T193 596Q195 591 319 336T445 80L697 596Z\"></path><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-N-D7\" d=\"M630 29Q630 9 609 9Q604 9 587 25T493 118L389 222L284 117Q178 13 175 11Q171 9 168 9Q160 9 154 15T147 29Q147 36 161 51T255 146L359 250L255 354Q174 435 161 449T147 471Q147 480 153 485T168 490Q173 490 175 489Q178 487 284 383L389 278L493 382Q570 459 587 475T609 491Q630 491 630 471Q630 464 620 453T522 355L418 250L522 145Q606 61 618 48T630 29Z\"></path><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-B-1D404\" d=\"M723 286Q721 284 700 145T677 3V0H39V62H147V618H39V680H660V676Q662 670 675 552T691 428V424H629V428Q629 429 627 448T618 494T601 541Q574 593 527 605T382 618H374H304V384H336Q338 384 347 384T361 384T376 386T392 390T407 397T421 407T432 423Q442 444 443 482V501H505V205H443V224Q442 258 435 278T411 307T380 318T336 322H304V62H375H394Q429 62 449 62T497 66T541 76T577 95T609 126T632 170T651 232Q661 287 661 289H723V286Z\"></path><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-N-3D\" d=\"M56 347Q56 360 70 367H707Q722 359 722 347Q722 336 708 328L390 327H72Q56 332 56 347ZM56 153Q56 168 72 173H708Q722 163 722 153Q722 140 707 133H70Q56 140 56 153Z\"></path><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-N-2212\" d=\"M84 237T84 250T98 270H679Q694 262 694 250T679 230H98Q84 237 84 250Z\"></path><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-I-1D715\" d=\"M202 508Q179 508 169 520T158 547Q158 557 164 577T185 624T230 675T301 710L333 715H345Q378 715 384