6 679 786 676Q786 674 617 326T444 -26Q439 -33 416 -33T388 -26Q385 -22 216 326T46 676ZM697 596Q697 597 445 597T193 596Q195 591 319 336T445 80L697 596Z\"></path><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-I-1D449\" d=\"M52 648Q52 670 65 683H76Q118 680 181 680Q299 680 320 683H330Q336 677 336 674T334 656Q329 641 325 637H304Q282 635 274 635Q245 630 242 620Q242 618 271 369T301 118L374 235Q447 352 520 471T595 594Q599 601 599 609Q599 633 555 637Q537 637 537 648Q537 649 539 661Q542 675 545 679T558 683Q560 683 570 683T604 682T668 681Q737 681 755 683H762Q769 676 769 672Q769 655 760 640Q757 637 743 637Q730 636 719 635T698 630T682 623T670 615T660 608T652 599T645 592L452 282Q272 -9 266 -16Q263 -18 259 -21L241 -22H234Q216 -22 216 -15Q213 -9 177 305Q139 623 138 626Q133 637 76 637H59Q52 642 52 648Z\"></path></defs><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D404\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-B-1D404\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1033.8,0)\"><use data-c=\"3D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-3D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(2089.6,0)\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(2867.6,0)\"><use data-c=\"2207\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-2207\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(3700.6,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D449\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-I-1D449\"></use></g></g></g></svg>','[]','[]','[\"scalar-potential-identity-e04ad8af\",\"conservative-rule-cc2b22d8\",\"technical-relation-7ca8146a\"]'),
(2009895,'vector-relation-potential','potential-theory','The Vector Potential Relation','<p>The <strong>Vector Potential Relation</strong> describes how fields without sources or sinks (divergence-free fields) are generated from a 4D <strong>Vector Potential</strong> (\\( \\mathbf{A} \\)). In university-level 4D <strong>Electromagnetism</strong>, this relation (\\( \\mathbf{B} = \\nabla \\times \\mathbf{A} \\)) is necessary because magnetic monopoles do not exist, requiring a more complex 4D <strong>Logical Basis</strong> than scalar potentials.</p>\n\n                <h3>1. Solenoidal Fields</h3>\n                <p><a href=\"/physics/subtopic/gausss-law-for-magnetism\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Gauss\'s Law for Magnetism</strong></a> states that the magnetic field is <strong>Solenoidal</strong> (\\( \\nabla \\cdot \\mathbf{B} = 0 \\)). Because the divergence of a curl is mathematically always zero (\\( \\nabla \\cdot (\\nabla \\times \\mathbf{A}) = 0 \\)), any solenoidal field can be represented as the curl of some vector field \\( \\mathbf{A} \\). This anchors 4D <strong>Mathematical Realism</strong> in vector calculus identities.</p>\n\n                <h3>2. Gauge Freedom and the Coulomb Gauge</h3>\n                <p>Unlike scalar potentials, \\( \\mathbf{A} \\) is highly non-unique. We can add the gradient of any scalar function to \\( \\mathbf{A} \\) without changing the physical \\( \\mathbf{B} \\) field (since \\( \\nabla \\times \\nabla f = 0 \\)). This 4D <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/gauge-freedom\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Gauge Freedom</strong></a>. To solve problems, physicists \"Fix the Gauge,\" commonly using the <strong>Coulomb Gauge</strong> (\\( \\nabla \\cdot \\mathbf{A} = 0 \\)), which simplifies the 4D <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/total-dynamics\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Total Dynamics</strong></a> equations into a set of 4D <strong>Poisson Equations</strong> for each vector component.</p>\n\n                <h3>3. The Aharonov-Bohm Effect</h3>\n                <p>Classically, \\( \\mathbf{A} \\) was viewed as a mathematical trick with no physical reality. However, in 4D <strong>Quantum Mechanics</strong>, the <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/aharonov-bohm-effect\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Aharonov-Bohm Effect</strong></a> proves that the vector potential directly alters the phase of an electron\'s 4D <strong>Wave Function</strong>, even in regions where \\( \\mathbf{B} = 0 \\). This elevated the 4D <strong>Vector Potential</strong> to a primary 4D <strong>Ontological Commitment</strong> of modern 4D <strong>Theoretical Physics</strong>.</p>','The Vector Potential Relation describes how fields without sources or sinks (divergence-free fields) are generated from a 4D Vector Potential. In university-level 4D Electromagnetism, this relation is necessary because magnetic monopoles do not exist, requiring a more complex 4D Logical Basis than scalar potentials. Gauss\'s Law for Magnetism states that the magnetic field is Solenoidal.','The Vector Potential Relation describes how fields without sources or sinks (divergence-free fields) are generated from a 4D Vector Potential (<svg style=\"color: #FFD700; vertical-align: 0;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.966ex\" height=\"1.579ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -698 869 698\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><defs><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-B-1D400\" d=\"M296 0Q278 3 164 3Q58 3 49 0H40V62H92Q144 62 144 64Q388 682 397 689Q403 698 434 698Q463 698 471 689Q475 686 538 530T663 218L724 64Q724 62 776 62H828V0H817Q796 3 658 3Q509 3 485 0H472V62H517Q561 62 561 63L517 175H262L240 120Q218 65 217 64Q217 62 261 62H306V0H296ZM390 237L492 238L440 365Q390 491 388 491Q287 239 287 237H390Z\"></path></defs><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D400\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-B-1D400\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg>). In university-level 4D Electromagnetism, this relation (<svg style=\"color: #FFD700; vertical-align: -0.186ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"11.484ex\" height=\"1.765ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -698 5076 780\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><defs><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-B-1D401\" d=\"M720 510Q720 476 704 448T665 404T619 377T580 362L564 359L583 356Q602 353 632 342T690 312Q712 292 725 276Q752 235 752 189V183Q752 160 741 125Q698 18 547 2Q543 1 288 0H39V62H147V624H39V686H264H409Q502 686 542 681T624 655Q720 607 720 510ZM563 513Q563 553 548 578T518 611T486 622Q479 624 385 624H293V382H375Q458 383 467 385Q563 405 563 513ZM590 192Q590 307 505 329Q504 330 503 330L398 331H293V62H391H400H444Q496 62 528 75T580 131Q590 155 590 192Z\"></path><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-N-3D\" d=\"M56 347Q56 360 70 367H707Q722 359 722 347Q722 336 708 328L390 327H72Q56 332 56 347ZM56 153Q56 168 72 173H708Q722 163 722 153Q722 140 707 133H70Q56 140 56 153Z\"></path><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-N-2207\" d=\"M46 676Q46 679 51 683H781Q786 679 786 676Q786 674 617 326T444 -26Q439 -33 416 -33T388 -26Q385 -22 216 326T46 676ZM697 596Q697 597 445 597T193 596Q195 591 319 336T445 80L697 596Z\"></path><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-N-D7\" d=\"M630 29Q630 9 609 9Q604 9 587 25T493 118L389 222L284 117Q178 13 175 11Q171 9 168 9Q160 9 154 15T147 29Q147 36 161 51T255 146L359 250L255 354Q174 435 161 449T147 471Q147 480 153 485T168 490Q173 490 175 489Q178 487 284 383L389 278L493 382Q570 459 587 475T609 491Q630 491 630 471Q630 464 620 453T522 355L418 250L522 145Q606 61 618 48T630 29Z\"></path><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-B-1D400\" d=\"M296 0Q278 3 164 3Q58 3 49 0H40V62H92Q144 62 144 64Q388 682 397 689Q403 698 434 698Q463 698 471 689Q475 686 538 530T663 218L724 64Q724 62 776 62H828V0H817Q796 3 658 3Q509 3 485 0H472V62H517Q561 62 561 63L517 175H262L240 120Q218 65 217 64Q217 62 261 62H306V0H296ZM390 237L492 238L440 365Q390 491 388 491Q287 239 287 237H390Z\"></path></defs><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D401\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-B-1D401\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1095.8,0)\"><use data-c=\"3D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-3D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(2151.6,0)\"><use data-c=\"2207\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-2207\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(3206.8,0)\"><use data-c=\"D7\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-D7\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\" transform=\"translate(4207,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D400\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-B-1D400\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg>) is necessary because magnetic monopoles do not exist, requiring a more complex 4D Logical Basis than scalar potentials. Gauss\'s Law for Magnetism states that the magnetic field is Solenoidal (<svg style=\"color: #FFD700; vertical-align: -0.186ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"9.518ex\" height=\"1.738ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -686 4207 768\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><defs><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-N-2207\" d=\"M46 676Q46 679 51 683H781Q786 679 786 676Q786 674 617 326T444 -26Q439 -33 416 -33T388 -26Q385 -22 216 326T46 676ZM697 596Q697 597 445 597T193 596Q195 591 319 336T445 80L697 596Z\"></path><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-N-22C5\" d=\"M78 250Q78 274 95 292T138 310Q162 310 180 294T199 251Q199 226 182 208T139 190T96 207T78 250Z\"></path><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-B-1D401\" d=\"M720 510Q720 476 704 448T665 404T619 377T580 362L564 359L583 356Q602 353 632 342T690 312Q712 292 725 276Q752 235 752 189V183Q752 160 741 125Q698 18 547 2Q543 1 288 0H39V62H147V624H39V686H264H409Q502 686 542 681T624 655Q720 607 720 510ZM563 513Q563 553 548 578T518 611T486 622Q479 624 385 624H293V382H375Q458 383 467 385Q563 405 563 513ZM590 192Q590 307 505 329Q504 330 503 330L398 331H293V62H391H400H444Q496 62 528 75T580 131Q590 155 590 192Z\"></path><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-N-3D\" d=\"M56 347Q56 360 70 367H707Q722 359 722 347Q722 336 708 328L390 327H72Q56 332 56 347ZM56 153Q56 168 72 173H708Q722 163 722 153Q722 140 707 133H70Q56 140 56 153Z\"></path><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-N-30\" d=\"M96 585Q152 666 249 666Q297 666 345 640T423 548Q460 465 460 320Q460 165 417 83Q397 41 362 16T301 -15T250 -22Q224 -22 198 -16T137 16T82 83Q39 165 39 320Q39 494 96 585ZM321 597Q291 629 250 629Q208 629 178 597Q153 571 145 525T137 333Q137 175 145 125T181 46Q209 16 250 16Q290 16 318 46Q347 76 354 130T362 333Q362 478 354 524T321 597Z\"></path></defs><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"2207\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-2207\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1055.2,0)\"><use data-c=\"22C5\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-22C5\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\" transform=\"translate(1555.4,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D401\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-B-1D401\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(2651.2,0)\"><use data-c=\"3D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-3D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(3707,0)\"><use data-c=\"30\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-30\"></use></g></g></g></svg>).','<svg style=\"color: #FFD700; vertical-align: 0;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.966ex\" height=\"1.579ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -698 869 698\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><defs><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-B-1D400\" d=\"M296 0Q278 3 164 3Q58 3 49 0H40V62H92Q144 62 144 64Q388 682 397 689Q403 698 434 698Q463 698 471 689Q475 686 538 530T663 218L724 64Q724 62 776 62H828V0H817Q796 3 658 3Q509 3 485 0H472V62H517Q561 62 561 63L517 175H262L240 120Q218 65 217 64Q217 62 261 62H306V0H296ZM390 237L492 238L440 365Q390 491 388 491Q287 239 287 237H390Z\"></path></defs><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D400\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-B-1D400\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg>','[]','[]','[\"magnetic-field-definition-22e80712\",\"a-href-physics-subtopic-differential-form-magnetism-class-subtopic-link-differential-form-a-f092566f\",\"technical-relation-91e1e316\"]'),
(2009896,'retardation-physics','potential-theory','Retardation and Finite Light Speed','<p><strong>Retardation</strong> is the 4D <strong>Logical Basis</strong> for the fact that changes in 4D <strong>Electromagnetic Fields</strong> do not propagate instantaneously. Because the speed of light (\\( c \\)) is finite, the 4D <strong>Potential</strong> at any point in space depends on the state of the source at an earlier <strong>Retarded Time</strong>. In university-level electrodynamics, this is origin of 4D <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/electromagnetic-radiation\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Electromagnetic Radiation</strong></a>.</p>\n\n                <h3>1. The Retarded Time (\\( t_r \\))</h3>\n                <p>If an observer at position \\( \\mathbf{r} \\) measures the potential at time \\( t \\), they are \"Seeing\" the source at position \\( \\mathbf{r}\' \\) as it was at time \\( t_r = t - |\\mathbf{r} - \\mathbf{r}\'|/c \\). This imposes strict 4D <strong>Einstein Locality</strong> on the 4D <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/total-dynamics\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Total Dynamics</strong></a> of the system, anchoring 4D <strong>Physical Causality</strong> in the 4D <strong>Light Cone Boundary</strong> of the .</p>\n\n                <h3>2. Retarded Potentials</h3>\n                <p>When solving the inhomogeneous 4D <strong>Wave Equations</strong> for \\( V \\) and \\( \\mathbf{A} \\), the solutions are the <strong>Retarded Potentials</strong> (the Liénard-Wiechert potentials for moving point charges). These equations sum the contributions of the 4D <strong>Charge Density</strong> \\( \\rho \\) and 4D <strong>Current Density</strong> \\( \\mathbf{J} \\) evaluated entirely at the retarded time \\( t_r \\). This breaks the instant \"Action at a Distance\" of classical 4D <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/coulombs-law\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Coulomb\'s Law</strong></a>.</p>\n\n                <h3>3. The Birth of Radiation</h3>\n                <p>Retardation is the reason antennas work. When a charge accelerates, the \"News\" of its changing velocity ripples outward at speed \\( c \\). This creates \"Kinks\" in the 4D <strong>Electric Field</strong> lines that detach and self-propagate as 4D <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/electromagnetic-radiation\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Electromagnetic Radiation</strong></a>. Without retardation, the 4D <strong>Vector Potential Relation</strong> would instantly adjust, and energy could never leave the source to travel across the 4D <strong>Block Universe</strong>.</p>','Retardation is the 4D Logical Basis for the fact that changes in 4D Electromagnetic Fields do not propagate instantaneously. Because the speed of light is finite, the 4D Potential at any point in space depends on the state of the source at an earlier Retarded Time. In university-level electrodynamics, this is origin of 4D Electromagnetic Radiation.','Retardation is the 4D Logical Basis for the fact that changes in 4D Electromagnetic Fields do not propagate instantaneously. Because the speed of light (<svg style=\"color: #FFD700; vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"0.98ex\" height=\"1.025ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -442 433 453\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><defs><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-I-1D450\" d=\"M34 159Q34 268 120 355T306 442Q362 442 394 418T427 355Q427 326 408 306T360 285Q341 285 330 295T319 325T330 359T352 380T366 386H367Q367 388 361 392T340 400T306 404Q276 404 249 390Q228 381 206 359Q162 315 142 235T121 119Q121 73 147 50Q169 26 205 26H209Q321 26 394 111Q403 121 406 121Q410 121 419 112T429 98T420 83T391 55T346 25T282 0T202 -11Q127 -11 81 37T34 159Z\"></path></defs><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D450\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-I-1D450\"></use></g></g></g></svg>) is finite, the 4D Potential at any point in space depends on the state of the source at an earlier Retarded Time. In university-level electrodynamics, this is origin of 4D Electromagnetic Radiation.','<svg style=\"color: #FFD700; vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"0.98ex\" height=\"1.025ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -442 433 453\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><defs><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-I-1D450\" d=\"M34 159Q34 268 120 355T306 442Q362 442 394 418T427 355Q427 326 408 306T360 285Q341 285 330 295T319 325T330 359T352 380T366 386H367Q367 388 361 392T340 400T306 404Q276 404 249 390Q228 381 206 359Q162 315 142 235T121 119Q121 73 147 50Q169 26 205 26H209Q321 26 394 111Q403 121 406 121Q410 121 419 112T429 98T420 83T391 55T346 25T282 0T202 -11Q127 -11 81 37T34 159Z\"></path></defs><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D450\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-I-1D450\"></use></g></g></g></svg>','[]','[]','[\"radiation-condition-d75fbaa1\",\"information-ripple-4858e072\",\"technical-relation-d378e4b1\"]'),
(2009897,'electromagnetic-energy-density','poynting-vector','Electromagnetic Energy Density','<p>The Electromagnetic Energy Density (\\( u \\)) is the total energy per unit volume stored in the configuration of electric and magnetic fields. In university-level electrodynamics, this quantity is fundamental to <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/poynting-theorem-physics\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Poynting\'s Theorem</strong></a> and represents the capacity of the 4D <strong>Subatomic Vacuum</strong> to hold work-equivalent energy in its structural fields.</p>\n\n                  <h3>1. Field Energy Components</h3>\n                  <p>The total density is composed of two quadratic terms:\n                  \\[ u = u_E + u_B = \\frac{1}{2}\\varepsilon_0 E^2 + \\frac{1}{2\\mu_0} B^2 \\]\n                  This shows that energy is distributed throughout the manifold wherever fields exist. For an electromagnetic wave in a vacuum, these two components are exactly equal (\\( u_E = u_B \\)), meaning the energy is shared perfectly between the 4D <strong>Electric Potential</strong> and the 4D <strong>Magnetic Induction</strong>.</p>\n\n                  <h3>2. Work and Assembly</h3>\n                  <p>The energy density represents the total 4D <strong>Work Done</strong> required to bring charges and currents from infinity to their current configuration. This 4D <strong>Logical Basis</strong> shifts the 4D <strong>Ontology</strong> of energy from the particles themselves to the surrounding space, anchoring <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/scientific-realism\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Scientific Realism</strong></a> in the physical reality of the  tensor.</p>\n\n                  <h3>3. Energy Density and Spacetime Curvature</h3>\n                  <p>According to <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/general-relativity\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>General Relativity</strong></a>, energy density is the primary source of the 4D <strong>Metric Tensor</strong> curvature. The field energy density \\( u \\) acts as the \\( T^{00} \\) component of the <strong>Stress-Energy Tensor</strong>. This proves that even in a vacuum without matter, the presence of electromagnetic fields creates a 4D <strong>Gravitational Field</strong>, linking 4D <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/total-dynamics\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Total Dynamics</strong></a> to the global geometry of the universe.</p>','The Electromagnetic Energy Density is the total energy per unit volume stored in the configuration of electric and magnetic fields. In university-level electrodynamics, this quantity is fundamental to Poynting\'s Theorem and represents the capacity of the 4D Subatomic Vacuum to hold work-equivalent energy in its structural fields. The total density is composed of two quadratic terms: This shows that energy is distributed throughout the manifold wherever fields exist.','The Electromagnetic Energy Density (<svg style=\"color: #FFD700; vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.294ex\" height=\"1.025ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -442 572 453\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><defs><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-I-1D462\" d=\"M21 287Q21 295 30 318T55 370T99 420T158 442Q204 442 227 417T250 358Q250 340 216 246T182 105Q182 62 196 45T238 27T291 44T328 78L339 95Q341 99 377 247Q407 367 413 387T427 416Q444 431 463 431Q480 431 488 421T496 402L420 84Q419 79 419 68Q419 43 426 35T447 26Q469 29 482 57T512 145Q514 153 532 153Q551 153 551 144Q550 139 549 130T540 98T523 55T498 17T462 -8Q454 -10 438 -10Q372 -10 347 46Q345 45 336 36T318 21T296 6T267 -6T233 -11Q189 -11 155 7Q103 38 103 113Q103 170 138 262T173 379Q173 380 173 381Q173 390 173 393T169 400T158 404H154Q131 404 112 385T82 344T65 302T57 280Q55 278 41 278H27Q21 284 21 287Z\"></path></defs><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D462\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1