anslate(848.3,413) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(10165.1,0)\"><use data-c=\"2B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-2B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mfrac\" transform=\"translate(11165.3,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(739.8,676)\"><use data-c=\"31\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-31\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mrow\" transform=\"translate(220,-686)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-32\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"msub\" transform=\"translate(500,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D707\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-I-1D707\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(636,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"30\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-30\"></use></g></g></g><rect width=\"1739.6\" height=\"60\" x=\"120\" y=\"220\"></rect></g><g data-mml-node=\"msup\" transform=\"translate(13144.9,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D435\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-I-1D435\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(792,413) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg>','[]','[]','[\"energy-distribution-57df8fad\",\"wave-symmetry-dcb0857e\",\"technical-relation-3740ce7e\"]'),
(2009898,'poynting-theorem-physics','poynting-vector','Poynting\'s Theorem','<p>Poynting\'s Theorem is the work-energy theorem of classical electrodynamics. It expresses the 4D <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/total-mechanical-energy\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Conservation of Energy</strong></a> for a system of fields and charges in a local, differential form. In university-level physics, it provides the rigorous mathematical link between 4D <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/total-dynamics\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Total Dynamics</strong></a>, energy flux, and the mechanical work performed on matter.</p>\n\n                  <h3>1. The Continuity of Energy</h3>\n                  <p>Theorem states that the rate of decrease of energy in a volume, minus the energy flowing out through the surface, equals the work done by the field on the charges:\n                  \\[ \\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial t} + \\nabla \\cdot \\mathbf{S} = -\\mathbf{J} \\cdot \\mathbf{E} \\]\n                  This a 4D <strong>Continuity Equation</strong> for energy. It ensures that energy cannot simply vanish; it must either move through the  (via the <strong>Poynting Vector</strong>) or be converted into 4D <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/kinetic-energy\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Kinetic Energy</strong></a> of the charges.</p>\n\n                  <h3>2. Ohmic Heating and Work</h3>\n                  <p>The term \\( \\mathbf{J} \\cdot \\mathbf{E} \\) represents the power density transferred to the matter. Since magnetic fields do no work (\\( \\mathbf{v} \\cdot (\\mathbf{v} \\times \\mathbf{B}) = 0 \\)), only the electric field can change the mechanical energy of the system. This provides the 4D <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/spacetime-causal-topology\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Causal Topology</strong></a> for 4D <strong>Resistive Heating</strong> and particle acceleration, anchoring 4D <strong>Epistemology</strong> in the observable transfer of power.</p>\n\n                  <h3>3. Radiative Loss</h3>\n                  <p>Poynting\'s theorem explains how energy \"Leaves\" a source. For an accelerating charge, the divergence of the Poynting vector is non-zero, indicating that 4D <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/electromagnetic-radiation\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Electromagnetic Radiation</strong></a> is carrying energy away to the 4D <strong>Block Universe</strong>. This framework is essential for the 4D <strong>Logical Basis</strong> of antennas and thermal cooling of 4D <strong>White Dwarfs</strong> via photon emission.</p>','Poynting\'s Theorem is the work-energy theorem of classical electrodynamics. It expresses the 4D Conservation of Energy for a system of fields and charges in a local, differential form. In university-level physics, it provides the rigorous mathematical link between 4D Total Dynamics, energy flux, and the mechanical work performed on matter.','Poynting\'s Theorem is the work-energy theorem of classical electrodynamics. It expresses the 4D Conservation of Energy for a system of fields and charges in a local, differential form. In university-level physics, it provides the rigorous mathematical link between 4D Total Dynamics, energy flux, and the mechanical work performed on matter.','<svg style=\"color: #FFD700; vertical-align: -1.602ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20.767ex\" height=\"4.749ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -1391 9178.9 2099\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><defs><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-I-1D715\" d=\"M202 508Q179 508 169 520T158 547Q158 557 164 577T185 624T230 675T301 710L333 715H345Q378 715 384 714Q447 703 489 661T549 568T566 457Q566 362 519 240T402 53Q321 -22 223 -22Q123 -22 73 56Q42 102 42 148V159Q42 276 129 370T322 465Q383 465 414 434T455 367L458 378Q478 461 478 515Q478 603 437 639T344 676Q266 676 223 612Q264 606 264 572Q264 547 246 528T202 508ZM430 306Q430 372 401 400T333 428Q270 428 222 382Q197 354 183 323T150 221Q132 149 132 116Q132 21 232 21Q244 