-I-1D715\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(566,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D462\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-I-1D462\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mrow\" transform=\"translate(325.5,-686)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D715\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-I-1D715\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(566,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D461\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-I-1D461\"></use></g></g><rect width=\"1338\" height=\"60\" x=\"120\" y=\"220\"></rect></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1800.2,0)\"><use data-c=\"2B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-2B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(2800.4,0)\"><use data-c=\"2207\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-2207\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(3855.7,0)\"><use data-c=\"22C5\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-22C5\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\" transform=\"translate(4355.9,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D412\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-B-1D412\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(5272.7,0)\"><use data-c=\"3D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-3D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(6328.4,0)\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\" transform=\"translate(7106.4,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D409\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-B-1D409\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(7922.7,0)\"><use data-c=\"22C5\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-22C5\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\" transform=\"translate(8422.9,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D404\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-B-1D404\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg>','[]','[]','[\"poynting-s-theorem-42e9b75f\",\"ohmic-work-761d6448\",\"technical-relation-692fe81d\"]'),
(2009899,'electromagnetic-stress-energy-tensor','poynting-vector','The Electromagnetic Stress-Energy Tensor','<p>The <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/electromagnetic-stress-energy\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Electromagnetic Stress-Energy Tensor</strong></a> (\\( T^{\\mu\\nu} \\)) is a symmetric second-rank tensor that unifies energy density, momentum density, and mechanical stress within the framework of <strong>Special Relativity</strong>. In university-level 4D <strong>Theoretical Physics</strong>, this tensor provides the 4D <strong>Holistic</strong> description of how electromagnetic fields interact with the .</p>\n\n                  <h3>1. Geometric Structure</h3>\n                  <p>The tensor is organized into 16 components:\n                  <ul>\n                    <li>\\( T^{00} \\): The <strong>Energy Density</strong> (\\( u \\)).</li>\n                    <li>\\( T^{0i} \\): The <strong>Poynting Vector</strong> components (\\( S_i/c \\)), representing energy flux.</li>\n                    <li>\\( T^{i0} \\): The <strong>Field Momentum</strong> density (\\( c g_i \\)).</li>\n                    <li>\\( T^{ij} \\): The 3D <strong>Maxwell Stress Tensor</strong>, representing pressure and shear.</li>\n                  </ul>\n                  This unification ensures that energy and momentum are conserved together in all 4D <strong>Inertial Frames</strong>.</p>\n\n                  <h3>2. The Maxwell Stress Tensor (\\( \\sigma_{ij} \\))</h3>\n                  <p>The spatial components describe the \"Tug\" and \"Push\" of field lines. Magnetic field lines act like stretched rubber bands (tension along the field) that also repel each other sideways (pressure perpendicular to the field). This 4D <strong>Structural</strong> view is critical for 4D <strong>Astrophysical Fluid Dynamics</strong> and the stability of 4D <strong>Tokamak</strong> fusion reactors.</p>\n\n                  <h3>3. Covariant Conservation</h3>\n                  <p>The 4D <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/total-dynamics\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Total Dynamics</strong></a> of the field is captured by the divergence of the tensor: \\( \\partial_mu T^{\\mu\\nu} = -f^\\nu \\), where \\( f^\\nu \\) is the 4D <strong>Lorentz Force Density</strong>. In a vacuum with no charges, the tensor is <strong>Divergence-Free</strong>, meaning energy and momentum are locally conserved. this is 4D <strong>Logical Basis</strong> for the propagation of 4D <strong>Light</strong> across the 4D <strong>Block Universe</strong>.</p>','The Electromagnetic Stress-Energy Tensor is a symmetric second-rank tensor that unifies energy density, momentum density, and mechanical stress within the framework of Special Relativity. In university-level 4D Theoretical Physics, this tensor provides the 4D Holistic description of how electromagnetic fields interact with the. The tensor is organized into 16 components: : The Energy Density.','The Electromagnetic Stress-Energy Tensor (<svg style=\"color: #FFD700; vertical-align: 0;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"3.72ex\" height=\"1.532ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -677 1644.2 677\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><defs><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-I-1D447\" d=\"M40 437Q21 437 21 445Q21 450 37 501T71 602L88 651Q93 669 101 677H569H659Q691 677 697 676T704 667Q704 661 687 553T668 444Q668 437 649 437Q640 437 637 437T631 442L629 445Q629 451 635 490T641 551Q641 586 628 604T573 629Q568 630 515 631Q469 631 457 630T439 622Q438 621 368 343T298 60Q298 48 386 46Q418 46 427 45T436 36Q436 31 433 22Q429 4 424 1L422 0Q419 0 415 0Q410 0 363 1T228 2Q99 2 64 0H49Q43 6 43 9T45 27Q49 40 55 46H83H94Q174 46 189 55Q190 56 191 56Q196 59 201 76T241 233Q258 301 269 344Q339 619 339 625Q339 630 310 630H279Q212 630 191 624Q146 614 121 583T67 467Q60 445 57 441T43 437H40Z\"></path><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-I-1D707\" d=\"M58 -216Q44 -216 34 -208T23 -186Q23 -176 96 116T173 414Q186 442 219 442Q231 441 239 435T249 423T251 413Q251 401