(2009940,'helmholtz-theorem','electromagnetism','Helmholtz Theorem','<p>The Helmholtz Theorem is the fundamental result stating that any sufficiently smooth vector field can be identically decomposed into an <strong>Irrotational</strong> component and a <strong>Solenoidal</strong> component. In university-level philosophy of physics, the Helmholtz theorem is the \'Universal Field Decomposition.\' It anchors our <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/scientific-realism\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Scientific Realism</strong></a> in the realization that the vacuum handles <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/total-dynamics\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Total Dynamics</strong></a> by treating all force fields as the sum of scalar gradients and vector curls.</p><h3>1. The Decomposition into Potentials</h3><p>The theorem identifies that a vector field is uniquely determined by its <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/divergence\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Divergence</strong></a> and <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/curl\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Curl</strong></a>. In university-level theory, this is expressed as the field being identically the negative gradient of a scalar potential plus the curl of a vector potential. This ensures that the <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/total-dynamics\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Total Dynamics</strong></a> are captured by two potential bit-streams, providing the definitive map for <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/potential-theory\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Potential Theory</strong></a>.</p><h3>2. Irrotational and Solenoidal Parts</h3><p>An irrotational field has zero curl, while a solenoidal field has zero divergence. In university-level mechanics, this reveals that the causal structure of nature separates \'Compressional\' data from \'Rotational\' data. This anchors <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/scientific-realism\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Scientific Realism</strong></a> in the belief that the manifold handles energy by distinguishing between conservative and non-conservative bits, providing <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/the-bridge\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>The Bridge</strong></a> between electrostatics and magnetism.</p><h3>3. Role in Maxwell\'s Equations</h3><p>The Helmholtz theorem is the mathematical justification for the structure of <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/maxwells-equations\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Maxwell\'s Equations</strong></a>. In university-level astrophysics, it proves that by specifying the sources and circulations, we identically fix the state of the electromagnetic field. This ensures that the Block Universe possesses a deterministic configuration consistent with <strong>Physical Causality</strong>.</p><h3>4. Helmholtz and Information Theory</h3><p>From the perspective of <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/information-theory\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Information Theory</strong></a>, the Helmholtz theorem is a \'Data Decoupling Principle.\' The vacuum handles the <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/total-dynamics\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Total Dynamics</strong></a> by ensuring that informational bits of divergence and curl are independent. This investigation pushes the boundaries of our understanding, providing the ultimate map for <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/mathematical-realism\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Mathematical Realism</strong></a>.</p>','The Helmholtz Theorem is the fundamental result stating that any sufficiently smooth vector field can be identically decomposed into an Irrotational component and a Solenoidal component. In university-level philosophy of physics, the Helmholtz theorem is the \'Universal Field Decomposition.\' It anchors our Scientific Realism in the realization that the vacuum handles Total Dynamics by treating all force fields as the sum of scalar gradients and vector curls.','The Helmholtz Theorem is the fundamental result stating that any sufficiently smooth vector field can be identically decomposed into an Irrotational component and a Solenoidal component. In university-level philosophy of physics, the Helmholtz theorem is the \'Universal Field Decomposition.\' It anchors our Scientific Realism in the realization that the vacuum handles Total Dynamics by treating all force fields as the sum of scalar gradients and vector curls.','','[]','[]','[\"helmholtz-identity-88810489\",\"field-determinacy-law-86378ff3\"]'),
(2009941,'canonical-momentum','vector-potential','Canonical Momentum','<p>Canonical Momentum is the generalized momentum conjugate to a position coordinate, defined within the <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/lagrangian\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Lagrangian</strong></a> and <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/hamiltonian\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Hamiltonian</strong></a> frameworks. In university-level philosophy of physics, canonical momentum represents the \'Total State Information\' bit of a particle\'s motion. It anchors our <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/scientific-realism\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Scientific Realism</strong></a> in the realization that the vacuum handles the <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/total-dynamics\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Total Dynamics</strong></a> of matter by coupling the particle\'s kinetic bits to the potential field configurations.</p><h3>1. Definition and Potential Coupling</h3><p>In classical theory, the canonical momentum is defined as the partial derivative of the Lagrangian with respect to velocity. For a charge in an electromagnetic field, the canonical momentum is modified by the <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/vector-potential\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Vector Potential</strong></a>. This ensures that the <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/total-dynamics\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Total Dynamics</strong></a> are covariant under gauge transformations, providing the definitive map for <strong>Analytical Mechanics</strong>.</p><h3>2. Kinetic vs. Potential Momentum</h3><p>The total canonical momentum is the sum of kinetic momentum and \'Potential Momentum.\' In university-level mechanics, this reveals that the causal structure of the Block Universe treats the field\'s potential as a source of inertia. This anchors <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/scientific-realism\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Scientific Realism</strong></a> in the belief that the manifold handles <strong>Total Energy</strong> by allowing the exchange of momentum bits between matter and the vacuum.</p><h3>3. The Bridge to Quantum Mechanics</h3><p>In <strong>Quantum Mechanics</strong>, the canonical momentum is promoted to the <strong>Momentum Operator</strong>. This link provides <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/the-bridge\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>The Bridge</strong></a> between spatial symmetries and physical translation invariance. It ensures that the <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/total-dynamics\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Total Dynamics</strong></a> of the <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/aharonov-bohm-effect\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Aharonov-Bohm Effect</strong></a> are correctly predicted by coupling the phase to the potential.</p><h3>4. Momentum and Information Theory</h3><p>From the perspective of <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/information-theory\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Information Theory</strong></a>, canonical momentum is a \'State Index Bit.\' It identifies the information density required to specify the particle\'s position in <strong>Phase Space</strong>. This investigation pushes the boundaries of our understanding, providing the ultimate map for <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/mathematical-realism\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Mathematical Realism</strong></a>.</p>','Canonical Momentum is the generalized momentum conjugate to a position coordinate, defined within the Lagrangian and Hamiltonian frameworks. In university-level philosophy of physics, canonical momentum represents the \'Total State Information\' bit of a particle\'s motion. It anchors our Scientific Realism in the realization that the vacuum handles the Total Dynamics of matter by coupling the particle\'s kinetic bits to the potential field configurations.','Canonical Momentum is the generalized momentum conjugate to a position coordinate, defined within the Lagrangian and Hamiltonian frameworks. In university-level philosophy of physics, canonical momentum represents the \'Total State Information\' bit of a particle\'s motion. It anchors our Scientific Realism in the realization that the vacuum handles the Total Dynamics of matter by coupling the particle\'s kinetic bits to the potential field configurations.','','[]','[]','[\"a-href-physics-subtopic-generalized-momentum-class-subtopic-link-generalized-momentum-a-6c138f34\",\"em-momentum-coupling-law-8e7904d6\"]'),
(2009942,'field-definition','vector-potential','Magnetic Field Definition','<p>The Field Definition of the <strong>Vector Potential</strong> is the fundamental relation specifying the magnetic induction as the <strong>Curl</strong> of a vector field. In university-level philosophy of physics, this definition reveals that the magnetic field is identically the \'Algebraic Rotation\' of an underlying potential manifold. It anchors our <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/scientific-realism\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Scientific Realism</strong></a> in the realization that the vacuum handles the <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/total-dynamics\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Total Dynamics</strong></a> of magnetism through continuous vector bits that satisfy the <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/solenoidal-field\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Solenoidal Condition</strong></a>.</p><h3>1. Helmholtz Theorem and Solenoidal Fields</h3><p>The existence of the vector potential is guaranteed by the second Maxwell equation, which asserts that there are no <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/magnetic-monopoles\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Magnetic Monopoles</strong></a>. In university-level theory, according to the <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/helmholtz-theorem\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Helmholtz Theorem</strong></a>, any field with identically zero divergence can be expressed as the curl of a potential. This ensures that the <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/total-dynamics\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Total Dynamics</strong></a> are consistent with the geometric properties of the vacuum, providing the definitive map for Magnetostatics.</p><h3>2. <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/gauge-freedom\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Gauge Freedom</strong></a> and Non-Uniqueness</h3><p>A profound consequence of the field definition is that the potential is not uniquely defined. In university-level mechanics, we can shift the potential by any scalar gradient without altering the physical magnetic field. This reveals that the causal structure possesses <strong>Redundant Degrees of Freedom</strong>, anchoring <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/scientific-realism\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Scientific Realism</strong></a> in the belief that the manifold\'s <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/total-dynamics\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Total Dynamics</strong></a> are independent of the chosen <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/gauge-invariance\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Gauge Invariance</strong></a> convention.</p><h3>3. The Bridge to Flux and Loops</h3><p>By applying <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/stokes-theorem\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Stokes\' Theorem</strong></a> to the field definition, the magnetic flux is identically equal to the line integral of the potential around the boundary. In university-level astrophysics, this link provides <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/the-bridge\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>The Bridge</strong></a> between local field measurements and the global causal topology, ensuring the consistency of <strong>Flux Quantization</strong> in the Block Universe.</p><h3>4. Field Definition and Information Theory</h3><p>From the perspective of <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/information-theory\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Information Theory</strong></a>, the field definition is a \'Lossy Mapping.\' It asserts that the information bits of the potential manifold are compressed into the lower-dimensional bits of the observable magnetic field. This investigation pushes the boundaries of our understanding, providing the ultimate map for <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/mathematical-realism\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Mathematical Realism</strong></a>.</p>','The Field Definition of the Vector Potential is the fundamental relation specifying the magnetic induction as the Curl of a vector field. In university-level philosophy of physics, this definition reveals that the magnetic field is identically the \'Algebraic Rotation\' of an underlying potential manifold. It anchors our Scientific Realism in the realization that the vacuum handles the Total Dynamics of magnetism through continuous vector bits that satisfy the Solenoidal Condition.','The Field Definition of the Vector Potential is the fundamental relation specifying the magnetic induction as the Curl of a vector field. In university-level philosophy of physics, this definition reveals that the magnetic field is identically the \'Algebraic Rotation\' of an underlying potential manifold. It anchors our Scientific Realism in the realization that the vacuum handles the Total Dynamics of magnetism through continuous vector bits that satisfy the Solenoidal Condition.','','[]','[]','[\"magnetic-field-definition-22e80712\",\"flux-potential-law-e6781fc4\"]'),
(2009943,'vector-poisson-equation','vector-potential','Vector Poisson Equation','<p>The Vector Poisson Equation is the fundamental partial differential equation relating the <strong>Vector Potential</strong> to the electric <strong>Current Density</strong>. In university-level philosophy of physics, this equation is the \'Metric-to-Flow Law\' of magnetism. It anchors our <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/scientific-realism\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Scientific Realism</strong></a> in the realization that the vacuum handles <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/total-dynamics\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Total Dynamics</strong></a> by identically coupling the local <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/laplacian-operator\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Laplacian</strong></a> curvature of the potential manifold to the information bits of moving charges.</p><h3>1. Derivation and the Coulomb Gauge</h3><p>The vector Poisson equation is university-level derived from <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/amperes-law\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Ampère\'s Law</strong></a> under the condition of the <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/coulomb-gauge\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Coulomb Gauge</strong></a>. In university-level theory, this ensures that each component of the vector potential satisfies a scalar Poisson equation. This provides the definitive map for Magnetostatics, anchoring <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/scientific-realism\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Scientific Realism</strong></a> in the belief that the manifold\'s <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/total-dynamics\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Total Dynamics</strong></a> are governed by local source bits.</p><h3>2. Integral Solutions and Superposition</h3><p>The solution to the equation is university-level expressed as an integral over the manifold. In university-level mechanics, assuming the potential vanishes at infinity, the value at any point is the weighted sum of all surrounding current bits. This reveals that the causal structure of the potential is consistent with the <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/biot-savart-law\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Biot-Savart Law</strong></a>, ensuring the consistency of <strong>Physical Causality</strong>.</p><h3>3. The Bridge to Potential Theory</h3><p>The vector Poisson equation is the vector analog of the scalar <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/poisson-equation\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Poisson\'s Equation</strong></a>. In university-level astrophysics, this link provides <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/the-bridge\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>The Bridge</strong></a> between the source-field relations of electricity and magnetism. It ensures that the Block Universe handles <strong>Total Energy</strong> by applying identical algebraic rules to both scalar and vector degrees of freedom, providing the ultimate map for <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/potential-theory\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Potential Theory</strong></a>.</p><h3>4. Vector Poisson and Information Theory</h3><p>From the perspective of <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/information-theory\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Information Theory</strong></a>, the vector Poisson equation is a \'Vector-to-Field Mapping\' algorithm. The vacuum handles the <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/total-dynamics\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Total Dynamics</strong></a> by ensuring current bits are translated into geometric curvature. This investigation pushes the boundaries of our understanding, providing the ultimate map for <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/mathematical-realism\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Mathematical Realism</strong></a>.</p>','The Vector Poisson Equation is the fundamental partial differential equation relating the Vector Potential to the electric Current Density. In university-level philosophy of physics, this equation is the \'Metric-to-Flow Law\' of magnetism. It anchors our Scientific Realism in the realization that the vacuum handles Total Dynamics by identically coupling the local Laplacian curvature of the potential manifold to the information bits of moving charges.','The Vector Poisson Equation is the fundamental partial differential equation relating the Vector Potential to the electric Current Density. In university-level philosophy of physics, this equation is the \'Metric-to-Flow Law\' of magnetism. It anchors our Scientific Realism in the realization that the vacuum handles Total Dynamics by identically coupling the local Laplacian curvature of the potential manifold to the information bits of moving charges.','','[]','[]','[\"vector-poisson-equation-768a0e19\",\"vector-potential-law-bffaccf7\"]'),
(2009944,'navier-stokes-equations','fluids-nonlinear','The Navier-Stokes Equations','<p>The <strong>Navier-Stokes Equations</strong> represent the pinnacle of classical fluid mechanics, providing a rigorous mathematical description of the motion of viscous fluid substances. In university-level physics, these partial differential equations (PDEs) are derived from the fundamental conservation laws of mass, momentum, and energy. They govern phenomena ranging from the laminar flow of blood in capillaries to the high-Reynolds-number turbulence in stellar interiors and galactic gas clouds.</p><h3>1. The Continuum Hypothesis and Conservation Laws</h3><p>The derivation of the Navier-Stokes equations rests on the <strong>Continuum Hypothesis</strong>, which treats the fluid as a continuous medium rather than a collection of discrete particles. The equations are essentially a statement of <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/isaac-newton\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Newton</strong></a>\'s Second Law applied to fluid elements. The first component is the <strong>Continuity Equation</strong>, representing the conservation of mass: \\( \\frac{\\partial \\rho}{\\partial t} + \\nabla \\cdot (\\rho \\mathbf{v}) = 0 \\). For an incompressible fluid, this simplifies to \\( \\nabla \\cdot \\mathbf{v} = 0 \\), imposing a divergence-free constraint on the velocity field.</p><h3>2. The Cauchy Stress Tensor and Stokes\' Hypothesis</h3><p>In a viscous fluid, internal forces are described by the <strong>Cauchy Stress Tensor</strong> (\\( \\sigma \\)), which accounts for both isotropic pressure and anisotropic viscous stresses. For a Newtonian fluid, the stress is assumed to be linearly proportional to the rate of strain. <strong>Stokes\' Hypothesis</strong> further simplifies this by relating the bulk viscosity to the shear viscosity. The resulting stress tensor is decomposed as: \\( \\sigma = -p\\mathbf{I} + \\mu (\\nabla \\mathbf{v} + (\\nabla \\mathbf{v})^T) + \\lambda (\\nabla \\cdot \\mathbf{v})\\mathbf{I} \\), where \\( \\mu \\) is the dynamic viscosity and \\( \\lambda \\) is the second viscosity coefficient.</p><h3>3. The Momentum Equation: Advection and Diffusion</h3><p>The core of the Navier-Stokes framework is the momentum equation: \\[ \\rho \\left( \\frac{\\partial \\mathbf{v}}{\\partial t} + \\mathbf{v} \\cdot \\nabla \\mathbf{v} \\right) = -\\nabla p + \\mu \\nabla^2 \\mathbf{v} + \\mathbf{f} \\] This equation highlights the competition between <strong>Advection</strong> (the non-linear term \\( \\mathbf{v} \\cdot \\nabla \\mathbf{v} \\)) and <strong>Diffusion</strong> (the viscous term \\( \\mu \\nabla^2 \\mathbf{v} \\)). The non-linearity of the advective term is the source of the complex, often chaotic behavior observed in fluid systems, making the equations notoriously difficult to solve analytically.</p><h3>4. Dimensionless Analysis: The Reynolds and Mach Numbers</h3><p>To characterize fluid regimes, physicists use dimensionless numbers derived from the Navier-Stokes equations. The most critical is the <strong>Reynolds Number</strong> (\\( Re = \\rho v L / \\mu \\)), which measures the ratio of inertial forces to viscous forces. At low \\( Re \\), flow is <strong>Laminar</strong> and predictable; at high \\( Re \\), it becomes <strong>Turbulent</strong>. Additionally, the <strong>Mach Number</strong> (\\( M = v/c_s \\)) determines the importance of compressibility, with \\( M \\gt 0.3 \\) typically requiring the full compressible form of the equations.</p><h3>5. The Millennium Problem: Existence and Smoothness</h3><p>Despite their widespread use, the mathematical foundation of the 3D incompressible Navier-Stokes equations remains incomplete. One of the seven <strong>Millennium Prize Problems</strong> is to prove whether, given smooth initial conditions, a solution always exists and remains smooth (without \"blowing up\") for all time. This is not merely a formal concern; it touches on whether the continuum description of fluids remains physically consistent at all scales or if the equations eventually fail to describe reality as singularities form.</p><h3>6. From Laminar Flow to High-Reynolds Turbulence</h3><p>In the limit of high Reynolds numbers, fluids enter the regime of <strong>Turbulence</strong>, characterized by a self-similar cascade of energy from large scales to small scales (the <strong>Kolmogorov Cascade</strong>). In astrophysics, turbulence in the <strong>Interstellar Medium (ISM)</strong> and <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/accretion-disk\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Accretion Disks</strong></a> is modeled using the Navier-Stokes equations coupled with magnetic fields (MHD). Because direct simulation of all scales is computationally impossible, researchers rely on <strong>Large Eddy Simulations (LES)</strong> and <strong>Reynolds-Averaged Navier-Stokes (RANS)</strong> models to approximate the chaotic transfer of momentum.</p>','The Navier-Stokes Equations represent the pinnacle of classical fluid mechanics, providing a rigorous mathematical description of the motion of viscous fluid substances. In university-level physics, these partial differential equations (PDEs) are derived from the fundamental conservation laws of mass, momentum, and energy. They govern phenomena ranging from the laminar flow of blood in capillaries to the high-Reynolds-number turbulence in stellar interiors and galactic gas clouds.','The Navier-Stokes Equations represent the pinnacle of classical fluid mechanics, providing a rigorous mathematical description of the motion of viscous fluid substances. In university-level physics, these partial differential equations (PDEs) are derived from the fundamental conservation laws of mass, momentum, and energy. They govern phenomena ranging from the laminar flow of blood in capillaries to the high-Reynolds-number turbulence in stellar interiors and galactic gas clouds.','<svg style=\"color: #FFD700; vertical-align: -2.148ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"37.522ex\" height=\"5.428ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -1449.5 16584.6 2399\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><defs><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-I-1D70C\" d=\"M58 -216Q25 -216 23 -186Q23 -176 73 26T127 234Q143 289 182 341Q252 427 341 441Q343 441 349 441T359 442Q432 442 471 394T510 276Q510 219 486 165T425 74T345 13T266 -10H255H248Q197 -10 165 35L160 41L133 -71Q108 -168 104 -181T92 -202Q76 -216 58 -216ZM424 322Q424 359 407 382T357 405Q322 405 287 376T231 300Q217 269 193 170L176 102Q193 26 260 26Q298 26 334 62Q367 92 389 158T418 266T424 322Z\"></path><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-S3-28\" d=\"M701 -940Q701 -943 695 -949H664Q662 -947 636 -922T591 -879T537 -818T475 -737T412 -636T350 -511T295 -362T250 -186T221 17T209 251Q209 962 573 1361Q596 1386 616 1405T649 1437T664 1450H695Q701 1444 701 1441Q701 1436 681 1415T629 1356T557 1261T476 1118T400 927T340 675T308 359Q306 321 306 250Q306 -139 400 -430T690 -924Q701 -936 701 -940Z\"></path><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-I-1D715\" d=\"M202 508Q179 508 169 520T158 547Q158 557 164 577T185 624T230 675T301 710L333 715H345Q378 715 384 714Q447 703 489 661T549 568T566 457Q566 362 519 240T402 53Q321 -22 223 -22Q123 -22 73 56Q42 102 42 148V159Q42 276 129 370T322 465Q383 465 414 434T455 367L458 378Q478 461 478 515Q478 603 437 639T344 676Q266 676 223 612Q264 606 264 572Q264 547 246 528T202 508ZM430 306Q430 372 401 400T333 428Q270 428 222 382Q197 354 183 323T150 221Q132 149 132 116Q132 21 232 21Q244 21 250 22Q327 35 374 112Q389 137 409 196T430 306Z\"></path><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-B-1D42F\" d=\"M401 444Q413 441 495 441Q568 441 574 444H580V382H510L409 156Q348 18 339 6Q331 -4 320 -4Q318 -4 313 -4T303 -3H288Q273 -3 264 12T221 102Q206 135 197 156L96 382H26V444H34Q49 441 145 441Q252 441 270 444H279V382H231L284 264Q335 149 338 149Q338 150 389 264T442 381Q442 382 418 382H394V444H401Z\"></path><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-I-1D461\" d=\"M26 385Q19 392 19 395Q19 399 22 411T27 425Q29 430 36 430T87 431H140L159 511Q162 522 166 540T173 566T179 586T187 603T