ranslate(722,0)\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(1147,-152.7) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"1D434\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-I-1D434\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(4197.6,0)\"><use data-c=\"28\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-28\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"msub\" transform=\"translate(4586.6,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D70C\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-I-1D70C\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" transform=\"translate(550,-152.7) scale(0.707)\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D434\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-I-1D434\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(750,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D435\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-I-1D435\"></use></g></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(6253.6,0)\"><use data-c=\"29\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-29\"></use></g></g></g></svg>','[]','[]','[\"the-ftl-block-33c4d8ec\",\"local-independence-45ec1276\",\"paradox-prevention-97250117\",\"born-defense-b6bec42b\"]'),
(2010025,'non-separable-states','determinism-and-locality','Non-Separable States','<p>Non-Separable States (or entangled states) are quantum states of composite systems that cannot be written as a product of the individual states of their components. In university-level physics, non-separability is the \"Source Code\" of <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/quantum-non-locality\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Quantum Non-Locality</strong></a>. It represents a fundamental departure from the classical assumption of <strong>Locality</strong>, proving that the  can host holistic entities that occupy multiple spatial regions simultaneously.</p>\n\n                    <h3>1. Product States vs. Entangled States</h3>\n                    <p>In a classical system, two objects A and B are always \"Separable\": the total state is simply the list of properties for A and the list for B (\\( \\Psi_{AB} = \\psi_A \\otimes \\phi_B \\)). In a <strong>Non-Separable</strong> state, however, the individual particles no longer have their own separate <strong>Wave Functions</strong>. Only the system as a whole has a well-defined state, a fact that challenges the <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/scientific-realism\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Scientific Realism</strong></a> of independent subatomic parts.</p>\n\n                    <h3>2. Schmidt Decomposition and Purity</h3>\n                    <p>The mathematical test for non-separability is the <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/schmidt-decomposition\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Schmidt Decomposition</strong></a>. If the Schmidt rank of a state is greater than 1, the state is non-separable. This quantified by the <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/von-neumann-entropy\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Von Neumann Entropy</strong></a> of the <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/reduced-density-matrix\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Reduced Density Matrix</strong></a>. A non-zero entropy in a sub-system of a pure global state is the definitive signature of entanglement, linking <strong>Statistical Mechanics</strong> to the 4D geometry of the <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/state-vector\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>State Vector</strong></a>.</p>\n\n                    <h3>3. Holism in the </h3>\n                    <p>Non-separability implies that the universe is <strong>Holistic</strong>. A measurement on particle A at one end of the galaxy instantly updates the mathematical description of particle B at the other. While this does not violate the <strong>Cosmic Speed Limit</strong> for information (<strong>No-Communication Theorem</strong>), it proves that the  is \"woven\" together by non-local correlations that do not diminish with distance.</p>\n\n                    <h3>4. <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/entanglement-entropy\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Entanglement Entropy</strong></a> and Space-Time</h3>\n                    <p>In modern <strong>Theoretical Physics</strong>, non-separability is seen as the \"Glue\" that creates space itself. The <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/ryu-takayanagi-formula\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Ryu-Takayanagi Formula</strong></a> relates the entanglement entropy of a region to the area of a minimal surface in a higher-dimensional space (the <strong>Holographic Principle</strong>). This suggests that the  is not a background stage, but an emergent property of the non-separable links between <strong>Qubits</strong> of information.</p>\n\n                    <h3>5. Non-Separability in Quantum Computing</h3>\n                    <p>Non-separable states are the \"Fuel\" of quantum computation. Algorithms like Shor\'s or Grover\'s rely on the large-scale non-separability of multiple qubits to perform calculations across a massive <strong>Phase Space</strong> simultaneously. This \"Parallelism\" is only possible because the computer exists in a single, non-separable 4D state, allowing for the processing of <strong>Information Density</strong> beyond classical limits.</p>\n\n                    <h3>6. Epistemic status: The One-ness of Matter</h3>\n                    <p>The existence of non-separable states forces us to rethink the <strong>Ontology</strong> of \"Objects.\" If two electrons can be non-separable, then the \"Electron\" is not a localized particle but a specific excitation of a global . This view, central to <strong>Relativistic Quantum Field Theory</strong>, dissolves the boundary between \"Me\" and \"the Universe,\" suggesting that <strong>Physical Causality</strong> is a property of a single, unified quantum system.</p>','Non-Separable States (or entangled states) are quantum states of composite systems that cannot be written as a product of the individual states of their components. In university-level physics, non-separability is the \"Source Code\" of Quantum Non-Locality. It represents a fundamental departure from the classical assumption of Locality, proving that the can host holistic entities that occupy multiple spatial regions simultaneously.','Non-Separable States (or entangled states) are quantum states of composite systems that cannot be written as a product of the individual states of their components. In university-level physics, non-separability is the \"Source Code\" of Quantum Non-Locality. It represents a fundamental departure from the classical assumption of Locality, proving that the  can host holistic entities that occupy multiple spatial regions simultaneously.','<svg style=\"color: #FFD700; vertical-align: -0.464ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"15.756ex\" height=\"2.034ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -694 6964 899\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><defs><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-N-3A8\" d=\"M340 622Q338 623 335 625T331 629T325 631T314 634T298 635T274 636T239 637H212V683H224Q248 680 389 680T554 683H566V637H539Q479 637 464 635T439 622L438 407Q438 192 439 192Q443 193 449 195T474 207T507 232T536 276T557 344Q560 365 562 417T573 493Q587 536 620 544Q627 546 671 546H715L722 5