237T84 250T98 270H679Q694 262 694 250T679 230H98Q84 237 84 250Z\"></path></defs><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D43B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-I-1D43B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1165.8,0)\"><use data-c=\"3D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-3D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mfrac\" transform=\"translate(2221.6,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\" transform=\"translate(220,676)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mover\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D44E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-I-1D44E\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(264.5,-2) translate(-250 0)\"><use data-c=\"2D9\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-2D9\"></use></g></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(220,-686)\"><use data-c=\"1D44E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-I-1D44E\"></use></g><rect width=\"729\" height=\"60\" x=\"120\" y=\"220\"></rect></g><g data-mml-node=\"mstyle\" transform=\"translate(3190.6,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mspace\"></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(3746.3,0)\"><use data-c=\"27F9\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-27F9\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mstyle\" transform=\"translate(5384.3,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mspace\"></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(5940.1,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D44E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-I-1D44E\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(6469.1,0)\"><use data-c=\"28\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-28\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(6858.1,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D461\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-I-1D461\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(7219.1,0)\"><use data-c=\"29\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-29\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(7885.9,0)\"><use data-c=\"3D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-3D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"msub\" transform=\"translate(8941.7,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D44E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-I-1D44E\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(562,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"30\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-30\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"msup\" transform=\"translate(9907.2,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D452\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-I-1D452\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" transform=\"translate(499,413) scale(0.707)\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D43B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-I-1D43B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(888,0)\"><use data-c=\"28\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-28\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(1277,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D461\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-I-1D461\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1638,0)\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"msub\" transform=\"translate(2416,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D461\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-I-1D461\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(394,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"30\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-30\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(3213.6,0)\"><use data-c=\"29\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-29\"></use></g></g></g></g></g></svg>','[]','[]','[\"exponential-growth-d48b2ba1\",\"lambda-drive-c11714f4\",\"communication-barrier-cefed637\",\"inflationary-stretching-c8b72931\"]'),
(2010037,'de-sitter-universe','friedmann-equations','The De Sitter Universe (\\(\\Omega_\\Lambda = 1\\))','<p>The <strong>De Sitter Universe</strong> is a cosmological model representing a spatially flat universe dominated entirely by a positive <strong>Cosmological Constant</strong> (\\( \\Lambda \\)). In university-level physics, it is the maximal-symmetry vacuum solution to the <strong>Einstein Field Equations</strong>. It represents both the \"Starting Point\" of the universe (during <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/cosmic-inflation\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Cosmic Inflation</strong></a>) and its \"Ending Point\" (the <strong>Big Freeze</strong>), illustrating the ultimate 4D geometry of empty, energized space.</p>\n\n                    <h3>1. The Pure Vacuum State</h3>\n                    <p>In a De Sitter universe, all matter and radiation densities are zero (\\( \\rho_m = \\rho_r = 0 \\)). The only <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/supernova-energy-source\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>energy source</strong></a> is the <strong>Dark Energy Density</strong> (\\( \\rho_\\Lambda \\)). Because this density is constant, the <strong>First Friedmann Equation</strong> yields a constant expansion rate \\( H \\), leading to <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/exponential-expansion\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Exponential Expansion</strong></a>. The  is \"Self-Similar\" in time, meaning the universe looks the same at every epoch.</p>\n\n                    <h3>2. Negative Pressure and Repulsion</h3>\n                    <p>The stability of the De Sitter model requires <strong>Negative Pressure</strong> (\\( P = -\\rho c^2 \\)). In the <strong>Acceleration Equation</strong>, this tension acts as a source of <strong>Repulsive Gravity</strong>.\n                    \\[ \\frac{\\ddot{a}}{a} = \\frac{\\Lambda c^2}{3} \\gt 0 \\]\n                    This ensures that the 4D grid is always accelerating outward, making the De Sitter universe the antithesis of the <strong>Einstein-de Sitter</strong> matter-only model.</p>\n\n                    <h3>3. Static vs. Expanding Coordinates</h3>\n                    <p>A university-level nuance of the De Sitter manifold is its dual coordinate representations. \n                        <ul>\n                            <li><strong>Expanding Form:</strong> \\( a(t) = e^{Ht} \\)—The \"Standard\" view for <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/cosmic-expansion\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Cosmic Expansion</strong></a>.</li>\n                            <li><strong>Static Form:</strong> The metric looks like a stationary gravitational field (similar to Schwarzschild) with a <strong>Potential Barrier</strong>.</li>\n                        </ul>\n                    This duality links <strong>Physical Cosmology</strong> to the 4D geometry of <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/black-hole\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Black Holes</strong></a>, where the De Sitter horizon behaves like an inverted event horizon.</p>\n\n                    <h3>4. The Cosmological Event Horizon</h3>\n                    <p>The De Sitter universe possesses a <strong>Cosmological Horizon</strong> at distance \\( r_H = c/H \\). Unlike the particle horizon of the <strong>Einstein-de Sitter</strong> model, which grows over time, the De Sitter horizon is fixed in size. Any light emitted beyond this  can never reach the origin. This represents the ultimate <strong>Epistemic Limit</strong> of the universe, as the interior becomes a causally isolated 4D bubble.</p>\n\n                    <h3>5. De Sitter Space and Quantum Fluctuations</h3>\n                    <p>During the <strong>Early Universe</strong> inflation, the De Sitter expansion stretched  fluctuations to macroscopic scales. This process generated the \"Acoustic Peaks\" of the <strong>CMB Theory</strong> and the <strong>Density Profile</strong> of modern galaxies. The De Sitter vacuum is thus the \"Mother\" of all structure in the , linking the empty vacuum to the visible stars.</p>\n\n                    <h3>6. Epistemic Status: The Final Attractor</h3>\n                    <p>The <strong>\\(\\Lambda\\)-CDM</strong> model shows that our universe is asymptotically approaching a De Sitter state. As matter dilutes to negligible levels, the 4D <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/spacetime-causal-topology\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Causal Topology</strong></a> will eventually become indistinguishable from the De Sitter geometry. It is the \"Final Attractor\" of the <strong>Expansion History</strong>, anchoring <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/scientific-realism\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Scientific Realism</strong></a> in the belief that the universe will end as it began: a vast, empty, accelerating void.</p>','The De Sitter Universe is a cosmological model representing a spatially flat universe dominated entirely by a positive Cosmological Constant. In university-level physics, it is the maximal-symmetry vacuum solution to the Einstein Field Equations. It represents both the \"Starting Point\" of the universe (during Cosmic Inflation) and its \"Ending Point\" (the Big Freeze), illustrating the ultimate 4D geometry of empty, energized space.','The De Sitter Universe is a cosmological model representing a spatially flat universe dominated entirely by a positive Cosmological Constant (<svg style=\"color: #FFD700; vertical-align: 0;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.57ex\" height=\"1.62ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -716 694 716\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><defs><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-N-39B\" d=\"M320 708Q326 716 340 716H348H355Q367 716 372 708Q374 706 423 547T523 226T575 62Q581 52 591 50T634 46H661V0H653Q644 3 532 3Q411 3 390 0H379V46H392Q464 46 464 65Q463 70 390 305T316 539L246 316Q177 95 177 84Q177 72 198 59T248 46H253V0H245Q230 3 130 3Q47 3 38 0H32V46H45Q112 51 127 91Q128 92 224 399T320 708Z\"></path></defs><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1