"221D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-221D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"msup\" transform=\"translate(3001.6,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D461\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-I-1D461\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" transform=\"translate(394,413) scale(0.707)\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\"><use data-c=\"31\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-31\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\" transform=\"translate(500,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2F\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-2F\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(1000,0)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g></g></g></g></svg>','[]','[]','[\"standard-1-2-law-1a6403e3\",\"relativistic-push-92ee709a\",\"the-crossover-2a4308d0\",\"silk-damping-404b5948\"]'),
(2010039,'expansion-law','friedmann-equations','Cosmic Expansion Laws','<p>The <strong>Expansion Law</strong> \\( a(t) \\) describes how the 4D distance between objects in the universe increases over time. In university-level cosmology, these laws are derived from the <strong>Friedmann Equations</strong> by assuming different <strong>Equations of State</strong> for the cosmic fluid. Each law represents a distinct epoch in the <strong>History of the Universe</strong>, dictating the <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/spacetime-causal-topology\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Causal Topology</strong></a> and structure of the .</p>\n\n                    <h3>1. The General Power-Law Form</h3>\n                    <p>For a universe dominated by a component with equation of state \\( w \\), the scale factor grows as:\n                    \\[ a(t) \\propto t^{\\frac{2}{3(1+w)}} \\]\n                    This general law unifies all of classical cosmology. \n                        <ul>\n                            <li><strong>Radiation (w=1/3):</strong> \\( a(t) \\propto t^{1/2} \\).</li>\n                            <li><strong>Matter (w=0):</strong> \\( a(t) \\propto t^{2/3} \\).</li>\n                            <li><strong>Curvature (w=-1/3):</strong> \\( a(t) \\propto t^1 \\) (constant velocity).</li>\n                        </ul></p>\n\n                    <h3>2. The Exponential Law (w=-1)</h3>\n                    <p>When the expansion is driven by a <strong>Cosmological Constant</strong> or <strong>Dark Energy</strong> with \\( w=-1 \\), the power-law form fails. The expansion becomes <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/exponential-expansion\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Exponential Expansion</strong></a>: \\( a(t) \\propto e^{Ht} \\). this is fastest possible stable growth, leading to the causal isolation of the <strong>Big Freeze</strong>. It represents the  \"Inflating\" due to vacuum tension.</p>\n\n                    <h3>3. The Big Bang Singularity</h3>\n                    <p>All power-law expansion laws imply a \"Zero Point\" at \\( t=0 \\). this is <strong>Big Bang Singularity</strong>, where the <strong>Energy Density</strong> and temperature become infinite. While the <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/euler-lagrange-equations\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Euler-Lagrange Equations</strong></a> and <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/general-relativity\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>General Relativity</strong></a> break down at this point, the expansion laws provide the mathematical trajectory that traces the 4D <strong>Block Universe</strong> back to its <strong>Geometric Origin</strong>.</p>\n\n                    <h3>4. Deceleration and Acceleration</h3>\n                    <p>The expansion law determines the <strong>Expansion Parameter</strong> \\( q \\). If the exponent of \\( t \\) is less than 1 (as in the radiation and matter eras), the expansion is \"Decelerating\"—gravity is winning. If the expansion is exponential, it is \"Accelerating.\" Current data shows a transition from the \\( t^{2/3} \\) law to the \\( e^{Ht} \\) law around \\( z \\approx 0.6 \\), a milestone in <strong>Physical Cosmology</strong>.</p>\n\n                    <h3>5. Expansion in Curved Space</h3>\n                    <p>In a universe with non-zero curvature (\\( k \\neq 0 \\)), the expansion laws are modified by hyperbolic or trigonometric functions. In a \"Closed\" universe, the expansion law eventually reaches a maximum and reverses, leading to a <strong>Big Crunch</strong>. In an \"Open\" universe, it approaches a constant velocity \\( a(t) \\propto t \\). The <strong>Planck Satellite</strong> confirms our universe follows the flat-space laws to high precision.</p>\n\n                    <h3>6. Epistemic Status: The Scale Factor Mapping</h3>\n                    <p>The scale factor \\( a(t) \\) is not a directly measurable quantity; we measure <strong>Redshift</strong> (\\( z \\)) and <strong>Distance Modulus</strong>. The \"Expansion Law\" is the <strong>Theoretical Physics</strong> bridge that converts these observations into a coherent . It is the \"Master Curve\" that summarizes everything we know about the global 4D geometry of the universe.</p>','The Expansion Law describes how the 4D distance between objects in the universe increases over time. In university-level cosmology, these laws are derived from the Friedmann Equations by assuming different Equations of State for the cosmic fluid. Each law represents a distinct epoch in the History of the Universe, dictating the Causal Topology and structure of the.','The Expansion Law <svg style=\"color: #FFD700; vertical-align: -0.566ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"3.774ex\" height=\"2.262ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -750 1668 1000\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><defs><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-I-1D44E\" d=\"M33 157Q33 258 109 349T280 441Q331 441 370 392Q386 422 416 422Q429 422 439 414T449 394Q449 381 412 234T374 68Q374 43 381 35T402 26Q411 27 422 35Q443 55 463 131Q469 151 473 152Q475 153 483 153H487Q506 153 506 144Q506 138 501 117T481 63T449 13Q436 0 417 -8Q409 -10 393 -10Q359 -10 336 5T306 36L300 51Q299 52 296 50Q294 48 292 46Q233 -10 172 -10Q117 -10 75 30T33 157ZM351 328Q351 334 346 350T323 385T277 405Q242 405 210 374T160 293Q131 214 119 129Q119 126 119 118T118 106Q118 61 136 44T179 26Q217 26 254 59T298 110Q300 114 325 217T351 328Z\"></path><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-N-28\" d=\"M94 250Q94 319 104 381T127 488T164 576T202 643T244 695T277 729T302 750H315H319Q333 750 333 741Q333 738 316 720T275 667T226 581T184 443T167 250T184 58T225 -81T274 -167T316 -220T333 -241Q333 -250 318 -250H315H302L274 -226Q180 -141 137 -14T94 250Z\"></path><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-I-1D461\" d=\"M26 385Q19 392 19 395Q19 399 22 411T27 425Q29 430 36 430T87 431H140L159 511Q162 522 166 540T173 566T179 586T187 603T197 615T211 624T229 626Q247 625 254 615T261 596Q261 589 252 549T232 470L222 433Q222 431 272 431H323Q330 424 330 420Q330 398 317 385H210L174