></g><g data-mml-node=\"mtext\" transform=\"translate(8917.3,0)\"><use data-c=\"66\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-66\"></use><use data-c=\"6F\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-6F\" transform=\"translate(306,0)\"></use><use data-c=\"72\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-72\" transform=\"translate(806,0)\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mstyle\" transform=\"translate(10115.3,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mspace\"></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(11115.3,0)\"><use data-c=\"28\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-28\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(11504.3,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D465\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-I-1D465\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(12298.6,0)\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(13298.8,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D466\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-I-1D466\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"msup\" transform=\"translate(13788.8,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"29\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-29\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(422,413) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(14892.1,0)\"><use data-c=\"3C\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-3C\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(15947.9,0)\"><use data-c=\"30\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-30\"></use></g></g></g></svg>','[]','[]','[\"operator-commutation-bb62125f\",\"antiparticle-basis-03a5165b\",\"technical-relation-efc6c437\"]'),
(2010105,'causal-sets-theory','physical-causality','Causal Sets and Discrete Spacetime','<p><strong>Causal Set Theory (CST)</strong> is an approach to <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/quantum-gravity\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Quantum Gravity</strong></a> that posits that spacetime is fundamentally discrete rather than continuous. In university-level foundations, CST replaces the smooth manifold with a <strong>Partially Ordered Set (Poset)</strong> of spacetime \"Atoms.\" This view suggests that causality is not a property added to spacetime, but is the very substance from which the 4D geometry of the universe emerges.</p>\n\n                  <h3>1. Order and Number</h3>\n                  <p>The central mantra of CST is \"Order + Number = Geometry.\" The <strong>Order</strong> of elements (which event precedes which) defines the 4D <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/spacetime-causal-topology\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Causal Topology</strong></a> and the light-cone structure. The <strong>Number</strong> of elements in a region defines the 4D <strong>Volume</strong> of that region. This discrete 4D <strong>Ontology</strong> removes the need for a continuous metric tensor, deriving all geometric facts from the 4D <strong>Poset Relation</strong>.</p>\n\n                  <h3>2. Spacetime Atomism</h3>\n                  <p>CST assumes that spacetime has a \"Graininess\" at the Planck scale. Between any two events, there is only a <strong>Finite Number</strong> of elements. This <strong>Local Finiteness</strong> prevents the mathematical singularities found in <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/general-relativity\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>General Relativity</strong></a>, providing a natural cutoff for high-energy processes in the 4D <strong>Subatomic Vacuum</strong>. It represents a radical form of 4D <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/scientific-realism\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Scientific Realism</strong></a> where \"Continuity\" is merely a macroscopic illusion.</p>\n\n                  <h3>3. The Causal Relation</h3>\n                  <p>The fundamental link in CST is the <strong>Poset Relation</strong> \\( x \\prec y \\). This relation is reflexive, antisymmetric, and transitive. It encodes all the 4D <strong>Logical Basis</strong> of the universe\'s history. By \"Sprinkling\" these discrete points into a manifold, physicists can reconstruct the 4D <strong>Minkowski Spacetime</strong>, showing that the discrete structure is consistent with the success of continuous 4D theories at large scales.</p>','Causal Set Theory (CST) is an approach to Quantum Gravity that posits that spacetime is fundamentally discrete rather than continuous. In university-level foundations, CST replaces the smooth manifold with a Partially Ordered Set (Poset) of spacetime \"Atoms.\" This view suggests that causality is not a property added to spacetime, but is the very substance from which the 4D geometry of the universe emerges. The central mantra of CST is \"Order + Number = Geometry.\" The Order of elements (which event precedes which) defines the 4D Causal Topology and the light-cone structure.','Causal Set Theory (CST) is an approach to Quantum Gravity that posits that spacetime is fundamentally discrete rather than continuous. In university-level foundations, CST replaces the smooth manifold with a Partially Ordered Set (Poset) of spacetime \"Atoms.\" This view suggests that causality is not a property added to spacetime, but is the very substance from which the 4D geometry of the universe emerges. The central mantra of CST is \"Order + Number = Geometry.\" The Order of elements (which event precedes which) defines the 4D Causal Topology and the light-cone structure.','<svg style=\"color: #FFD700; vertical-align: -0.464ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"5.42ex\" height=\"1.683ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -539 2395.6 744\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><defs><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-I-1D465\" d