(2010120,'tensor-product-space','quantum-entanglement','Tensor Product Space','<p>The Tensor Product Space (\\( \\mathcal{H}_A \\otimes \\mathcal{H}_B \\)) is the mathematical framework used to describe composite quantum systems. In university-level quantum mechanics, when two independent systems with Hilbert spaces \\( \\mathcal{H}_A \\) and \\( \\mathcal{H}_B \\) are combined, the state space of the total system is not the direct sum, but the tensor product of the individual spaces. This construction is fundamental to the existence of <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/quantum-entanglement\" class=\"subtopic-link\">Quantum Entanglement</a>.</p>\n                    <h3>1. Dimensionality and Basis Construction</h3>\n                    <p>If \\( \\mathcal{H}_A \\) has dimension \\( N \\) and \\( \\mathcal{H}_B \\) has dimension \\( M \\), the composite space \\( \\mathcal{H}_{AB} \\) has dimension \\( N \\times M \\). If \\( \\{|i\\rangle_A\\} \\) and \\( \\{|j\\rangle_B\\} \\) are orthonormal bases for the individual spaces, then the set of all product states \\( \\{|i\\rangle_A \\otimes |j\\rangle_B\\} \\) forms an orthonormal basis for the composite space. This exponential growth in dimensionality is the primary reason why simulating large quantum systems is classically intractable.</p>\n                    <h3>2. Separable vs. Entangled States</h3>\n                    <p>A state \\( |\\Psi\\rangle_{AB} \\) is called <strong>Separable</strong> (or a product state) if it can be written as a simple product of states from each subsystem: \\( |\\Psi\\rangle_{AB} = |\\psi\\rangle_A \\otimes |\\phi\\rangle_B \\). However, the vast majority of vectors in the tensor product space cannot be written in this form. These <strong>Entangled States</strong> represent systems where the properties of the individual particles are inextricably linked, a phenomenon that has no classical counterpart.</p>','The Tensor Product Space is the mathematical framework used to describe composite quantum systems. In university-level quantum mechanics, when two independent systems with Hilbert spaces and are combined, the state space of the total system is not the direct sum, but the tensor product of the individual spaces. This construction is fundamental to the existence of Quantum Entanglement.','The Tensor Product Space (<svg style=\"color: #FFD700; vertical-align: -0.345ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"9.379ex\" height=\"1.891ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -683 4145.5 835.7\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><defs><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-C-48\" d=\"M18 487Q18 496 29 517T67 566T127 621T216 665T330 683Q359 683 376 669T397 643T400 622Q400 584 382 488T348 343Q348 342 467 342H587L594 366Q615 440 648 534T690 641Q701 656 723 669T764 683Q783 683 783 672L750 578Q716 485 677 346T625 101Q624 92 623 82T622 65T621 56Q621 20 658 20Q666 20 701 25Q709 52 736 69T785 87Q803 87 803 75T791 44T754 3T685 -33T588 -48Q568 -48 562 -46Q522 -31 522 13V23Q531 129 562 250L569 281L565 280Q561 278 556 277T549 274L438 273H328L321 249Q307 202 275 107T232 0Q219 -16 196 -28T155 -41Q149 -41 145 -39T140 -34T139 -29Q139 -24 148 -3T181 86T233 247Q240 270 240 272Q240 273 194 273H169Q139 273 139 285Q139 295 153 308T187 332Q206 341 236 342L260 343L264 359Q278 414 289 482T300 578Q300 613 260 613H254Q198 613 169 592Q148 578 127 544T104 508Q72 478 37 475Q18 475 18 487Z\"></path><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-I-1D434\" d=\"M208 74Q208 50 254 46Q272 46 272 35Q272 34 270 22Q267 8 264 4T251 0Q249 0 239 0T205 1T141 2Q70 2 50 0H42Q35 7 35 11Q37 38 48 46H62Q132 49 164 96Q170 102 345 401T523 704Q530 716 547 716H555H572Q578 707 578 706L606 383Q634 60 636 57Q641 46 701 46Q726 46 726 36Q726 34 723 22Q720 7 718 4T704 0Q701 0 690 0T651 1T578 2Q484 2 455 0H443Q437 6 437 9T439 27Q443 40 445 43L449 46H469Q523 49 533 63L521 213H283L249 155Q208 86 208 74ZM516 260Q516 271 504 416T490 562L463 519Q447 492 400 412L310 260L413 259Q516 259 516 260Z\"></path><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-N-2297\" 