(2010129,'superdense-coding','quantum-entanglement','Superdense Coding','<p>Superdense Coding is the inverse of <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/quantum-teleportation\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Quantum Teleportation</strong></a>. It is a communication protocol that allows a sender (Alice) to transmit two classical bits of information to a receiver (Bob) by sending only a single qubit, provided they share a pre-existing <a href=\"/physics/topic/quantum-physics\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Bell Pair</strong></a>.</p>\n\n                    <h3>1. Encoding via Local Unitary Operations</h3>\n                    <p>Alice and Bob start with a shared maximally entangled state \\( |\\Phi^+\\rangle_{AB} \\). To send the classical bits \\( 00, 01, 10, \\) or \\( 11 \\), Alice applies a specific <strong>Unitary Transformation</strong> to her local qubit (A). These operations map the shared state to one of the four orthogonal Bell states:\n                    \\[ |\\Phi^+\\rangle \\xrightarrow{I} |\\Phi^+\\rangle, \\quad |\\Phi^+\\rangle \\xrightarrow{X} |\\Psi^+\\rangle, \\quad |\\Phi^+\\rangle \\xrightarrow{Z} |\\Phi^-\\rangle, \\quad |\\Phi^+\\rangle \\xrightarrow{iY} |\\Psi^-\\rangle \\]\n                    Alice then sends her qubit A to Bob.</p>\n\n                    <h3>2. Decoding and Bell Measurement</h3>\n                    <p>Upon receiving qubit A, Bob possesses both qubits of the entangled pair. He performs a <strong>Bell State Measurement (BSM)</strong> in the 2-qubit Hilbert space. Because the four Bell states are <strong>Maximally Entangled</strong> and mutually orthogonal, Bob can distinguish between them with 100% certainty. The measurement outcome directly reveals the two classical bits Alice intended to send.</p>\n\n                    <h3>3. The Efficiency Paradox</h3>\n                    <p>In classical information theory, a single two-level system (a bit) can only carry one bit of information. Superdense coding seemingly doubles this capacity (2 bits per qubit). However, the \"extra\" bit is effectively stored in the pre-shared entanglement. This highlights that <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/quantum-entanglement\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Entanglement</strong></a> acts as a communication resource that, while not carrying information itself, can be \"consumed\" to enhance classical data transmission.</p>','Superdense Coding is the inverse of Quantum Teleportation. It is a communication protocol that allows a sender (Alice) to transmit two classical bits of information to a receiver (Bob) by sending only a single qubit, provided they share a pre-existing Bell Pair. Alice and Bob start with a shared maximally entangled state.','Superdense Coding is the inverse of Quantum Teleportation. It is a communication protocol that allows a sender (Alice) to transmit two classical bits of information to a receiver (Bob) by sending only a single qubit, provided they share a pre-existing Bell Pair. Alice and Bob start with a shared maximally entangled state <svg style=\"color: #FFD700; vertical-align: -0.566ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"7.177ex\" height=\"2.32ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -775.2 3172.2 1025.2\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><defs><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-N-7C\" d=\"M139 -249H137Q125 -249 119 -235V251L120 737Q130 750 139 750Q152 750 159 735V-235Q151 -249 141 -249H139Z\"></path><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-N-3A6\" d=\"M312 622Q310 623 307 625T303 629T297 631T286 634T270 635T246 636T211 637H184V683H196Q220 680 361 680T526 683H538V637H511Q468 637 447 635T422 631T411 622V533L425 531Q525 519 595 466T665 342Q665 301 642 267T583 209T506 172T425 152L411 150V61Q417 55 421 53T447 48T511 46H538V0H526Q502 3 361 3T196 0H184V46H211Q231 46 245 46T270 47T286 48T297 51T303 54T307 57T312 61V150H310Q309 151 289 153T232 166T160 195Q149 201 136 210T103 238T69 284T56 342Q56 414 128 467T294 530Q309 532 310 533H312V622ZM170 342Q170 207 307 188H312V495H309Q301 495 282 491T231 469T1