(2010153,'pilot-wave','theoretical-physics','Pilot Wave Theory','<p>Pilot Wave Theory (de Broglie-Bohm Mechanics) is a deterministic, non-local interpretation of quantum mechanics. It posits that particles have definite trajectories guided by a \"pilot wave,\" anchoring <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/scientific-realism\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Scientific Realism</strong></a> in objective reality.</p><h3>1. The Guidance Equation</h3><p>The state of a system is defined by the <strong>Wave Function (\\( \\psi \\))</strong> and the particle <strong>Positions (\\( \\mathbf{Q} \\))</strong>. The particles are moved by the <strong>Guidance Equation</strong>: \\[ \\mathbf{v} = \\frac{d\\mathbf{Q}}{dt} = \\frac{\\hbar}{m} \\text{Im}\\left( \\frac{\\nabla \\psi}{\\psi} \\right) \\] This ensures the <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/total-dynamics\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Total Dynamics</strong></a> are deterministic and trackable.</p><h3>2. The Quantum Potential</h3><p>By writing \\( \\psi = R e^{iS/\\hbar} \\), the Schr\\u00f6dinger equation becomes a Hamilton-Jacobi equation with an extra term, the <strong>Quantum Potential (Q)</strong>: \\[ Q = -\\frac{\\hbar^2}{2m} \\frac{\\nabla^2 R}{R} \\] This potential explains \"quantum\" behavior (like interference) as a classical-like force from the <strong>Hidden Variables</strong>.</p><h3>3. Quantum Equilibrium Hypothesis</h3><p>The probability density \\( P = |\\psi|^2 \\) is not an axiom but an equilibrium state (\\( P = \\rho \\)). Systems in \"quantum non-equilibrium\" would allow for <strong>Superluminal Signaling</strong>, but <strong>Statistical Mechanics</strong> drive the universe toward the standard Born Rule distribution.</p><h3>4. Non-Locality</h3><p>Pilot Wave Theory is explicitly non-local: the velocity of one particle depends on the positions of all other particles via the shared wave function. This reflects the <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/spacetime-causal-topology\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Causal Topology</strong></a> required to violate <strong>Bell\'s Inequality</strong>.</p><h3>5. Resolution of the Measurement Problem</h3><p>There is no \"collapse\" in Pilot Wave Theory. The \"cat\" is always either dead or alive because the particles have definite positions. Measurement simply reveals which branch of the <strong>Wave Function</strong> the particles are inhabiting.</p><h3>6. Theoretical Status</h3><p>While mathematically equivalent to standard quantum mechanics, Pilot Wave Theory is often preferred by those seeking a clear ontology for <strong>Quantum Physics</strong>. It provides a bridge between classical <strong>Theoretical Physics</strong> and the subatomic manifold.</p>','Pilot Wave Theory (de Broglie-Bohm Mechanics) is a deterministic, non-local interpretation of quantum mechanics. It posits that particles have definite trajectories guided by a \"pilot wave,\" anchoring Scientific Realism in objective reality.','Pilot Wave Theory (de Broglie-Bohm Mechanics) is a deterministic, non-local interpretation of quantum mechanics. It posits that particles have definite trajectories guided by a \"pilot wave,\" anchoring Scientific Realism in objective reality.','<svg style=\"color: #FFD700; vertical-align: -2.148ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"25.278ex\" height=\"5.428ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -1449.5 11172.8 2399\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><defs><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-B-1D42F\" d=\"M401 444Q413 441 495 441Q568 441 574 444H580V382H510L409 156Q348 18 339 6Q331 -4 320 -4Q318 -4 313 -4T303 -3H288Q273 -3 264 12T221 102Q206 135 197 156L96 382H26V444H34Q49 441 145 441Q252 441 270 444H279V382H231L284 264Q335 149 338 149Q338 150 389 264T442 381Q442 382 418 382H394V444H401Z\"></path><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-N-3D\" d=\"M56 347Q56 360 70 367H707Q722 359 722 347Q722 336 708 328L390 327H72Q56 332 56 347ZM56 153Q56 168 72 173H708Q722 163 722 153Q722 140 707 133H70Q56 140 56 153Z\"></path><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-I-1D451