(2010166,'quantum-entanglement','quantum-physics','Quantum Entanglement','<p>Quantum Entanglement occurs when particles interact such that the state of each cannot be described independently. In university-level physics, it represents the ultimate form of <strong>Inseparability</strong> in <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/hilbert-space\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Hilbert Space</strong></a>.</p><h3>1. Non-Separability</h3><p>A system is entangled if its <strong>State Vector (\\( |\\Psi\\rangle \\))</strong> cannot be written as a <strong>Tensor Product</strong>: \\[ |\\Psi\\rangle \\neq |\\psi_A\\rangle \\otimes |\\psi_B\\rangle \\] This implies the \"Whole\" is ontologically prior to the \"Parts\" in the <strong>Quantum Vacuum</strong>.</p><h3>2. Entanglement Entropy</h3><p>The degree of entanglement is quantified by the <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/von-neumann-entropy\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Von Neumann Entropy</strong></a> of the reduced density matrix: \\[ S = -\\text{Tr}(\\rho_A \\ln \\rho_A) \\] This metric is central to the study of <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/hawking-radiation\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Hawking Radiation</strong></a> and the <strong>Information Paradox</strong>.</p><h3>3. ER=EPR Conjecture</h3><p>The <strong>ER=EPR</strong> conjecture proposes that entangled particles are connected by a microscopic <strong>Einstein-Rosen Bridge</strong> (wormhole). This suggests that <strong>Entanglement</strong> is the \"glue\" that constructs the <strong>Structure of Spacetime</strong>.</p><h3>4. Bell State Basis</h3><p>The four <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/bell-state\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Bell States</strong></a> are the maximally entangled states for two qubits. They form a complete basis for the state space, providing the fundamental resource for <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/quantum-teleportation\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Quantum Teleportation</strong></a> and <strong>Quantum Computing</strong>.</p><h3>5. Monogamy of Entanglement</h3><p>Entanglement is \"monogamous\": if particle A is maximally entangled with B, it cannot be entangled with C. This restriction is a core principle of <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/information-theory\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Information Theory</strong></a> and ensures the security of <strong>Quantum Key Distribution</strong>.</p><h3>6. Geometric Entanglement</h3><p>In the <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/ads-cft\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>AdS/CFT Correspondence</strong></a>, the entanglement entropy of a boundary region is proportional to the area of a minimal surface in the bulk. This <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/ryu-takayanagi-formula\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Ryu-Takayanagi Formula</strong></a> provides a geometric origin for <strong>Quantum Physics</strong>.</p>','Quantum Entanglement occurs when particles interact such that the state of each cannot be described independently. In university-level physics, it represents the ultimate form of Inseparability in Hilbert Space.','Quantum Entanglement occurs when particles interact such that the state of each cannot be described independently. In university-level physics, it represents the ultimate form of Inseparability in Hilbert Space.','<svg style=\"color: #FFD700; vertical-align: -0.566ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"17.805ex\" height=\"2.262ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -750 7870 1000\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><defs><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-N-7C\" d=\"M139 -249H137Q125 -249 119 -235V251L120 737Q130 750 139 750Q152 750 159 735V-235Q151 -249 141 -249H139Z\"></path><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-N-3A8\" d=\"M340 622Q338 623 335 625T331 629T325 631T314 634T298 635T274 636T239 637H212V683H224Q248 680 389 680T554 683H566V637H539Q479 637 464 635T439 622L438 407Q438 192 439 192Q443 193 449 195T474 207T507 232T536 276T557 344Q560 365 562 417T573 493Q587 536 620 544Q627 546 671 546H715L722 540V515Q714 509 708 509Q680 505 671 476T658 392T644 307Q59