></g><g data-mml-node=\"msup\" transform=\"translate(694,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D450\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-I-1D450\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(466,363) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(751.8,-686)\"><use data-c=\"33\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-33\"></use></g><rect width=\"1763.6\" height=\"60\" x=\"120\" y=\"220\"></rect></g></g></g></svg>','[]','[]','[\"a-href-physics-subtopic-expansion-law-class-subtopic-link-expansion-law-a-4d5e3231\",\"a-href-physics-subtopic-cosmic-gravity-class-subtopic-link-cosmic-gravity-a-41a2a7bb\",\"a-href-physics-subtopic-energy-conservation-class-subtopic-link-energy-conservation-a-e48c9bc0\",\"a-href-physics-subtopic-expansion-parameter-class-subtopic-link-expansion-parameter-a-b9ac2004\"]'),
(2010169,'big-bang-theory','astrophysics','The Big Bang','<p>The Big Bang is the prevailing cosmological model for the <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/geometric-origin\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Geometric Origin</strong></a> and evolution of the universe. It asserts that the 4D spacetime manifold originated from a state of extremely high density and temperature approximately 13.8 billion years ago. In university-level cosmology, the Big Bang is not an explosion <em>in</em> space, but the expansion <em>of</em> space itself, governed by the <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/general-relativity\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>General Relativity</strong></a> and the unique <strong>Initial Conditions</strong> of the <strong>Early Universe</strong>.</p><h3>1. The Expansion of the Manifold</h3><p>The primary evidence for the Big Bang is the <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/cosmic-expansion\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Cosmic Expansion</strong></a> observed through the redshift of distant galaxies. According to <strong>Hubble\'s Law</strong>, the distance between any two points in the universe is increasing over time. This expansion is modeled by the <strong>Scale Factor (\\( a(t) \\))</strong> in the <strong>Friedmann-Lemaître-Robertson-Walker (FLRW)</strong> metric, showing that the <strong>Structure of Spacetime</strong> is a dynamic participant in the <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/total-dynamics\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Total Dynamics</strong></a> of the cosmos.</p><h3>2. The Cosmic Microwave Background (CMB)</h3><p>The \'Afterglow\' of the Big Bang is the <strong>CMB</strong> radiation, which was released during the <strong>Recombination</strong> era when the universe first became transparent. This background radiation is a nearly perfect blackbody, carrying a 4D snapshot of the <strong>Density Fluctuations</strong> that would later form galaxies. The uniformity of the CMB is a primary driver of the <strong>Inflationary Theory</strong>, suggesting a period of super-exponential growth in the first fraction of a second.</p><h3>3. Big Bang Nucleosynthesis (BBN)</h3><p>In the first few minutes, the universe was a dense nuclear reactor. <strong>BBN</strong> correctly predicts the primordial abundances of light elements (Hydrogen, Helium, Lithium), matching observations to extreme precision. This success anchors our <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/scientific-realism\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Scientific Realism</strong></a> in the belief that the subatomic laws of the <strong>Standard Model</strong> were active even at the birth of the 4D <strong>Block Universe</strong>.</p><h3>4. The Problem of the Singularity</h3><p>Classical <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/general-relativity\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>General Relativity</strong></a> predicts that the Big Bang started with a <strong>Physical Singularity</strong> where curvature and density become infinite. Theoretical physicists view this as an <strong>Epistemic Limit</strong>, indicating that our current models are incomplete. The quest for <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/quantum-gravity\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Quantum Gravity</strong></a> aims to replace the singularity with a <strong>Big Bounce</strong> or a discrete transition, seeking the fundamental <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/geometric-origin\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Geometric Origin</strong></a> of existence.</p><h3>5. <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/past-hypothesis\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>The Past Hypothesis</strong></a> and Entropy</h3><p>The Big Bang represents the <strong>Initial Condition</strong> of <strong>Extremely Low Entropy</strong>. This <strong>Past Hypothesis</strong> is the ultimate source of the <strong>Arrow of Time</strong>. Without this highly ordered beginning, the universe would be in thermal equilibrium, and the complex <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/history-of-the-universe\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>History of the Universe</strong></a> would be physically impossible. This links <strong>Thermodynamics</strong> directly to the <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/spacetime-causal-topology\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Causal Topology</strong></a> of the initial state.</p><h3>6. Fine-Tuning and the Multiverse</h3><p>The specific values of the <strong>Constants of Nature</strong> at the Big Bang appear to be <strong>Fine-Tuned</strong> for the emergence of complexity. This leads to the debate over the <strong>Anthropic Principle</strong> and the <strong>Multiverse</strong>. Philosophers and physicists utilize the <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/geometric-origin\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Geometric Origin</strong></a> of these parameters to test whether our Big Bang is a unique necessary event or one of many \'Bubbles\' in a vast 11D <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/m-theory\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>M-Theory</strong></a> landscape.</p>','The Big Bang is the prevailing cosmological model for the Geometric Origin and evolution of the universe. It asserts that the 4D spacetime manifold originated from a state of extremely high density and temperature approximately 13.8 billion years ago. In university-level cosmology, the Big Bang is not an explosion in space, but the expansion of space itself, governed by the General Relativity and the unique Initial Conditions of the Early Universe.','The Big Bang is the prevailing cosmological model for the Geometric Origin and evolution of the universe. It asserts that the 4D spacetime manifold originated from a state of extremely high density and temperature approximately 13.8 billion years ago. In university-level cosmology, the Big Bang is not an explosion in space, but the expansion of space itself, governed by the General Relativity and the unique Initial Conditions of the Early Universe.','<svg style=\"color: #FFD700; vertical-align: -0.566ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"3.774ex\" height=\"2.262ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -750 1668 1000\" xmlns:xlink=