1-TEX-I-1D706\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(261.5,-686)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-32\"></use></g><rect width=\"783\" height=\"60\" x=\"120\" y=\"220\"></rect></g></g></g></svg>','[]','[]','[\"constructive-fit-a6967b68\",\"fixed-endpoints-f1f44b04\",\"atomic-loops-e4743c90\",\"energy-minimum-096eab4a\"]'),
(2010245,'davisson-germer-experiment','de-broglie-hypothesis','The Davisson-Germer Experiment','<p>The <strong>Davisson-Germer Experiment</strong> (1927) provided the first experimental confirmation of the <strong>de Broglie Hypothesis</strong>, proving that electrons behave as waves. In university-level physics, this experiment is the \"Mirror\" of X-ray diffraction: it showed that a beam of particles reflecting off a crystal surface produces an interference pattern, definitively establishing <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/wave-particle-duality\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Wave-Particle Duality</strong></a> as a physical reality.</p>\n\n                    <h3>1. The Setup: Electron Scattering</h3>\n                    <p>Clinton Davisson and Lester Germer fired low-energy electrons at a nickel crystal target in a vacuum. They measured the intensity of scattered electrons as a function of the scattering angle (\\( \\phi \\)). According to classical physics, the intensity should be uniform. Instead, they found sharp \"peaks\" of intensity at specific angles, exactly as one would see with <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/electromagnetic-radiation\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Electromagnetic Radiation</strong></a>.</p>\n\n                    <h3>2. Application of Bragg\'s Law</h3>\n                    <p>The peaks intensity were the result of <strong>Interference</strong> between matter waves reflecting off different planes of atoms in the crystal. This described by <strong>Bragg\'s Law</strong>:\n                    \\[ n\\lambda = d \\sin \\theta \\]\n                    By calculating the <strong>Matter Wave</strong> wavelength from the accelerating voltage (\\( V \\)) and the <strong>de Broglie Relation</strong>, Davisson and Germer found that the measured diffraction angles matched theory to within 1%. This was the \"Smoking Gun\" for quantum mechanics.</p>\n\n                    <h3>3. The Nickel Crystal Accident</h3>\n                    <p>The discovery was partly accidental. During the experiment, a vacuum leak caused the nickel target to oxidize. To clean it, Davisson and Germer heated the nickel, which caused it to form large, highly regular crystal grains. These grains acted as a <strong>Diffraction Grating</strong> for the electrons. This \"Clean Lab\" accident revealed the hidden <strong>Geometric Origin</strong> of the electron\'s behavior, which had been blurred in poly-crystalline samples.</p>\n\n                    <h3>4. Matter Wave vs. X-ray Distinction</h3>\n                    <p>A university-level detail is the distinction between electron diffraction and X-ray diffraction. While X-rays interact with the electron cloud of atoms, electrons interact with the <strong>Electric Potential</strong> (nucleus and cloud). This makes electron diffraction much more sensitive to the surface properties of materials, leading to the modern technology of <strong>LEED</strong> (Low-Energy Electron Diffraction).</p>\n\n                    <h3>5. Confirmation of non-relativistic c</h3>\n                    <p>The experiment also verified that the wavelength follows the <strong>non-relativistic</strong> momentum formula at low speeds. For a voltage \\( V \\), the wavelength is \\( \\lambda = h/\\sqrt{2meV} \\). The success of this formula across different voltages proved that the <strong>Planck Constant</strong> (\\( h \\)) is the universal scaling factor between the classical world of energy and the quantum world of waves.</p>\n\n                    <h3>6. Legacy: The Birth of Quantum Engineering</h3>\n                    <p>The Davisson-Germer experiment turned \"Matter Waves\" from a wild hypothesis into a practical tool. It led directly to the development of the <strong>Electron Microscope</strong>, which uses the short wavelengths of high-speed electrons to see objects thousands of times smaller than light microscopes can. It proved that the <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/total-dynamics\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Total Dynamics</strong></a> of the subatomic world can be controlled by manipulating the wave phase of matter.</p>','The Davisson-Germer Experiment (1927) provided the first experimental confirmation of the de Broglie Hypothesis, proving that electrons behave as waves. In university-level physics, this experiment is the \"Mirror\" of X-ray diffraction: it showed that a beam of particles reflecting off a crystal surface produces an interference pattern, definitively establishing Wave-Particle Duality as a physical reality. Clinton Davisson and Lester Germer fired low-energy electrons at a nickel crystal target in a vacuum.','The Davisson-Germer Experiment (1927) provided the first experimental confirmation of the de Broglie Hypothesis, proving that electrons behave as waves. In university-level physics, this experiment is the \"Mirror\" of X-ray diffraction: it showed that a beam of particles reflecting off a crystal surface produces an interference pattern, definitively establishing Wave-Particle Duality as a physical reality. Clinton Davisson and Lester Germer fired low-energy electrons at a nickel crystal target in a vacuum.','<svg style=\"color: #FFD700; vertical-align: -0.186ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"11.464ex\" height=\"1.781ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -705 5066.9 787\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><defs><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-I-1D45B\" d=\"M21 287Q22 293 24 303T36 341T56 388T89 425T135 442Q171 442 195 424T225 390T231 369Q231 367 232 367L243 378Q304 442 382 442Q436 442 469 415T503 336T465 179T427 52Q427 26 444 26Q450 26 453 27Q482 32 505 65T540 145Q542 153 560 153Q580 153 580 145Q580 144 576 130Q568 101 554 73T508 17T439 -10Q392 -10 371 17T350 73Q350 92 386 193T423 345Q423 404 379 404H374Q288 404 229 303L222 291L189 157Q156 26 151 16Q138 -11 108 -11Q95 -11 87 -5T76 7T74 17Q74 30 112 180T152 343Q153 348 153 366Q153 405 129 405Q91 405 66 305Q60 285 60 284Q58 278 41 278H27Q21 284 21 287Z\"></path><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-I-1D706\" d=\"M166 673Q166 685 183 694H202Q292 691 316 644Q322 629 373 486T474 207T524 67Q531 47 537 34T546 15T551 6T555 2T556 -2T550 -11H482Q457 3 450 18T399 152L354 277L340 262Q327 246 293 207T236 141Q211 112 174 69Q123 9 111 -1T83 -12Q47 -12 47 20Q47 37 61 52T199 187Q229 216 266 252T321 306L338 322Q338 323 288 462T234 612Q214 657 183 657Q166 657 166 673Z\"></path><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-N-3D\" d=\"M56 347Q56 360 70 367H707Q722 359 722 347Q722 336 708 328L390 327H72Q56 332 56 347ZM56 153Q56 168 72 173H708Q722 163 722 153Q722 140 707 133H70Q56 140 56 153Z\"></path><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-I-1D451\" d=\"M366 683Q367 683 438 688T511 694Q523 694 523 686Q523 679 450 384T375 83T374 68Q374 26 402 26Q411 27 422 35Q443 55 463 131Q469 151 473 152Q475 153 483 153H487H491Q506 153 506 145Q506 140 503 129Q490 79 473 48T445 8T417 -8Q409 -10 393 -10Q359 -10 336 5T306 36L300 51Q299 52 296 50Q294 48 292 46Q233 -10 172 -10Q117 -10 75 30T33 157Q33 205 53 255T101 341Q148 398 195 420T280 442Q336 442 364 400Q369 394 369 396Q370 400 396 505T424 616Q424 629 417 632T378 637H357Q351 643 351 645T353 664Q358 683 366 683ZM352 326Q329 405 277 405Q242 405 210 374T160 293Q131 214 119 129Q119 126 119 118T118 106Q118 61 136 44T179 26Q233 26 290 98L298 109L352 326Z\"></path><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-N-73\" d=\"M295 316Q295 356 268 385T190 414Q154 414 128 401Q98 382 98 349Q97 344 98 336T114 312T157 287Q175 282 201 278T245 269T277 256Q294 248 310 236T342 195T359 133Q359 71 321 31T198 -10H190Q138 -10 94 26L86 19L77 10Q71 4 65 -1L54 -11H46H42Q39 -11 33 -5V74V132Q33 153 35 157T45 162H54Q66 162 70 158T75 146T82 119T101 77Q136 26 198 26Q295 26 295 104Q295 133 277 151Q257 175 194 187T111 210Q75 227 54 256T33 318Q33 357 50 384T93 424T143 442T187 447H198Q238 447 268 432L283 424L292 431Q302 440 314 448H322H326Q329 448 335 442V310L329 304H301Q295 310 295 316Z\"></path><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-N-69\" d=\"M69 609Q69 637 87 653T131 669Q154 667 171 652T188 609Q188 579 171 564T129 549Q104 549 87 564T69 609ZM247 0Q232 3 143 3Q132 3 106 3T56 1L34 0H26V46H42Q70 46 91 49Q100 53 102 60T104 102V205V293Q104 345 102 359T88 378Q74 385 41 385H30V408Q30 431 32 431L42 432Q52 433 70 434T106 436Q123 437 142 438T171 441T182 442H185V62Q190 52 197 50T232 46H255V0H247Z\"></path><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-N-6E\" d=\"M41 46H55Q94 46 102 60V68Q102 77 102 91T102 122T103 161T103 203Q103 234 103 269T102 328V351Q99 370 88 376T43 385H25V408Q25 431 27 431L37 432Q47 433 65 434T102 436Q119 437 138 438T167 441T178 442H181V402Q181 364 182 364T187 369T199 384T218 402T247 421T285 437Q305 442 336 442Q450 438 463 329Q464 322 464 190V104Q464 66 466 59T477 49Q498 46 526 46H542V0H534L510 1Q487 2 460 2T422 3Q319 3 310 0H302V46H318Q379 46 379 62Q380 64 380 200Q379 335 378 343Q372 371 358 385T334 402T308 404Q263 404 229 370Q202 343 195 315T187 232V168V108Q187 78 188 68T191 55T200 49Q221 46 249 46H265V0H257L234 1Q210 2 183 2T145 3Q42 3 33 0H25V46H41Z\"></path><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-N-2061\" d=\"\"></path><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-I-1D703\" d=\"M35 200Q35 302 74 415T180 610T319 704Q320 704 327 704T339 705Q393 701 423 656Q462 596 462 495Q462 380 417 261T302 66T168 -10H161Q125 -10 99 10T60 63T41 130T35 200ZM383 566Q383 668 330 668Q294 668 260 623T204 521T170 421T157 371Q206 370 254 370L351 371Q352 372 359 404T375 484T383 566ZM113 132Q113 26 166 26Q181 26 198 36T239 74T287 161T335 307L340 324H145Q145 321 136 286T120 208T113 132Z\"></path></defs><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D45B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-I-1D45B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(600,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D706\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-I-1D706\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1460.8,0)\"><use data-c=\"3D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-3D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(2516.6,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D451\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-I-1D451\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(3203.2,0)\"><use data-c=\"73\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-73\"></use><use data-c=\"69\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-69\" transform=\"translate(394,0)\"></use><use data-c=\"6E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-6E\" transform=\"translate(672,0)\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(4431.2,0)\"><use data-c=\"2061\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-2061\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(4597.9,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D703\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-I-1D703\"></use></g></g></g></svg>','[]','[]','[\"interference-proof-7b444759\",\"crystal-math-d2818099\",\"speed-color-link-b545d5aa\",\"surface-probe-9127b18d\"]'),
(2010246,'de-broglie-relation','de-broglie-hypothesis','The de Broglie Relation (\\(\\lambda = h/p\\))','<p>The <strong>de Broglie Relation</strong> is the fundamental mathematical link between the mechanical momentum of a particle and the wavelength of its associated <strong>Matter Wave</strong>. In university-level quantum mechanics, this relation (\\( \\lambda = h/p \\)) is the dual of Einstein\'s photon energy relation, asserting that the wavelength of any physical entity is inversely proportional to its momentum. It serves as the primary operator mapping between the spatial and momentum representations of the .</p>\n\n                    <h3>1. The Wavelength-Momentum Duality</h3>\n                    <p>Building on the symmetry of <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/electromagnetic-radiation\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Electromagnetic Radiation</strong></a>, Louis de Broglie postulated that if light waves behave as particles (photons), then particles should behave as waves.\n                    \\[ \\lambda = \\frac{h}{p} = \\frac{h}{mv} \\]\n                    This relation shows that the \"Wave Nature\" of an object is only detectable when the <strong>Planck Constant</strong> (\\( h \\)) is significant compared to the momentum. For heavy macroscopic objects, the wavelength is so small that the wave effects are completely masked by <strong>Classical Mechanics</strong>.</p>\n\n                    <h3>2. Momentum as a Wave Vector</h3>\n                    <p>In the language of <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/vector-calculus\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Vector Calculus</strong></a>, the de Broglie relation is more elegantly expressed in terms of the wave vector \\( \\mathbf{k} \\).\n                    \\[ \\mathbf{p} = \\hbar \\mathbf{k} \\]\n                    Where \\( \\hbar = h/2\\pi \\) and \\( |\\mathbf{k}| = 2\\pi/\\lambda \\). This form highlights that momentum is the spatial frequency of the <strong>Wave Function</strong>. It identifies the  of momentum space as the <strong>Fourier Transform</strong> of the coordinate space, a concept central to <strong>Theoretical Quantum Mechanics</strong>.</p>\n\n                    <h3>3. Experimental Confirmation via Electrons</h3>\n                    <p>The relation was first verified by the <strong>Davisson-Germer Experiment</strong>. By accelerating electrons through a potential \\( V \\), they acquired a momentum \\( p = \\sqrt{2meV} \\). The resulting diffraction peaks from a nickel crystal matched the de Broglie wavelength perfectly. This proof transformed the de Broglie relation from a speculative hypothesis into the rigorous foundation for the <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/schrodinger-equation\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Schrödinger Equation</strong></a> and all subsequent wave mechanics.</p>\n\n                    <h3>4. The Bohr Quantization Link</h3>\n                    <p>The de Broglie relation provided the first physical \"Reason\" for the quantized orbits in the Bohr model. By substituting \\( \\lambda = h/p \\) into the <strong>Standing Wave</strong> condition (\\( 2\\pi r = n\\lambda \\)), one recovers Bohr\'s angular momentum quantization: \\( L = n\\hbar \\). This proved that the stability of atoms is a geometric consequence of the de Broglie wavelength fitting perfectly into circular paths.</p>\n\n                    <h3>5. Relativistic Correction</h3>\n                    <p>For high-speed particles, the de Broglie relation must use the <strong>Relativistic Momentum</strong>: \\( p = \\gamma m v \\). As a particle approaches the <strong>Cosmic Speed Limit</strong> (\\( c \\)), its wavelength continues to shrink, even as its velocity levels off. This allows ultra-relativistic particles (like those in the LHC) to probe the subatomic 4D structure of <strong>Quarks</strong> and <strong>Leptons</strong> at incredibly small spatial scales.</p>\n\n                    <h3>6. Epistemic Status: What is waving?</h3>\n                    <p>The de Broglie relation raises the <strong>Measurement Problem</strong>: is the \"Matter Wave\" a physical oscillation of a medium, or a <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/probability-amplitude\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Probability Amplitude</strong></a>? The <strong>Born Interpretation</strong> identifies the wave as a tool for predicting the outcome of measurements. The de Broglie relation thus serves as the \"Translation Key\" that allows us to calculate the wave-like evolution of the universe while maintaining <strong>Physical Causality</strong> for individual particle detections.</p>','The de Broglie Relation is the fundamental mathematical link between the mechanical momentum of a particle and the wavelength of its associated Matter Wave. In university-level quantum mechanics, this relation is the dual of Einstein\'s photon energy relation, asserting that the wavelength of any physical entity is inversely proportional to its momentum. It serves as the primary operator mapping between the spatial and momentum representations of the.','The de Broglie Relation is the fundamental mathematical link between the mechanical momentum of a particle and the wavelength of its associated Matter Wave. In university-level quantum mechanics, this relation (<svg style=\"color: #FFD700; vertical-align: -0.566ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"7.908ex\" height=\"2.262ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -750 3495.6 1000\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><defs><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-I-1D706\" d=\"M166 673Q166 685 183 694H202Q292 691 316 644Q322 629 373 486T474 207T524 67Q531 47 537 34T546 15T551 6T555 2T556 -2T550 -11H482Q457 3 450 18T399 152L354 277L340 262Q327 246 293 207T236 141Q211 112 174 69Q123 9 111 -1T83 -12Q47 -12 47 20Q47 37 61 52T199 187Q229 216 266 252T321 306L338 322Q338 323 288 462T234 612Q214 657 183 657Q166 657 166 673Z\"></path><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-N-3D\" d=\"M56 347Q56 360 70 367H707Q722 359 722 347Q722 336 708 328L390 327H72Q56 332 56 347