 data-mml-node=\"msup\" transform=\"translate(1837.6,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D438\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-I-1D438\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(848.3,363) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg>).','<svg style=\"color: #FFD700; vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"6.99ex\" height=\"1.912ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -833.9 3089.4 844.9\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><defs><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-I-1D43C\" d=\"M43 1Q26 1 26 10Q26 12 29 24Q34 43 39 45Q42 46 54 46H60Q120 46 136 53Q137 53 138 54Q143 56 149 77T198 273Q210 318 216 344Q286 624 286 626Q284 630 284 631Q274 637 213 637H193Q184 643 189 662Q193 677 195 680T209 683H213Q285 681 359 681Q481 681 487 683H497Q504 676 504 672T501 655T494 639Q491 637 471 637Q440 637 407 634Q393 631 388 623Q381 609 337 432Q326 385 315 341Q245 65 245 59Q245 52 255 50T307 46H339Q345 38 345 37T342 19Q338 6 332 0H316Q279 2 179 2Q143 2 113 2T65 2T43 1Z\"></path><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-N-221D\" d=\"M56 124T56 216T107 375T238 442Q260 442 280 438T319 425T352 407T382 385T406 361T427 336T442 315T455 297T462 285L469 297Q555 442 679 442Q687 442 722 437V398H718Q710 400 694 400Q657 400 623 383T567 343T527 294T503 253T495 235Q495 231 520 192T554 143Q625 44 696 44Q717 44 719 46H722V-5Q695 -11 678 -11Q552 -11 457 141Q455 145 454 146L447 134Q362 -11 235 -11Q157 -11 107 56ZM93 213Q93 143 126 87T220 31Q258 31 292 48T349 88T389 137T413 178T421 196Q421 200 396 239T362 288Q322 345 288 366T213 387Q163 387 128 337T93 213Z\"></path><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-I-1D438\" d=\"M492 213Q472 213 472 226Q472 230 477 250T482 285Q482 316 461 323T364 330H312Q311 328 277 192T243 52Q243 48 254 48T334 46Q428 46 458 48T518 61Q567 77 599 117T670 248Q680 270 683 272Q690 274 698 274Q718 274 718 261Q613 7 608 2Q605 0 322 0H133Q31 0 31 11Q31 13 34 25Q38 41 42 43T65 46Q92 46 125 49Q139 52 144 61Q146 66 215 342T285 622Q285 629 281 629Q273 632 228 634H197Q191 640 191 642T193 659Q197 676 203 680H757Q764 676 764 669Q764 664 751 557T737 447Q735 440 717 440H705Q698 445 698 453L701 476Q704 500 704 528Q704 558 697 578T678 609T643 625T596 632T532 634H485Q397 633 392 631Q388 629 386 622Q385 619 355 499T324 377Q347 376 372 376H398Q464 376 489 391T534 472Q538 488 540 490T557 493Q562 493 565 493T570 492T572 491T574 487T577 483L544 351Q511 218 508 216Q505 213 492 213Z\"></path><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-N-32\" d=\"M109 429Q82 429 66 447T50 491Q50 562 103 614T235 666Q326 666 387 610T449 465Q449 422 429 383T381 315T301 241Q265 210 201 149L142 93L218 92Q375 92 385 97Q392 99 409 186V189H449V186Q448 183 436 95T421 3V0H50V19V31Q50 38 56 46T86 81Q115 113 136 137Q145 147 170 174T204 211T233 244T261 278T284 308T305 340T320 369T333 401T340 431T343 464Q343 527 309 573T212 619Q179 619 154 602T119 569T109 550Q109 549 114 549Q132 549 151 535T170 489Q170 464 154 447T109 429Z\"></path></defs><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D43C\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-I-1D43C\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(781.8,0)\"><use data-c=\"221D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-221D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"msup\" transform=\"translate(1837.6,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D438\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-I-1D438\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(848.3,363) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg>','[]','[]','[\"light-density-ecb50c0b\",\"intensity-energy-separation-6a3db801\",\"technical-relation-f1651f50\"]'),
(2010252,'threshold-frequency-photoelectric','photoelectric-effect','Frequency and the Threshold Limit','<p>The <strong>Threshold Frequency</strong> (\\( f_0 \\)) is the minimum frequency of incident light required to eject a single electron from a material. In university-level quantum mechanics, this limit proves that the 4D <strong>Photoelectric Effect</strong> is a energy-dependent process rather than a power-dependent one, directly validating Einstein\'s 4D <strong>Photon Hypothesis</strong>.</p>\n\n                <h3>1. The Cutoff Phenomenon</h3>\n                <p>Experimental data shows a sharp \"cutoff\" frequency for every material. Below this 4D <strong>Threshold</strong>, even the most intense light fails to produce a current. This was a 4D \"Hole\" in classical theory, which assumed that energy could be \"soaked up\" until emission occurred. The existence of \\( f_0 \\) proves that the 4D <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/total-dynamics\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Total Dynamics</strong></a> of the electron is governed by the energy of a <em>single</em> 4D <strong>Quantized Interaction</strong>.</p>\n\n                <h3>2. Determining the Work Function</h3>\n                <p>The threshold frequency is a direct measure of the <strong>Work Function</strong> (\\( \\Phi \\)) of the metal: \\( \\Phi = hf_0 \\). Different metals have different 4D atomic structures and thus different 4D binding energies. Measuring the x-intercept of a 4D <strong>Stopping Potential</strong> vs. frequency graph is the most precise way to determine these surface properties in 4D <strong>Solid State Physics</strong>.</p>\n\n                <h3>3. Blue-Shift and Kinetic Energy</h3>\n                <p>As the frequency of incident light increases (blue-shift), the energy of each photon increases linearly. This excess energy is converted into the <strong>Maximum Kinetic Energy</strong> of the photoelectron. This linear relationship is the cornerstone of the 4D <strong>Photoelectric Equation</strong>, providing a robust defense of 4D <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/scientific-realism\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Scientific Realism</strong></a> by showing a perfectly predictable response to the 4D frequency of the vacuum.</p>','The Threshold Frequency is the minimum frequency of incident light required to eject a single electron from a material. In university-level quantum mechanics, this limit proves that the 4D Photoelectric Effect is a energy-dependent process rather than a power-dependent one, directly validating Einstein\'s 4D Photon Hypothesis. Experimental data shows a sharp \"cutoff\" frequency for every material.','The Threshold Frequency (<svg style=\"color: #FFD700; vertical-align: -0.464ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"2.096ex\" height=\"2.059ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -705 926.6 910\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><defs><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-I-1D453\" d=\"M118 -162Q120 -162 124 -164T135 -167T147 -168Q160 -168 171 -155T187 -126Q197 -99 221 27T267 267T289 382V385H242Q195 385 192 387Q188 390 188 397L195 425Q197 430 203 430T250 431Q298 431 298 432Q298 434 307 482T319 540Q356 705 465 705Q502 703 526 683T550 630Q550 594 529 578T487 561Q443 561 443 603Q443 622 454 636T478 657L487 662Q471 668 457 668Q445 668 434 658T419 630Q412 601 403 552T387 469T380 433Q380 431 435 431Q480 431 487 430T498 424Q499 420 496 407T491 391Q489 386 482 386T428 385H372L349 263Q301 15 282 -47Q255 -132 212 -173Q175 -205 139 -205Q107 -205 81 -186T55 -132Q55 -95 76 -78T118 -61Q162 -61 162 -103Q162 -122 151 -136T127 -157L118 -162Z\"></path><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-N-30\" d=\"M96 585Q152 666 249 666Q297 666 345 640T423 548Q460 465 460 320Q460 165 417 83Q397 41 362 16T301 -15T250 -22Q224 -22 198 -16T137 16T82 83Q39 165 39 320Q39 494 96 585ZM321 597Q291 629 250 629Q208 629 178 597Q153 571 145 525T137 333Q137 175 145 125T181 46Q209 16 250 16Q290 16 318 46Q347 76 354 130T362 333Q362 478 354 524T321 597Z\"></path></defs><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D453\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-I-1D453\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(523,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"30\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-30\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg>) is the minimum frequency of incident light required to eject a single electron from a material. In university-level quantum mechanics, this limit proves that the 4D Photoelectric Effect is a energy-dependent process rather than a power-dependent one, directly validating Einstein\'s 4D Photon Hypothesis. Experimental data shows a sharp \"cutoff\" frequency for every material.','<svg style=\"color: #FFD700; vertical-align: -0.464ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"2.096ex\" height=\"2.059ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -705 926.6 910\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><defs><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-I-1D453\" d=\"M118 -162Q120 -162 124 -164T135 -167T147 -168Q160 -168 171 -155T187 -126Q197 -99 221 27T267 267T289 382V385H242Q195 385 192 387Q188 390 188 397L195 425Q197 430 203 430T250 431Q298 431 298 432Q298 434 307 482T319 540Q356 705 465 705Q502 703 526 683T550 630Q550 594 529 578T487 561Q443 561 443 603Q443 622 454 636T478 657L487 662Q471 668 457 668Q445 668 434 658T419 630Q412 601 403 552T387 469T380 433Q380 431 435 431Q480 431 487 430T498 424Q499 420 496 407T491 391Q489 386 482 386T428 385H372L349 263Q301 15 282 -47Q255 -132 212 -173Q175 -205 139 -205Q107 -205 81 -186T55 -132Q55 -95 76 -78T118 -61Q162 -61 162 -103Q162 -122 151 -136T127 -157L118 -162Z\"></path><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-N-30\" d=\"M96 585Q152 666 249 666Q297 666 345 640T423 548Q460 465 460 320Q460 165 417 83Q397 41 362 16T301 -15T250 -22Q224 -22 198 -16T137 16T82 83Q39 165 39 320Q39 494 96 585ZM321 597Q291 629 250 629Q208 629 178 597Q153 571 145 525T137 333Q137 175 145 125T181 46Q209 16 250 16Q290 16 318 46Q347 76 354 130T362 333Q362 478 354 524T321 597Z\"></path></defs><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D453\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-I-1D453\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(523,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"30\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-30\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg>','[]','[]','[\"threshold-frequency-276709a4\",\"material-specificity-52f933f5\",\"universal-constant-685e36dd\"]'),
(2010253,'work-function-photoelectric','photoelectric-effect','The Work Function (\\( \\Phi \\))','<p>The <strong>Work Function</strong> (\\( \\Phi \\)) is the minimum energy required to remove an electron from the surface of a solid. In university-level physics, this defined as the difference between the <strong>Fermi Level</strong> of the metal and the 4D <strong>Vacuum Level</strong>. It represents the \"Potential Barrier\" that an electron must overcome during a 4D <strong>Photoelectric</strong> interaction.</p>\n\n                <h3>1. Atomic Binding Energy</h3>\n                <p>Electrons in a metal are bound by the 4D electromagnetic attraction of the positive nuclei. In the 4D <strong>Sommerfeld Model</strong> of metals, electrons occupy a \"Potential Well.\" The work function is the \"depth\" of the well relative to the surface. It is a 4D structural property influenced by the crystal lattice and the 4D <strong>Surface Dipole</strong> layer of the material.</p>\n\n                <h3>2. Temperature and the Work Function</h3>\n                <p>While the work function is often treated as a constant, it is technically temperature-dependent. As a metal heats up, the distribution of electron energies (the <strong>Fermi-Dirac Distribution</strong>) changes, allowing some electrons to escape with less additional energy (<strong>Thermionic Emission</strong>). However, for standard photoelectric experiments, the 4D <strong>Work Function</strong> is the dominant 4D <strong>Ontological Commitment</strong> defining the threshold.</p>\n\n                <h3>3. Surface Contamination and Engineering</h3>\n                <p>The work function is highly sensitive to surface conditions. A single layer of oxide or contaminant can radically shift the 4D <strong>Threshold Frequency</strong>. In modern technology, the work function is \"engineered\" by coating surfaces with materials like Cesium to lower the barrier, which is essential for the 4D <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/total-dynamics\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Total Dynamics</strong></a> of 4D <strong>Photomultiplier Tubes</strong> and night-vision devices.</p>','The Work Function is the minimum energy required to remove an electron from the surface of a solid. In university-level physics, this defined as the difference between the Fermi Level of the metal and the 4D Vacuum Level. It represents the \"Potential Barrier\" that an electron must overcome during a 4D Photoelectric interaction.','The Work Function (<svg style=\"color: #FFD700; vertical-align: 0;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.633ex\" height=\"1.545ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -683 722 683\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><defs><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-N-3A6\" d=\"M312 622Q310 623 307 625T303 629T297 631T286 634T270 635T246 636T211 637H184V683H196Q220 680 361 680T526 683H538V637H511Q468 637 447 635T422 631T411 622V533L425 531Q525 519 595 466T665 342Q665 301 642 267T583 209T506 172T425 152L411 150V61Q417 55 421 53T447 48T511 46H538V0H526Q502 3 361 3T196 0H184V46H211Q231 46 245 46T270 47T286 48T297 51T303 54T307 57T312 61V150H310Q309 151 289 153T232 166T160 195Q149 201 136 210T103 238T69 284T56 342Q56 414 128 467T294 530Q309 532 310 533H312V622ZM170 342Q170 207 307 188H312V495H309Q301 495 282 491T231 469T186 423Q170 389 170 342ZM415 188Q487 199 519 236T551 342Q551 384 539 414T507 459T470 481T434 491T415 495H410V188H415Z\"></path></defs><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"3A6\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-3A6\"></use></g></g></g></svg>) is the minimum energy required to remove an electron from the surface of a solid. In university-level physics, this defined as the difference between the Fermi Level of the metal and the 4D Vacuum Level. It represents the \"Potential Barrier\" that an electron must overcome during a 4D Photoelectric interaction.','<svg style=\"color: #FFD700; vertical-align: 0;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.633ex\" height=\"1.545ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -683 722 683\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><defs><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-N-3A6\" d=\"M312 622Q310 623 307 625T303 629T297 631T286 634T270 635T246 636T211 637H184V683H196Q220 680 361 680T526 683H538V637H511Q468 637 447 635T422 631T411 622V533L425 531Q525 519 595 466T665 342Q665 301 642 267T583 209T506 172T425 152L411 150V61Q417 55 421 53T447 48T511 46H538V0H526Q502 3 361 3T196 0H184V46H211Q231 46 245 46T270 47T286 48T297 51T303 54T307 57T312 61V150H310Q309 151 289 153T232 166T160 195Q149 201 136 210T103 238T69 284T56 342Q56 414 128 467T294 530Q309 532 310 533H312V622ZM170 342Q170 207 307 188H312V495H309Q301 495 282 491T231 469T186 423Q170 389 170 342ZM415 188Q487 199 519 236T551 342Q551 384 539 414T507 459T470 481T434 491T415 495H410V188H415Z\"></path></defs><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"3A6\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-3A6\"></use></g></g></g></svg>','[]','[]','[\"energy-barrier-ffd47868\",\"conservation-law-907a412f\",\"technical-relation-01fbbf48\"]'),
(2010254,'quantized-interaction-quantum','photoelectric-effect','Quantized Interaction: The One-to-One Exchange','<p>The 4D <strong>Quantized Interaction</strong> is the fundamental mechanism of <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/photoelectric-effect\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>the photoelectric effect</strong></a>, where a single photon transfers its entire 4D <strong>Energy Packet</strong> to a single electron. This \"All-or-Nothing\" exchange is the university-level proof that light-matter interactions are discrete rather than continuous, providing the 4D <strong>Logical Basis</strong> for the 4D <strong>Photon Model</strong>.</p>\n\n                <h3>1. The Collision Model</h3>\n                <p>In this view, <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/photoelectric-effect\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>the photoelectric effect</strong></a> is modeled as a 4D <strong>Point-Like Collision</strong> between a photon and a bound electron. There is no sharing of energy between multiple electrons, and no partial absorption of photons. This 4D <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/spacetime-causal-topology\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Causal Topology</strong></a> explains why there is zero 4D \"Time Lag\" even at very low light intensities: as soon as the first photon arrives, an electron can be ejected instantly.</p>\n\n                <h3>2. Cross-Section and Probability</h3>\n                <p>While the interaction is quantized, it is also <strong>Probabilistic</strong>. The 4D <strong>Photoelectric Cross-Section</strong> determines the likelihood that a photon will actually strike an electron. This probability depends on the photon\'s energy and the 4D <strong>Wave Function</strong> of the electron. This shifts <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/scientific-realism\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Scientific Realism</strong></a> from a deterministic billiard-ball model to a 4D <strong>Quantized Probability</strong> field.</p>\n\n                <h3>3. <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/total-mechanical-energy\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Conservation of Energy</strong></a> and Momentum</h3>\n                <p>The interaction must obey the 4D <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/total-dynamics\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Total Dynamics</strong></a> of conservation laws. However, a \"Free\" electron cannot absorb a photon and conserve both energy and momentum simultaneously; it needs the 4D <strong>Recoil</strong> of the atomic nucleus to balance the equations. This why the 4D <strong>Photoelectric Effect</strong> only happens in bound systems (like metals) and not in a 4D <strong>Pure Vacuum</strong>, anchoring the effect in 4D <strong>Solid State Ontology</strong>.</p>','The 4D Quantized Interaction is the fundamental mechanism of the photoelectric effect, where a single photon transfers its entire 4D Energy Packet to a single electron. This \"All-or-Nothing\" exchange is the university-level proof that light-matter interactions are discrete rather than continuous, providing the 4D Logical Basis for the 4D Photon Model. In this view, the photoelectric effect is modeled as a 4D Point-Like Collision between a photon and a bound electron.','The 4D Quantized Interaction is the fundamental mechanism of the photoelectric effect, where a single photon transfers its entire 4D Energy Packet to a single electron. This \"All-or-Nothing\" exchange is the university-level proof that light-matter interactions are discrete rather than continuous, providing the 4D Logical Basis for the 4D Photon Model. In this view, the photoelectric effect is modeled as a 4D Point-Like Collision between a photon and a bound electron.','','[]','[]','[\"zero-lag-255271e7\",\"discrete-exchange-0e48111c\",\"technical-relation-f9fe12f5\"]'),
(2010255,'photoelectric-equation-einstein','photoelectric-effect','Einstein\'s Photoelectric Equation','<p>Einstein\'s Photoelectric Equation (1905) is the mathematical expression of the conservation of energy in a 4D <strong>Quantized Interaction</strong>. It was for this specific derivation, rather than relativity, that Einstein was awarded the Nobel Prize, as it provided the first 4D <strong>Theoretical Physics</strong> bridge between the 4D <strong>Work Function</strong> and the 4D <strong>Quantum of Light</strong>.</p>\n\n                <h3>1. Mathematical Form</h3>\n                <p>The equation is a simple statement of 4D energy bookkeeping: \\( hf = \\Phi + K_{max} \\). The energy of the incoming photon (\\( hf \\)) is equal to the energy used to escape the metal (the 4D <strong>Work Function</strong> \\( \\Phi \\)) plus the leftover 4D <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/kinetic-energy\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Kinetic Energy</strong></a> of the electron. This proves that the 4D <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/total-dynamics\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Total Dynamics</strong></a> of the vacuum is governed by discrete 4D <strong>Planckian</strong> units.</p>\n\n                <h3>2. Linear Correlation</h3>\n                <p>The equation predicts a <strong>Linear Relationship</strong> between the frequency of light and the maximum kinetic energy of photoelectrons. Before 1905, such a relationship was unthinkable in 4D <strong>Classical Electrodynamics</strong>. The slope of this line is exactly <strong>Planck\'s Constant</strong> (\\( h \\)), a universal constant that appears in everything from 4D <strong>Blackbody Radiation</strong> to 4D <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/quantum-gravity\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Quantum Gravity</strong></a>, anchoring 4D <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/scientific-realism\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Scientific Realism</strong></a> in a single number.</p>\n\n                <h3>3. Predictive Power</h3>\n                <p>Einstein\'s equation allows for the calculation of the <strong>Stopping Potential</strong> (\\( V_s \\)) required to halt the current. It predicts that if you double the frequency, you don\'t double the energy; you increase it by exactly \\( h \\Delta f \\). This precision allowed 4D <strong>Robert Millikan</strong> to verify theory with 4D 1% accuracy, turning a 4D <strong>Heuristic Hypothesis</strong> into a foundational 4D <strong>Physical Law</strong>.</p>','Einstein\'s Photoelectric Equation (1905) is the mathematical expression of the conservation of energy in a 4D Quantized Interaction. It was for this specific derivation, rather than relativity, that Einstein was awarded the Nobel Prize, as it provided the first 4D Theoretical Physics bridge between the 4D Work Function and the 4D Quantum of Light. The equation is a simple statement of 4D energy bookkeeping:.','Einstein\'s Photoelectric Equation (1905) is the mathematical expression of the conservation of energy in a 4D Quantized Interaction. It was for this specific derivation, rather than relativity, that Einstein was awarded the Nobel Prize, as it provided the first 4D Theoretical Physics bridge between the 4D Work Function and the 4D Quantum of Light. The equation is a simple statement of 4D energy bookkeeping: <svg style=\"color: #FFD700; vertical-align: -0.464ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"15.238ex\" height=\"2.059ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -705 6735.4 910\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><defs><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-I-210E\" d=\"M137 683Q138 683 209 688T282 694Q294 694 294 685Q294 674 258 534Q220 386 220 383Q220 381 227 388Q288 442 357 442Q411 442 444 415T478 336Q478 285 440 178T402 50Q403 36 407 31T422 26Q450 26 474 56T513 138Q516 149 519 151T535 153Q555 153 555 145Q555 144 551 130Q535 71 500 33Q466 -10 419 -10H414Q367 -10 346 17T325 74Q325 90 361 192T398 345Q398 404 354 404H349Q266 404 205 306L198 293L164 158Q132 28 127 16Q114 -11 83 -1