roke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msubsup\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D445\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-I-1D445\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(792,506.3) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"1D70C\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-I-1D70C\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" transform=\"translate(792,-138.9) scale(0.707)\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D70E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-I-1D70E\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(571,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D707\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-I-1D707\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(1174,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D708\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-I-1D708\"></use></g></g></g></g></g></svg>) is the fundamental mathematical object that completely describes the Curvature of Spacetime. In university-level General Relativity, it is a 4th-rank tensor that quantifies the non-commutativity of Covariant Divergence. It contains all the information about the local geometry of the , from Tidal Forces to the 10 components of the Einstein Tensor.','<svg style=\"color: #FFD700; vertical-align: -0.66ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"4.631ex\" height=\"2.513ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -818.9 2046.9 1110.6\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><defs><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-I-1D445\" d=\"M230 637Q203 637 198 638T193 649Q193 676 204 682Q206 683 378 683Q550 682 564 680Q620 672 658 652T712 606T733 563T739 529Q739 484 710 445T643 385T576 351T538 338L545 333Q612 295 612 223Q612 212 607 162T602 80V71Q602 53 603 43T614 25T640 16Q668 16 686 38T712 85Q717 99 720 102T735 105Q755 105 755 93Q755 75 731 36Q693 -21 641 -21H632Q571 -21 531 4T487 82Q487 109 502 166T517 239Q517 290 474 313Q459 320 449 321T378 323H309L277 193Q244 61 244 59Q244 55 245 54T252 50T269 48T302 46H333Q339 38 339 37T336 19Q332 6 326 0H311Q275 2 180 2Q1