href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-I-1D706\"></use></g></g><rect width=\"1749.8\" height=\"60\" x=\"120\" y=\"220\"></rect></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(0,201.3)\"><use data-c=\"221A\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-S3-221A\"></use></g><rect width=\"6170.3\" height=\"60\" x=\"1020\" y=\"1591.3\"></rect></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(11024.9,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D451\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-I-1D451\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(11544.9,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D706\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-I-1D706\"></use></g></g></g></svg>','[]','[]','[\"total-aging-3e17bf27\",\"dynamic-foundation-f036926d\"]'),
(2010365,'four-velocity-definition','proper-time','Definition of Four-Velocity','<p>In relativity, the standard 3-velocity (\\(\\mathbf{v} = d\\mathbf{x}/dt\\)) is not a Lorentz-covariant quantity because it involves the frame-dependent coordinate time. To resolve this, we define the <strong>Four-Velocity</strong>, a vector in 4D spacetime that transforms correctly under Lorentz transformations.</p>\n\n                <h3>1. <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/vector-definition\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Vector Definition</strong></a> in Spacetime</h3>\n                <p>The Four-Velocity (\\(U^\\mu\\)) is defined as the derivative of the spacetime position 4-vector with respect to <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/proper-time\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Proper Time</strong></a> (\\(\\tau\\)):\n                \\[U^\\mu = \\frac{dx^\\mu}{d\\tau}\\]\n                Since \\(dx^\\mu\\) is a 4-vector and \\(d\\tau\\) is an invariant scalar, \\(U^\\mu\\) is a true 4-vector (specifically, it is the unit tangent vector to the world-line).</p>\n\n                <h3>2. Components and the Lorentz Factor</h3>\n                <p>In a specific inertial frame, the components of the four-velocity are related to the ordinary velocity \\(\\mathbf{v}\\) by the Lorentz factor \\(\\gamma\\):\n                \\[U^\\mu = (\\gamma c, \\gamma \\mathbf{v})\\]\n                The temporal component \\(U^0 = \\gamma c\\) represents the rate at which coordinate time passes relative to proper time, while the spatial components \\(U^i\\) represent the spatial displacement per unit proper time.</p>\n\n                <h3>3. The <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/normalization-physics\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Normalization</strong></a> Constraint</h3>\n                <p>A fundamental property of the four-velocity for any massive particle is that its magnitude is always constant. In a Minkowski metric with signature (\\(-,+,+,+\\)):\n                \\[g_{\\mu\\nu} U^\\mu U^\\nu = -c^2\\]\n                This normalization constraint implies that all objects move through 4D spacetime at a \"speed\" equal to the speed of light. An object at rest in a coordinate frame is still \"moving\" through the time dimension at speed \\(c\\).</p>','In relativity, the standard 3-velocity is not a Lorentz-covariant quantity because it involves the frame-dependent coordinate time. To resolve this, we define the Four-Velocity, a vector in 4D spacetime that transforms correctly under Lorentz transformations. The Four-Velocity is defined as the derivative of the spacetime position 4-vector with respect to Proper Time : Since is a 4-vector and is an invariant scalar, is a true 4-vector (specifically, it is the unit tangent vector to the world-line).','In relativity, the standard 3-velocity (<svg style=\"color: #FFD700; vertical-align: -0.566ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"10.065ex\" height=\"2.262ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -750 4448.6 1000\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><defs><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-B-1D42F\" d=\"M401 444Q413 441 495 441Q568 441 574 444H580V382H510L409 156Q348 18 339 6Q331 -4 320 -4Q318 -4 313 -4T303 -3H288Q273 -3 264 12T221 102Q206 135 197 156L96 382H26V444H34Q49 441 145 441Q252 441 270 444H279V382H231L284 264Q335 149 338 149Q338 150 389 264T442 381Q442 382 418 382H394V444H401Z\"></path><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-N-3D\" d=\"M56 347Q56 360 70 367H707Q722 359 722 347Q722 336 708 328L390 327H72Q56 332 56 347ZM56 153Q56 168 72 173H708Q722 163 722 153Q722 140 707 133H70Q56 140 56 153Z\"></path><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-I-1D451\" d=\"M366 683Q367 683 438 688T511 694Q523 694 523 686Q523 679 450 384T375 83T374 68Q374 26 402 26Q411 27 422 35Q443 55 463 131Q469 151 473 152Q475 153 483 153H487H491Q506 153 506 145Q506 140 503 129Q490 79 473 48T445 8T417 -8Q409 -10 393 -10Q359 -10 336 5T306 36L300 51Q299 52 296 50Q294 48 292 46Q233 -10 172 -10Q117 -10 75 30T33 157Q33 205 53 255T101 341Q148 398 195 420T280 442Q336 442 364