 stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msup\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D465\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-I-1D465\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(605,363) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"2032\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-V-2032\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1127.2,0)\"><use data-c=\"3D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-3D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(2183,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D465\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-I-1D465\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(2977.2,0)\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(3977.5,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D463\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-I-1D463\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(4462.5,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D461\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-I-1D461\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(4823.5,0)\"><use data-c=\"2C\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-2C\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"msup\" transform=\"translate(5268.1,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D461\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-I-1D461\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(394,363) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"2032\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-V-2032\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(6184.4,0)\"><use data-c=\"3D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-3D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(7240.1,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D461\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-I-1D461\"></use></g></g></g></svg>','[]','[]','[\"coordinate-transformation-89fecb34\",\"covariant-maxwell-equation-f1d6ea22\",\"a-href-physics-subtopic-homogeneous-maxwell-class-subtopic-link-homogeneous-maxwell-a-68cba42c\"]'),
(2010375,'constancy-of-light-speed','relativity','The Constancy of Light Speed (\\( c \\))','<p>The second postulate of Special Relativity states that the speed of light in a vacuum (\\(c\\)) is a universal constant, independent of the motion of the source or the observer. This postulate is the \"keystone\" that bridges the gap between Maxwell\'s electrodynamics and the geometry of spacetime.</p>\n\n                    <h3>1. The Universal Speed Limit and Causality</h3>\n                    <p>The constant \\(c\\) (exactly \\(299,792,458\\) m/s) is not just the speed of photons; it is the fundamental speed at which information and causality propagate through the universe. This establishes a <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/cosmic-speed-limit\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Cosmic Speed Limit</strong></a>: because the energy required to accelerate a massive object to \\(c\\) is infinite, no causal influence can ever travel faster than light, ensuring the chronological consistency of events.</p>\n\n                    <h3>2. The Light Cone and Spacetime Topology</h3>\n                    <p>The constancy of \\(c\\) defines the causal structure of the universe, visualized through the <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/light-cone\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Light Cone</strong></a>. For any event in spacetime, the light cone divides all other events into three distinct regions: the \"Past\" (events that could have influenced the present), the \"Future\" (events the present can influence), and \"Elsewhere\" (events that are causally disconnected). This topology is invariant for all observers, providing a rigid framework for an otherwise relative universe.</p>\n\n                    <h3>3. The Foundation of the Metric</h3>\n                    <p>Because \\(c\\) is constant, it acts as a conversion factor between space and time. In the Minkowski metric (\\(ds^2 = c^2dt^2 - dx^2\\)), the term \\(c\\) ensures that space and time have the same units, allowing them to be treated as components of a single 4D geometry. If light speed were not constant, the very notion of a \"spacetime interval\" would collapse, returning us to a world of disjointed space and absolute time.</p>','The second postulate of Special Relativity states that the speed of light in a vacuum is a universal constant, independent of the motion of the source or the observer. This postulate is the \"keystone\" that bridges the gap between Maxwell\'s electrodynamics and the geometry of spacetime. The constant (exactly m/s) is not just the speed of photons; it is the fundamental speed at which information and causality propagate through the universe.','The second postulate of Special Relativity states that the speed of light in a vacuum (<svg style=\"color: #FFD700; vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"0.98ex\" height=\"1.025ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -442 433 453\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><defs><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-I-1D450\" d=\"M34 159Q34 268 120 355T306 442Q362 442 394 418T427 355Q427 326 408 306T360 285Q341 285 330 295T319 325T330 359T352 380T366 386H367Q367 388 361 392T340 400T306 404Q276 404 249 390Q228 381 206 359Q162 315 142 235T121 119Q121 73 147 50Q169 26 205 26H209Q321 26 394 111Q403 121 406 121Q410 121 419 112T429 98T420 83T391 55T346 25T282 0T202 -11Q127 -11 81 37T34 159Z\"></path></defs><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D450\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-I-1D450\"></use></g></g></g></svg>) is a universal constant, independent of the motion of the source or the observer. This postulate is the \"keystone\" that bridges the gap between Maxwell\'s electrodynamics and the geometry of spacetime. The constant <svg style=\"color: #FFD700; vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"0.98ex\" height=\"1.025ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" view