e data-c=\"1D6FD\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-I-1D6FD\"></use></g></g></g></svg>) is an extremely rare, hypothetical nuclear decay process in which two neutrons in a nucleus simultaneously transform into two protons and two electrons, without the emission of any neutrinos. In university-level physics, the observation of this decay would be a discovery of monumental importance: it would prove that neutrinos are Majorana Fermions and that Lepton Number is not a conserved quantity in nature. Ordinary double beta decay (<svg style=\"color: #FFD700; vertical-align: -0.439ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"4.891ex\" height=\"2.034ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -705 2162 899\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><defs><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-N-32\" d=\"M109 429Q82 429 66 447T50 491Q50 562 103 614T235 666Q326 666 387 610T449 465Q449 422 429 383T381 315T301 241Q265 210 201 149L142 93L218 92Q375 92 385 97Q392 99 409 186V189H449V186Q448 183 436 95T421 3V0H50V19V31Q50 38 56 46T86 81Q115 113 136 137Q145 147 170 174T204 211T233 244T261 278T284 308T305 340T320 369T333 401T340 431T343 464Q343 527 309 573T212 619Q179 619 154 602T119 569T109 550Q109 549 114 549Q132 549 151 535T170 489Q170 464 154 447T109 429Z\"></path><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-I-1D708\" d=\"M74 431Q75 431 146 436T219 442Q231 442 231 434Q231 428 185 241L137 51H140L150 55Q161 59 177 67T214 86T261 119T312 165Q410 264 445 394Q458 442 496 442Q509 442 519 434T530 411Q530 390 516 352T469 262T388 162T267 70T106 5Q81 -2 71 -2Q66 -2 59 -1T51 1Q45 5 45 11Q45 13 88 188L132 364Q133 377 125 380T86 385H65Q59 391 59 393T61 412Q65 431 74 431Z\"></path><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-I-1D6FD\" d=\"M29 -194Q23 -188 23 -186Q23 -183 102 134T186 465Q208 533 243 584T309 658Q365 705 429 705H431Q493 705 533 667T573 570Q573 465 469 396L482 383Q533 332 533 252Q533 139 448 65T257 -10Q227 -10 203 -2T165 17T143 40T131 59T126 65L62 -188Q60 -194 42 -194H29ZM353 431Q392 431 427 419L432 422Q436 426 439 429T449 439T461 453T472 471T484 495T493 524T501 560Q503 569 503 593Q503 611 502 616Q487 667 426 667Q384 667 347 643T286 582T247 514T224 455Q219 439 186 308T152 168Q151 163 151 147Q151 99 173 68Q204 26 260 26Q302 26 349 51T425 137Q441 171 449 214T457 279Q457 337 422 372Q380 358 347 358H337Q258 358 258 389Q258 396 261 403Q275 431 353 431Z\"></path></defs><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-32\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(500,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D708\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-I-1D708\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(1030,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D6FD\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-I-1D6FD\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(1596,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D6FD\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-I-1D6FD\"></use></g></g></g></svg>) is a Standard Model process where two neutrinos are emitted to conserve lepton number.','<svg style=\"color: #FFD700; vertical-align: 0;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.199ex\" height=\"1ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -442 530 442\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><defs><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-I-1D708\" d=\"M74 431Q75 431 146 436T219 442Q231 442 231 434Q231 428 185 241L137 51H140L150 55Q161 59 177 67T214 86T261 119T312 165Q410 264 445 394Q458 442 496 442Q509 442 519 434T530 411Q530 390 516 352T469 262T388 162T267 70T106 5Q81 -2 71 -2Q66 -2 59 -1T51 1Q45 5 45 11Q45 13 88 188L132 364Q133 377 125 380T86 385H65Q59 391 59 393T61 412Q65 431 74 431Z\"></path></defs><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D708\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-I-1D708\"></use></g></g></g></svg>','[]','[]','[\"self-interaction-0e098478\",\"experimental-target-1b9dcf3f\",\"stability-measure-5751e166\",\"structural-map-71b9ec3b\"]'),
(2010406,'edm-physics','baryogenesis','Electric Dipole Moments (EDMs)','<p>An <strong>Electric Dipole Moment (EDM)</strong> of a fundamental particle is a permanent separation of positive and negative charge along the axis of the particle\'s spin. In university-level physics, a non-zero EDM for a particle like the electron or neutron would be a definitive signal of <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/c-and-cp-violation\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>C and CP Violation</strong></a>. Because the Standard Model predicts EDMs that are too small to be measured, detecting any EDM today would be a direct discovery of the <strong>\"New Physics\"</strong> that drove the process of <strong>Baryogenesis</strong>.</p>\n\n                    <h3>1. Symmetry and the EDM</h3>\n                    <p>For a particle to have a permanent EDM, both <strong>Parity (P)</strong> and <strong>Time-Reversal (T)</strong> symmetries must be violated. According to the <strong>CPT Theorem</strong>, T-violation is equivalent to <strong>CP Violation</strong>. Therefore, an EDM is a \"Static Record\" of the same subatomic asymmetries that caused matter to dominate over antimatter in the early universe. Measuring an EDM is equivalent to looking at the \"frozen\" reflection of the Big Bang\'s asymmetry.</p>\n\n                    <h3>2. Standard Model Predictions</h3>\n                    <p>In the Standard Model, EDMs only arise through complex loops involving the <strong>CKM Matrix</strong>. For the electron, the predicted EDM is \\( \\sim 10^{-38} \\text{ e}\\cdot\\text{cm} \\). This so small that it would require an instrument the size of the solar system to measure. Because of this \"Standard Model Background\" of nearly zero, EDM experiments are the cleanest <strong>Null Tests</strong> in physics; any signal is an immediate proof BSM (Beyond Standard Model) physics.</p>\n\n                    <h3>3. The Neutron EDM and the Strong CP Problem</h3>\n                    <p>The <strong>Neutron EDM</strong> (\\( d_n \\)) is particularly significant. While the weak force CP violation is small, the <strong>Strong Interaction</strong> (QCD) has a term (the \\( \\theta \\)-angle) that could produce a large EDM. The fact that \\( d_n \\lt 10^{-26} \\text{ e}\\cdot\\text{cm} \\) implies that \\( \\theta \\) is almost exactly zero. This \"Fine-Tuning\" mystery is the <strong>Strong CP Problem</strong>, leading to the prediction of the <strong>Axion</strong> as a restorative symmetry particle.</p>\n\n                    <h3>4. Electron EDM and Supersymmetry</h3>\n                    <p>The <strong>Electron EDM</strong> (\\( d_e \\)) is a primary target for <strong>Supersymmetry (SUSY)</strong> searches. Many SUSY models predict an electron EDM near \\( 10^{-28} - 10^{-30} \\text{ e}\\cdot\\text{cm} \\), just below current experimental limits. Experiments like <strong>ACME</strong> use polar molecules to create intense internal electric fields, allowing them to measure the subatomic \"wobble\" of electrons with enough precision to rule out many popular versions of SUSY.</p>\n\n                    <h3>5. Link to the Sakharov Conditions</h3>\n                    <p>To generate the observed <strong>Baryon-to-Photon Ratio</strong>, the early universe required a source of CP violation roughly a billion times stronger than what is in the CKM matrix. This \"Strong CP Violation\" would naturally leave a signature in the form of particle EDMs. The search for EDMs is thus a direct probe of the <strong>Theoretical Requirements</strong> of baryogenesis, searching for the \"extra kick\" that saved matter from annihilation.</p>\n\n                    <h3>6. Experimental Techniques: Spin Precession</h3>\n                    <p>EDMs are measured by placing particles intense <strong>Electric and Magnetic Fields</strong> and observing their <strong>Spin Precession</strong>. If an EDM exists, the precession frequency will shift slightly when the electric field is reversed. This measurement requires extreme control over magnetic shielding and geometric phases, making EDM physics the pinnacle of <strong>Precision Measurement</strong> and a vital companion to high-energy collider physics at the <strong>LHC</strong>.</p>','An Electric Dipole Moment (EDM) of a fundamental particle is a permanent separation of positive and negative charge along the axis of the particle\'s spin. In university-level physics, a non-zero EDM for a particle like the electron or neutron would be a definitive signal of C and CP Violation. Because the Standard Model predicts EDMs that are too small to be measured, detecting any EDM today would be a direct discovery of the \"New Physics\" that drove the process of Baryogenesis.','An Electric Dipole Moment (EDM) of a fundamental particle is a permanent separation of positive and negative charge along the axis of the particle\'s spin. In university-level physics, a non-zero EDM for a particle like the electron or neutron would be a definitive signal of C and CP Violation. Because the Standard Model predicts EDMs that are too small to be measured, detecting any EDM today would be a direct discovery of the \"New Physics\" that drove the process of Baryogenesis.','<svg style=\"color: #FFD700; vertical-align: -0.05ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"13.777ex\" height=\"2.005ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -864 6089.5 886\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><defs><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-N-223C\" d=\"M55 166Q55 241 101 304T222 367Q260 367 296 349T362 304T421 252T484 208T554 189Q616 189 655 236T694 338Q694 350 698 358T708 367Q722 367 722 334Q722 260 677 197T562 134H554Q517 134 481 152T414 196T355 248T292 293T223 311Q179 311 145 286Q109 257 96 218T80 156T69 133Q55 133 55 166Z\"></path><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-N-31\" d=\"M213 578L200 573Q186 568 160 563T102 556H83V602H102Q149 604 189 617T245 641T273 663Q275 666 285 666Q294 666 302 660V361L303 61Q310 54 315 52T339 48T401 46H427V0H416Q395 3 257 3Q121 3 100 0H88V46H114Q136 46 152 46T177 47T193 50T201 52T207 57T213 61V578Z\"></path><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-N-30\" d=\"M96 585Q152 666 249 666Q297 666 345 640T423 548Q460 465 460 320Q460 165 417 83Q397 41 362 16T301 -15T250 -22Q224 -22 198 -16T137 16T82 83Q39 165 39 320Q39 494 96 585ZM321 597Q291 629 250 629Q208 629 178 597Q153 571 145 525T137 333Q137 175 145 125T181 46Q209 16 250 16Q290 16 318 46Q347 76 354 130T362 333Q362 478 354 524T321 597Z\"></path><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-N-2212\" d=\"M84 237T84 250T98 270H679Q694 262 694 250T679 230H98Q84 237 84 250Z\"></path><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-N-33\" d=\"M127 463Q100 463 85 480T69 524Q69 579 117 622T233 665Q268 665 277 664Q351 652 390 611T430 522Q430 470 396 421T302 350L299 348Q299 347 308 345T337 336T375 315Q457 262 457 175Q457 96 395 37T238 -22Q158 -22 100 21T42 130Q42 158 60 175T105 193Q133 193 151 175T169 130Q169 119 166 110T159 94T148 82T136 74T126 70T118 67L114 66Q165 21 238 21Q293 21 321 74Q338 107 338 175V195Q338 290 274 322Q259 328 213 329L171 330L168 332Q166 335 166 348Q166 366 174 366Q202 366 232 371Q266 376 294 413T322 525V533Q322 590 287 612Q265 626 240 626Q208 626 181 615T143 592T132 580H135Q138 579 143 578T153 573T165 566T175 555T183 540T186 520Q186 498 172 481T127 463Z\"></path><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-N-38\" d=\"M70 417T70 494T124 618T248 666Q319 666 374 624T429 515Q429 485 418 459T392 417T361 389T335 371T324 363L338 354Q352 344 366 334T382 323Q457 264 457 174Q457 95 399 37T249 -22Q159 -22 101 29T43 155Q43 263 172 335L154 348Q133 361 127 368Q70 417 70 494ZM286 386L292 390Q298 394 301 396T311 403T323 413T334 425T345 438T355 454T364 471T369 491T371 513Q371 556 342 586T275 624Q268 625 242 625Q201 625 165 599T128 534Q128 511 141 492T167 463T217 431Q224 426 228 424L286 386ZM250 21Q308 21 350 55T392 137Q392 154 387 169T375 194T353 216T330 234T301 253T274 270Q260 279 244 289T218 306L210 311Q204 311 181 294T133 239T107 157Q107 98 150 60T250 21Z\"></path><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-N-A0\" d=\"\"></path><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-N-65\" d=\"M28 218Q28 2