mi\"><use data-c=\"1D44A\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-I-1D44A\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1136.2,363) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"B1\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-B1\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg> and <svg style=\"color: #FFD700; vertical-align: 0;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"2.741ex\" height=\"1.887ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -833.9 1211.6 833.9\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><defs><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-I-1D44D\" d=\"M58 8Q58 23 64 35Q64 36 329 334T596 635L586 637Q575 637 512 637H500H476Q442 637 420 635T365 624T311 598T266 548T228 469Q227 466 226 463T224 458T223 453T222 450L221 448Q218 443 202 443Q185 443 182 453L214 561Q228 606 241 651Q249 679 253 681Q256 683 487 683H718Q723 678 723 675Q723 673 717 649Q189 54 188 52L185 49H274Q369 50 377 51Q452 60 500 100T579 247Q587 272 590 277T603 282H607Q628 282 628 271Q547 5 541 2Q538 0 300 0H124Q58 0 58 8Z\"></path><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-N-30\" d=\"M96 585Q152 666 249 666Q297 666 345 640T423 548Q460 465 460 320Q460 165 417 83Q397 41 362 16T301 -15T250 -22Q224 -22 198 -16T137 16T82 83Q39 165 39 320Q39 494 96 585ZM321 597Q291 629 250 629Q208 629 178 597Q153 571 145 525T137 333Q137 175 145 125T181 46Q209 16 250 16Q290 16 318 46Q347 76 354 130T362 333Q362 478 354 524T321 597Z\"></path></defs><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msup\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D44D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-I-1D44D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(808,363) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"30\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-30\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg> bosons \"eat\" three of the four degrees of freedom of the Complex Scalar Doublet Higgs field, turning an Infinite Range force into a subatomic one. In the symmetric state, the electroweak Lagrangian Density contains 4 massless Gauge Bosons (<svg style=\"color: #FFD700; vertical-align: 