te(684,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"1D43F\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-I-1D43F\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(7628.8,0)\"><use data-c=\"3A6\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-3A6\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"msub\" transform=\"translate(8350.8,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D713\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-I-1D713\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(684,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"1D445\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-I-1D445\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(9843.7,0)\"><use data-c=\"2B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-2B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(10843.9,0)\"><use data-c=\"210E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-I-210E\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(11419.9,0)\"><use data-c=\"2E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-2E\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(11864.6,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D450\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-I-1D450\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(12297.6,0)\"><use data-c=\"2E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-2E\"></use></g></g></g></svg>','[]','[]','[\"a-href-physics-subtopic-fermion-mass-origin-class-subtopic-link-fermion-mass-origin-a-1aba5583\",\"the-flavor-mystery-4d76416f\",\"handedness-link-37d42f64\",\"the-y-number-e022cb94\"]'),
(2010454,'electroweak-symmetry-group','leptons','The Electroweak Symmetry Group \\( SU(2)_L \\times U(1)_Y \\)','<p>The <strong>Electroweak Symmetry Group</strong> is the mathematical foundation of the unified force that combines electromagnetism and the weak nuclear force.</p>','The Electroweak Symmetry Group is the mathematical foundation of the unified force that combines electromagnetism and the weak nuclear force.','The Electroweak Symmetry Group is the mathematical foundation of the unified force that combines electromagnetism and the weak nuclear force.','','[]','[]','[\"symmetry-structure-9fe76fcd\"]'),
(2010455,'v-a-interaction','leptons','The V-A (Vector minus Axial-vector) Interaction','<p>The <strong>V-A Interaction</strong> is the specific mathematical form of the weak force that describes how <strong>Leptons</strong> and quarks interact with \\( W^\\pm \\) bosons.</p>','The V-A Interaction is the specific mathematical form of the weak force that describes how Leptons and quarks interact with bosons.','The V-A Interaction is the specific mathematical form of the weak force that describes how Leptons and quarks interact with <svg style=\"color: #FFD700; vertical-align: -0.05ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"3.928ex\" height=\"1.937ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -833.9 1736.3 855.9\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><defs><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-I-1D44A\" d=\"M436 683Q450 683 486 682T553 680Q604 680 638 681T677 682Q695 682 695 674Q695 670 692 659Q687 641 683 639T661 637Q636 636 621 632T600 624T597 615Q597 603 613 377T629 138L631 141Q633 144 637 151T649 170T666 200T690 241T720 295T759 362Q863 546 877 572T892 604Q892 619 873 628T831 637Q817 637 817 647Q817 650 819 660Q823 676 825 679T839 682Q842 682 856 682T895 682T949 681Q1015 681 1034 683Q1048 683 1048 672Q1048 666 1045 655T1038 640T1028 637Q1006 637 988 631T958 617T939 600T927 584L923 578L754 282Q586 -14 585 -15Q579 -22 561 -22Q546 -22 542 -17Q539 -14 523 229T506 480L494 462Q472 425 366 239Q222 -13 220 -15T215 -19Q210 -22 197 -22Q178 -22 176 -15Q176 -12 154 304T131 622Q129 631 121 633T82 637H58Q51 644 51 648Q52 671 64 683H76Q118 680 176 680Q301 680 313 683H323Q329 677 329 674T327 656Q322 641 318 637H297Q236 634 232 620Q262 160 266 136L501 550L499 587Q496 629 489 632Q483 636 447 637Q428 637 422 639T416 648Q416 650 418 660Q419 664 420 669T421 676T424 680T428 682T436 683Z\"></path><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-N-B1\" d=\"M56 320T56 333T70 353H369V502Q369 651 371 655Q376 666 388 666Q402 666 405 654T409 596V500V353H707Q722 345 722 333Q722 320 707 313H409V40H707Q722 32 722 20T707 0H70Q56 7 56 20T70 40H369V313H70Q56 320 56 333Z\"></path></defs><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msup\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D44A\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-I-1D44A\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1136.2,363) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"B1\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-B1\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg> bosons.','<svg style=\"color: #FFD700; vertical-align: -0.05ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"3.928ex\" height=\"1.937ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -833.9 1736.3 855.9\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><defs><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-I-1D44A\" d=\"M436 683Q450 683 486 682T553 680Q604 680 638 681T677 682Q695 682 695 674Q695 670 692 659Q687 641 683 639T661 637Q636 636 621 632T600 624T597 615Q597 603 613 377T629 138L631 141Q633 144 637 151T649 170T666 200T690 241T720 295T759 362Q863 546 877 572T892 604Q892 619 873 628T831 637Q817 637 817 647Q817 650 819 660Q823 676 825 679T839 682Q842 682 856 682T895 682T949 681Q1015 681 1034 683Q1048 683 1048 672Q1048 666 1045 655T1038 640T1028 637Q1006 637 988 631T958 617T939 600T927 584L923 578L754 282Q586 -14 585 -15Q579 -22 561 -22Q546 -22 542 -17Q539 -14 523 229T506 480L494 462Q472 425 366 239Q222 -13 220 -15T215 -19Q210 -22 197 -22Q178 -22 176 -15Q176 -12 154 304T131 622Q129 631 121 633T82 637H58Q51 644 51 648Q52 671 64 683H76Q118 680 176 680Q301 680 313 683H323Q329 677 329 674T327 656Q322 641 318 637H297Q236 634 232 620Q262 160 266 136L501 550L499 587Q496 629 489 632Q483 636 447 637Q428 637 422 639T416 648Q416 650 418 660Q419 664 420 669T421 676T424 680T428 682T436 683Z\"></path><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-N-B1\" d=\"M56 320T56 333T70 353H369V502Q369 651 371 655Q376 666 388 666Q402 666 405 654T409 596V500V353H707Q722 345 722 333Q722 320 707 313H409V40H707Q722 32 722 20T707 0H70Q56 7 56 20T70 40H369V313H70Q56 320 56 333Z\"></path></defs><g stroke=\"