mn\" transform=\"translate(220,-686)\"><use data-c=\"33\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-33\"></use></g><rect width=\"700\" height=\"60\" x=\"120\" y=\"220\"></rect></g><g data-mml-node=\"msub\" transform=\"translate(5666.8,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D45B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-I-1D45B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(633,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"1D453\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-I-1D453\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"msub\" transform=\"translate(6738.7,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D447\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-I-1D447\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(617,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"1D439\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-I-1D439\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(7935.3,0) translate(0 -0.5)\"><use data-c=\"29\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-S3-29\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg>','[]','[]','[\"scaling-law-ba721db7\"]'),
(2010469,'color-confinement','quarks','Color Confinement','<p>Color confinement is the physical principle stating that color-charged particles, such as quarks and gluons, cannot be isolated and consequently cannot be directly observed in nature. They are \"confined\" within color-neutral composite particles called hadrons (mesons and baryons).</p>\n\n                    <h3>1. The Confinement Mechanism</h3>\n                    <p>As the distance between two quarks increases, the self-interaction of gluons causes the color field lines to collapse into a narrow \"flux tube\" or string. The energy required to stretch this string increases linearly with distance (\\( V(r) \\approx \\kappa r \\)). Eventually, it becomes energetically more favorable to create a new quark-antiquark pair from the vacuum, snapping the string and producing two new color-neutral hadrons. This process is known as <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/hadronization\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Hadronization</strong></a>.</p>\n\n                    <h3>2. Mathematical Complexity</h3>\n                    <p>Unlike asymptotic freedom, which can be studied using perturbation theory, confinement is a non-perturbative phenomenon. It occurs at the \"QCD scale\" (\\( \\Lambda_{QCD} \\approx 200 \\text{ MeV} \\)), where the coupling constant becomes large. Understanding confinement rigorously is one of the \"Millennium Prize Problems\" in mathematics, typically approached via <strong>Lattice QCD</strong> simulations.</p>','Color confinement is the physical principle stating that color-charged particles, such as quarks and gluons, cannot be isolated and consequently cannot be directly observed in nature. They are \"confined\" within color-neutral composite particles called hadrons (mesons and baryons). As the distance between two quarks increases, the self-interaction of gluons causes the color field lines to collapse into a narrow \"flux tube\" or string.','Color confinement is the physical principle stating that color-charged particles, such as quarks and gluons, cannot be isolated and consequently cannot be directly observed in nature. They are \"confined\" within color-neutral composite particles called hadrons (mesons and baryons). As the distance between two quarks increases, the self-interaction of gluons causes the color field lines to collapse into a narrow \"flux tube\" or string.','<svg style=\"color: #FFD700; vertical-align: -0.566ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"9.861ex\" height=\"2.262ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -750 4358.6 1000\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><defs><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-I-1D449\" d=\"M52 648Q52 670 65 683H76Q118 680 181 680Q299 680 320 683H330Q336 677 336 674T334 656Q329 641 325 637H304Q282 635 274 635Q245 630 242 620Q242 618 271 369T301 118L374 235Q447 352 520 471T595 594Q599 601 599 609Q599 633 555 637Q537 637 537 648Q537 649 539 661Q542 675 545 679T558 683Q560 683 570 683T604 682T668 681Q737 681 755 683H762Q769 676 769 672Q769 655 760 640Q757 637 743 637Q730 636 719 635T698 630T682 623T670 615T660 608T652 599T645 592L452 282Q272 -9 266 -16Q263 -18 259 -21L241 -22H234Q216 -22 216 -15Q213 -9 177 305Q139 623 138 626Q133 637 76 637H59Q52 642 52 648Z\"></path><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-N-28\" d=\"M94 250Q94 319 104 381T127 488T164 576T202 643T244 695T277 729T302 750H315H319Q333 750 333 741Q333 738 316 720T275 667T226 581T184 443T167 250T184 58T225 -81T274 -167T316 -220T333 -241Q333 -250 318 -250H315H302L274 -226Q180 -141 137 -14T94 250Z\"></path><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-I-1D45F\" d=\"M21 287Q22 290 23 295T28 317T38 348T53 381T73 411T99 433T132 442Q161 442 183 430T214 408T225 388Q227 382 228 382T236 389Q284 441 347 441H350Q398 441 422 400Q430 381 430 363Q430 333 417 315T391 292T366 288Q346 288 334 299T322 328Q322 376 378 392Q356 405 342 405Q286 405 239 331Q229 315 224 298T190 165Q156 25 151 16Q138 -11 108 -11Q95 -11 87 -5T76 7T74 17Q74 30 114 189T154 366Q154 405 128 405Q107 405 92 377T68 316T57 28