olor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"28\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-28\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(389,0)\"><use data-c=\"25FB\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-I-25FB\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1389.2,0)\"><use data-c=\"2B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-2B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"msup\" transform=\"translate(2389.4,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D45A\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-I-1D45A\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(911,413) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(3704,0)\"><use data-c=\"29\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-29\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(4093,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D719\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-I-1D719\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(4966.8,0)\"><use data-c=\"3D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-3D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(6022.6,0)\"><use data-c=\"30\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-30\"></use></g></g></g></svg>','[]','[]','[\"wave-operator-e4fcf61b\",\"field-inertia-b0bf119f\"]'),
(2010480,'dirac-equation','relativistic-quantum-field-theory','The Dirac Equation','<p>The <strong>Dirac Equation</strong> is one of the most profound discoveries in theoretical physics, providing the fundamental description of fermions (matter particles) and predicting the existence of antimatter.</p>\n\n                    <h3>1. The First-Order Requirement</h3>\n                    <p>Paul Dirac sought a relativistic equation that was first-order in time (like the Schrödinger equation) but also respected the symmetry between time and space. To achieve this, he introduced a set of 4x4 matrices (<strong>Dirac Matrices</strong>, \\( \\gamma^\\mu \\)) that satisfy a <strong>Clifford Algebra</strong>: \\( \\{ \\gamma^\\mu, \\gamma^\\nu \\} = 2\\eta^{\\mu\\nu} \\). The resulting equation acts on a 4-component object called a <strong>Dirac Spinor</strong>.</p>\n\n                    <h3>2. The Origin of Spin</h3>\n                    <p>Unlike the Schrödinger equation, where spin must be added by hand, the Dirac equation <strong>necessitates spin</strong>. For the equation to be consistent with relativity, the particles it describes must have intrinsic angular momentum of 1/2. This explains why electrons, quarks, and neutrinos are all fermions, linking the geometry of spacetime to the internal structure of matter.</p>\n\n                    <h3>3. Antimatter and the Dirac Sea</h3>\n                    <p>The Dirac equation predicted states with negative energy. Dirac initially imagined a \"sea\" of filled negative energy states, where a \"hole\" in the sea would behave like a particle with positive charge. We now recognize these holes as <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/antimatter\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Antimatter</strong></a>. This prediction was brilliantly confirmed by the discovery of the <strong>Positron</strong> in 1932, proving that for every matter particle, a twin \"anti-particle\" must exist.</p>','The Dirac Equation is one of the most profound discoveries in theoretical physics, providing the fundamental description of fermions (matter particles) and predicting the existence of antimatter. Paul Dirac sought a relativistic equation that was first-order in time (like the Schrödinger equation) but also respected the symmetry between time and space. To achieve this, he introduced a set of 4x4 matrices (Dirac Matrices, ) that satisfy a Clifford Algebra:.','The Dirac Equation is one of the most profound discoveries in theoretical physics, providing the fundamental description of fermions (matter particles) and predicting the existence of antimatter. Paul Dirac sought a relativistic equation that was first-order in time (like the Schrödinger equation) but also respected the symmetry between time and space. To achieve this, he introduced a set of 4x4 matrices (Dirac Matrices, <svg style=\"color: #FFD700; vertical-align: -0.489ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"2.497ex\" height=\"2.017ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -675.5 1103.6 891.5\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><defs><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-I-1D6FE\" d=\"M31 249Q11 249 11 258Q11 275 26 304T66 365T129 418T206 441Q233 441 239 440Q287 429 318 386T371 255Q385 195 385 170Q385 166 386 166L398 193Q418 244 443 300T486 391T508 430Q510 431 524 431H537Q543 425 543 422Q543 418 522 378T463 251T391 71Q385 55 378 6T357 -100Q341 -165 330 -190T303 -216Q286 -216 286 -188Q286 -138 340 32L346 51L347 69Q348 79 348 100Q348 257 291 317Q251 355 196 355Q148 355 108 329T51 260Q49 251 47 251Q45 249 31 249Z\"></path><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-I-1D707\" d=\"M58 -216Q44 -216 34 -208T23 -186Q23 -176 96 116T173 414Q186 442 219 442Q231 441 239 435T249 423T251 413Q251 401 220 279T187 142Q185 131 185 107V99Q185 26 252 26Q261 26 270 27T287 31T302 38T315 45T327 55T338 65T348 77T356 88T365 100L372 110L408 253Q444 395 448 404Q461 431 491 431Q504 431 512 424T523 412T525 402L449 84Q448 79 448 68Q448 43 455 35T476 26Q485 27 496 35Q517 55 537 131Q543 151 547 152Q549 153