transform=\"translate(566,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"4C\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-C-4C\"></use></g></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mrow\" transform=\"translate(220,-727)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D715\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-I-1D715\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"msub\" transform=\"translate(566,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mover\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D45E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-I-1D45E\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(316.8,-2) translate(-250 0)\"><use data-c=\"2D9\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-2D9\"></use></g></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(479,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"1D456\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-I-1D456\"></use></g></g></g><rect width=\"1539\" height=\"60\" x=\"120\" y=\"220\"></rect></g></g></g></svg>','[]','[]','[\"a-href-physics-subtopic-conjugate-momentum-class-subtopic-link-conjugate-momentum-a-9d0a572e\",\"cyclic-rule-d6793beb\",\"potential-link-125e324c\",\"slope-of-the-wave-be799285\"]');
INSERT INTO `subtopics` VALUES
(2010574,'field-equations','euler-lagrange-equations','Field Equations','<p>Field Equations are the partial differential equations (PDEs) that govern the evolution and distribution of a continuous physical field in the . In university-level physics, these equations are the infinite-dimensional version of the <strong>Equations of Motion</strong>. They describe how the \"stretching\" and \"vibrating\" of the  itself carries forces and information, serving as the foundation for both <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/general-relativity\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>General Relativity</strong></a> and the <strong>Standard Model</strong>.</p>\n\n                    <h3>1. Sourcing from <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/lagrangian\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Lagrangian</strong></a> Density</h3>\n                    <p>Field equations are derived by applying the <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/euler-lagrange-equations\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Euler-Lagrange Equations</strong></a> to a <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/lagrangian-density\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Lagrangian Density</strong></a> (\\( \\mathcal{L} \\)). This process ensures that the resulting laws are <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/manifestly-covariant\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Manifestly Covariant</strong></a>. For a scalar field \\( \\phi \\), the master equation is:\n                    \\[ \\partial_\\mu \\left( \\frac{\\partial \\mathcal{L}}{\\partial (\\partial_\\mu \\phi)} \\right) - \\frac{\\partial \\mathcal{L}}{\\partial \\phi} = 0 \\]\n                    This equation identifies the \"Balance of Power\" between the field\'s kinetic energy (derivatives) and its potential energy (value).</p>\n\n                    <h3>2. Maxwell\'s Equations: The Vector Field</h3>\n                    <p>The most famous set of field equations are <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/maxwells-equations\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Maxwell\'s Equations</strong></a>. In the <strong>Covariant Formulation</strong>, these are derived from the <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/lagrangian\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Lagrangian</strong></a> of the <strong>Electromagnetic Field Tensor</strong>. The inhomogeneous equation \\( \\partial_\\mu F^{\\mu\\nu} = \\mu_0 J^\\nu \\) describes how charges act as \"Sources\" for the field geometry, proving that electromagnetism is a 4D geometric necessity.</p>\n\n                    <h3>3. Einstein Field Equations: The Metric Field</h3>\n                    <p>In <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/general-relativity\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>General Relativity</strong></a>, the \"Field\" being solved for is the <strong>Metric Tensor</strong> (\\( g_{\\mu\\nu} \\)) itself. The <strong>Einstein Field Equations</strong> relate the <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/curvature-of-spacetime\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Curvature of Spacetime</strong></a> to the <strong>Stress-Energy Tensor</strong>. This a non-linear field equation: unlike light, gravity acts as its own source, creating the complex 4D <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/spacetime-causal-topology\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Causal Topology</strong></a> of black holes and the expanding universe.</p>\n\n                    <h3>4. Schrödinger and Klein-Gordon Equations</h3>\n                    <p>In <strong>Theoretical Quantum Mechanics</strong>, the <strong>Wave Function</strong> (\\( \\Psi \\)) is the field being solved for. The <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/schrodinger-equation\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Schrödinger Equation</strong></a> is the non-relativistic field equation for probability amplitude. Its relativistic extension, the <strong>Klein-Gordon Equation</strong>, describes how matter ripples propagate at the <strong>Cosmic Speed Limit</strong>. This links the discrete world of particles to the continuous world of PDEs.</p>\n\n                    <h3>5. Green\'s Functions and Field Response</h3>\n                    <p>Solving field equations often involves <strong>Green\'s Functions</strong>. A Green\'s function represents the \"Impulse Response\" of a field to a single <strong>Dirac Delta Function</strong> point source. By using the <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/quantum-superposition\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Principle of Superposition</strong></a>, we can build the total field of any complex matter distribution, a technique essential for calculating <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/electromagnetic-radiation\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Electromagnetic Radiation</strong></a> from accelerating charges.</p>\n\n                    <h3>6. Epistemic Status: The Primary Reality</h3>\n                    <p>Field equations suggest that the universe is not made of \"objects\" in space, but of \"conditions\" of space. This <strong>Ontological</strong> shift identifies the  as a single, dynamic fabric where every force is just a different PDE being solved. Field equations are the \"Rules of the Grid,\" anchoring <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/scientific-realism\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Scientific Realism</strong></a> in the mathematical consistency of the 4D <strong>Block Universe</strong>.</p>','Field Equations are the partial differential equations (PDEs) that govern the evolution and distribution of a continuous physical field in the. In university-level physics, these equations are the infinite-dimensional version of the Equations of Motion. They describe how the \"stretching\" and \"vibrating\" of the itself carries forces and information, serving as the foundation for both General Relativity and the Standard Model.','Field Equations are the partial differential equations (PDEs) that govern the evolution and distribution of a continuous physical field in the . In university-level physics, these equations are the infinite-dimensional version of the Equations of Motion. They describe how the \"stretching\" and \"vibrating\" of the  itself carries forces and information, serving as the foundation for both General Relativity and the Standard Model.','<svg style=\"color: #FFD700; vertical-align: -2.291ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24.551ex\" height=\"5.571ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -1449.5 10851.4 2462.2\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><defs><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-I-1D715\" d=\"M202 508Q179 508 169 520T158 547Q158 557 164 577T185 624T230 675T301 710L333 715H345Q378 715 384 714Q447 703 489 661T549 568T566 457Q566 362 519 240T402 53Q321 -22 223 -22Q123 -22 73 56Q42 102 42 148V159Q42 276 129 370T322 465Q383 465 414 434T455 367L458 378Q478 461 478 515Q478 603 437 639T344 676Q266 676 223 612Q264 606 264 572Q264 547 246 528T202 508ZM430 306Q430 372 401 400T333 428Q270 428 222 382Q197 354 183 323T150 221Q132 149 132 116Q132 21 232 21Q244 21 250 22Q327 35 374 112Q389 137 409 196T430 306Z\"></path><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-I-1D707\" d=\"M58 -216Q44 -216 34 -208T23 -186Q23 -176 96 116T173 414Q186 442 219 442Q231 441 239 435T249 423T251 413Q251 401 220 279T187 142Q185 131 185 107V99Q185 26 252 26Q261 26 270 27T287 31T302 38T315 45T327 55T338 65T348 77T356 88T365 100L372 110L408 253Q444 395 448 404Q461 431 491 431Q504 431 512 424T523 412T525 402L449 84Q448 79 448 68Q448 43 455 35T476 26Q485 27 496 35Q517 55 537 131Q543 151 547 152Q549 153 557 153H561Q580 153 580 144Q580 138 575 117T555 63T523 13Q510 0 491 -8Q483 -10 467 -10Q446 -10 429 -4T402 11T385 29T376 44T374 51L368 45Q362 39 350 30T324 12T288 -4T246 -11Q199 -11 153 12L129 -85Q108 -167 104 -180T92 -202Q76 -216 58 -216Z\"></path><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-S3-28\" d=\"M701 -940Q701 -943 695 -949H664Q662 -947 636 -922T591 -879T537 -818T475 -737T412 -636T350 -511T295 -362T250 -186T221 17T209 251Q209 962 573 1361Q596 1386 616 1405T649 1437T664 1450H695Q701 1444 701 1441Q701 1436 681 1415T629 1356T557 1261T476 1118T400 927T340 675T308 359Q306 321 306 250Q306 -139 400 -430T690 -924Q701 -936 701 -940Z\"></path><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-C-4C\" d=\"M62 -22T47 -22T32 -11Q32 -1 56 24T83 55Q113 96 138 172T180 320T234 473