=\"translate(1055.2,0)\"><use data-c=\"22C5\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-22C5\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\" transform=\"translate(1555.4,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D401\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-B-1D401\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(2651.2,0)\"><use data-c=\"3D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-3D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"msub\" transform=\"translate(3707,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D707\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-I-1D707\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(636,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"30\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-30\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"msub\" transform=\"translate(4746.6,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D70C\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-I-1D70C\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(550,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"1D45A\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-I-1D45A\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg>','[]','[]','[\"the-monopole-46072aa5\",\"dirac-link-9222b6e7\",\"gut-monopole-657cebdb\",\"inflation-link-b2b0deb6\"]'),
(2010580,'su5-model','grand-unification','The SU(5) Grand Unified Model','<p>The <strong>SU(5) Model</strong>, proposed by Georgi and Glashow in 1974, is the simplest and most elegant <strong>Grand Unified Theory</strong>. It unifies the three <strong>Standard Model</strong> forces—strong (\\( SU(3) \\)), weak (\\( SU(2) \\)), and electromagnetic (\\( U(1) \\))—into a single <strong>Gauge Symmetry</strong> group of rank 4. In university-level physics, \\( SU(5) \\) represents the 4D \"Geometric Origin\" of the particle spectrum, proving that quarks and leptons are two sides of the same subatomic coin.</p>\n\n                    <h3>1. The Group Structure and Generators</h3>\n                    <p>The group \\( SU(5) \\) consists of \\( 5^2 - 1 = 24 \\) generators. In the , these generators correspond to 24 <strong>Gauge Bosons</strong>:\n                        <ul>\n                            <li>8 Gluons (strong force).</li>\n                            <li>3 Weak Bosons (\\( W^\\pm, Z^0 \\)).</li>\n                            <li>1 Photon (\\( \\gamma \\)).</li>\n                            <li>12 New <strong>X and Y Bosons</strong> (Leptoquarks).</li>\n                        </ul>\n                    This unification predicts that at the <strong>Unification Energy</strong> (\\( \\sim 10^{15} \\) GeV), the distinction between these forces disappears, merging into a single symmetric .</p>\n\n                    <h3>2. Fermion Multiplets: 5-bar and 10</h3>\n                    <p>The most stunning feature of \\( SU(5) \\) is how it organizes the 15 <strong>Fermions</strong> of a single generation into two irreducible representations: the <strong>fundamental-representation-gut</strong> (\\( \\bar{\\mathbf{5}} \\)) and the <strong>decuplet-representation-gut</strong> (\\( \\mathbf{10} \\)).\n                    \\[ \\bar{\\mathbf{5}} = \\begin{pmatrix} d^c_R & d^c_G & d^c_B & e & -\\nu_e \\end{pmatrix}_L \\]\n                    The fact that the sum of electric charges in these multiplets is exactly zero provides the 4D mathematical proof for the <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/charge-quantization\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Quantization of Electric Charge</strong></a>.</p>\n\n                    <h3>3. Proton Decay: The Fatal Prediction</h3>\n                    <p>Because \\( SU(5) \\) puts quarks and leptons in the same multiplet, the heavy <strong>X and Y Bosons</strong> can mediate transitions between them. This leads to <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/proton-decay\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Proton Decay</strong></a> (e.g., \\( p \\to e^+ \\pi^0 \\)). The predicted lifetime in the minimal \\( SU(5) \\) model (\\( \\sim 10^{31} \\) years) has been experimentally ruled out by detectors like Super-Kamiokande, signaling a <strong>Theoretical Crisis</strong> that necessitates <strong>Supersymmetry</strong>.</p>\n\n                    <h3>4. <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/hierarchy-problem\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>The Hierarchy Problem</strong></a> in SU(5)</h3>\n                    <p>A major university-level challenge for \\( SU(5) \\) is the <strong>Hierarchy Problem</strong>. The model contains two extremely different energy scales: the Electroweak scale (\\( 246 \\) GeV) and the GUT scale (\\( 10^{15} \\) GeV). Without <strong>\"New Physics\"</strong> like <strong>MSSM</strong>, quantum corrections would naturally drive the Higgs mass to the GUT scale, requiring \"Fine-Tuning\" of 1 part in \\( 10^{26} \\).</p>\n\n                    <h3>5. Gauge Coupling Unification</h3>\n                    <p>According to the <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/rge\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Renormalization Group Equations (RGEs)</strong></a>, the three coupling constants of the Standard Model change with energy. In minimal \\( SU(5) \\), they approach each other but do not perfectly meet. Only by adding the particle content of <strong>Supersymmetry</strong> do the three forces converge precisely at a single 4D point, supporting the <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/scientific-realism\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Scientific Realism</strong></a> of the 4D unified manifold.</p>\n\n                    <h3>6. Epistemic Status: The Prototype Theory</h3>\n                    <p>Although the minimal \\( SU(5) \\) model is ruled out by proton decay limits, it remains the \"Prototype\" for all <strong>Grand Unification</strong>. It taught us that the 4D <strong>Block Universe</strong> is governed by hidden 4D <strong>Symmetries</strong> that reveal themselves only at extreme energies. \\( SU(5) \\) is the foundational <strong>Epistemic</strong> map that guides the search for <strong>SO(10)</strong> and <strong>String Theory</strong> models.</p>','The SU(5) Model, proposed by Georgi and Glashow in 1974, is the simplest and most elegant Grand Unified Theory. It unifies the three Standard Model forces—strong, weak, and electromagnetic —into a single Gauge Symmetry group of rank The group consists of generators. In the, these generators correspond to 24 Gauge Bosons: 8 Gluons (strong force).','The SU(5) Model, proposed by Georgi and Glashow in 1974, is the simplest and most elegant Grand Unified Theory. It unifies the three Standard Model forces—strong (<svg style=\"color: #FFD700; vertical-align: -0.566ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"6.086ex\" height=\"2.262ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -750 2690 1000\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><defs><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-I-1D446\" d=\"M308 24Q367 24 416 76T466 197Q466 260 414 284Q308 311 278 321T236 341Q176 383 176 462Q176 523 208 573T273 648Q302 673 343 688T407 704H418H425Q521 704 564 640Q565 640 577 653T603 682T623 704Q624 704 627 704T632 705Q645 705 645 698T617 577T585 459T569 456Q549 456 549 465Q549 471 550 475Q550 478 551 494T553 520Q553 554 544 579T526 616T501 641Q465 662 419 662Q362 662 313 616T263 510Q263 480 278 458T319 427Q323 425 389 408T456 390Q490 379 522 342T554 242Q554 216 546 186Q541 164 5