wBox=\"0 -750 2278 1000\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><defs><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-N-2212\" d=\"M84 237T84 250T98 270H679Q694 262 694 250T679 230H98Q84 237 84 250Z\"></path><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-N-31\" d=\"M213 578L200 573Q186 568 160 563T102 556H83V602H102Q149 604 189 617T245 641T273 663Q275 666 285 666Q294 666 302 660V361L303 61Q310 54 315 52T339 48T401 46H427V0H416Q395 3 257 3Q121 3 100 0H88V46H114Q136 46 152 46T177 47T193 50T201 52T207 57T213 61V578Z\"></path><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-N-2F\" d=\"M423 750Q432 750 438 744T444 730Q444 725 271 248T92 -240Q85 -250 75 -250Q68 -250 62 -245T56 -231Q56 -221 230 257T407 740Q411 750 423 750Z\"></path><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-N-33\" d=\"M127 463Q100 463 85 480T69 524Q69 579 117 622T233 665Q268 665 277 664Q351 652 390 611T430 522Q430 470 396 421T302 350L299 348Q299 347 308 345T337 336T375 315Q457 262 457 175Q457 96 395 37T238 -22Q158 -22 100 21T42 130Q42 158 60 175T105 193Q133 193 151 175T169 130Q169 119 166 110T159 94T148 82T136 74T126 70T118 67L114 66Q165 21 238 21Q293 21 321 74Q338 107 338 175V195Q338 290 274 322Q259 328 213 329L171 330L168 332Q166 335 166 348Q166 366 174 366Q202 366 232 371Q266 376 294 413T322 525V533Q322 590 287 612Q265 626 240 626Q208 626 181 615T143 592T132 580H135Q138 579 143 578T153 573T165 566T175 555T183 540T186 520Q186 498 172 481T127 463Z\"></path></defs><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(778,0)\"><use data-c=\"31\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-31\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\" transform=\"translate(1278,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2F\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-2F\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(1778,0)\"><use data-c=\"33\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-33\"></use></g></g></g></svg>.','<svg style=\"color: #FFD700; vertical-align: 0;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.717ex\" height=\"1.545ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -683 759 683\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><defs><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-I-1D435\" d=\"M231 637Q204 637 199 638T194 649Q194 676 205 682Q206 683 335 683Q594 683 608 681Q671 671 713 636T756 544Q756 480 698 429T565 360L555 357Q619 348 660 311T702 219Q702 146 630 78T453 1Q446 0 242 0Q42 0 39 2Q35 5 35 10Q35 17 37 24Q42 43 47 45Q51 46 62 46H68Q95 46 128 49Q142 52 147 61Q150 65 219 339T288 628Q288 635 231 637ZM649 544Q649 574 634 600T585 634Q578 636 493 637Q473 637 451 637T416 636H403Q388 635 384 626Q382 622 352 506Q352 503 351 500L320 374H401Q482 374 494 376Q554 386 601 434T649 544ZM595 229Q595 273 572 302T512 336Q506 337 429 337Q311 337 310 336Q310 334 293 263T258 122L240 52Q240 48 252 48T333 46Q422 46 429 47Q491 54 543 105T595 229Z\"></path></defs><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D435\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-I-1D435\"></use></g></g></g></svg>','[]','[]','[\"standard-accounting-8044f6d9\",\"symmetry-break-e820a2a4\",\"the-deeper-rule-d2609183\",\"vacuum-tunnels-1bdaf91a\"]'),
(2010591,'matter-antimatter-asymmetry','grand-unification','Matter-Antimatter Asymmetry','<p>Matter-Antimatter Asymmetry (or Baryon Asymmetry) is the observational fact that the <strong>observable universe</strong> is composed almost entirely of matter, with no significant primordial pockets of <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/antimatter\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Antimatter</strong></a>. In university-level cosmology, this asymmetry is a major <strong>Theoretical Crisis</strong>, as the <strong>Standard Model</strong> and <strong>Big Bang</strong> theory predict they should have been created in equal amounts. Resolving this requires <strong>Baryogenesis</strong> via <strong>Grand Unification</strong>.</p>\n\n                    <h3>1. The Annihilation Problem</h3>\n                    <p>If the universe began with equal parts matter and antimatter, they would have annihilated into <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/electromagnetic-radiation\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Electromagnetic Radiation</strong></a> as the  cooled. The resulting 4D universe would be a dark void of photons with almost no atoms. The fact that we exist proves that for every billion antiquarks, there were approximately a billion and one quarks. This \"One in a Billion\" excess is the <strong>Initial Condition</strong> for all 4D structure.</p>\n\n                    <h3>2. The Sakharov Conditions</h3>\n                    <p>In 1967, Andrei Sakharov proved that any theory explaining the asymmetry must satisfy three conditions:\n                        <ul>\n                            <li><strong>B-Violation:</strong> To create an excess of baryons.</li>\n                            <li><strong>C and <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/cp-violation\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>CP Violation</strong></a>:</strong> To ensure matter and antimatter reactions are not mirror images.</li>\n                            <li><strong>Out-of-Equilibrium:</strong> To prevent the reverse reactions from washing out the excess.</li>\n                        </ul>\n                    These conditions are the 4D blueprint for <strong>Baryogenesis</strong>, linking subatomic 4D <strong>Symmetry</strong> to the global <strong>Cosmic Budget</strong>.</p>\n\n                    <h3>3. Baryogenesis at the GUT Scale</h3>\n                    <p>GUTs provide a natural site for fulfilling these conditions. The decay of heavy <strong>X and Y Bosons</strong> in the first \\( 10^{-35} \\) seconds provides both <strong>B-Violation</strong> and the required CP-violation. Because the expansion of the universe was so rapid (<a href=\"/physics/subtopic/cosmic-inflation\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Cosmic Inflation</strong></a>), the decays occurred out of thermal equilibrium, \"Freezing in\" the matter excess before it could be erased.</p>\n\n                    <h3>4. Leptogenesis and Neutrinos</h3>\n                    <p>An alternative theory, <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/leptogenesis\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Leptogenesis</strong></a>, suggests the asymmetry started in the lepton sector. The CP-violating decays of heavy <strong>right-handed neutrino</strong> particles created a lepton excess, which was later converted into a baryon excess by <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/sphalerons\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Sphalerons</strong></a>. This links the <strong>Mass Origin</strong> of neutrinos to the very existence of matter, a primary focus of the <strong>DUNE</strong> experiment.</p>\n\n                    <h3>5. Observational Evidence: The CMB</h3>\n                    <p>The magnitude of the asymmetry is measured using the <strong>Baryon-to-Photon Ratio</strong> (\\( \\eta \\)) derived from the <strong>Cosmic Microwave Background (CMB)</strong> and <strong>Big Bang Nucleosynthesis</strong>.\n                    \\[ \\eta = \\frac{n_B - n_{\\bar{B}}}{n_\\gamma} \\approx 6 \\times 10^{-10} \\]\n                    This precise number confirms that the  had a tiny, consistent \"Lean\" toward matter, dictating the <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/total-dynamics\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Total Dynamics</strong></a> of the radiation-dominated era.</p>\n\n                    <h3>6. Epistemic Status: The Lucky Residue</h3>\n                    <p>The matter-antimatter asymmetry teaches us that the entire visible universe is a \"Luck residue\" of a great subatomic war. Everything we see—stars, planets, and people—is the 4D leftover of a near-perfect annihilation. This <strong>Ontological</strong> fact anchors <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/scientific-realism\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Scientific Realism</strong></a> in the subatomic 4D <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/spacetime-causal-topology\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Causal Topology</strong></a> of the <strong>Early Universe</strong>, proving that small 4D imbalances create large-scale 4D realities.</p>','Matter-Antimatter Asymmetry (or Baryon Asymmetry) is the observational fact that the observable universe is composed almost entirely of matter, with no significant primordial pockets of Antimatter. In university-level cosmology, this asymmetry is a major Theoretical Crisis, as the Standard Model and Big Bang theory predict they should have been created in equal amounts. Resolving this requires Baryogenesis via Grand Unification.','Matter-Antimatter Asymmetry (or Baryon Asymmetry) is the observational fact that the observable universe is composed almost entirely of matter, with no significant primordial pockets of Antimatter. In university-level cosmology, this asymmetry is a major Theoretical Crisis, as the Standard Model and Big Bang theory predict they should have been created in equal amounts. Resolving this requires Baryogenesis via Grand Unification.','<svg style=\"color: #FFD700; vertical-align: -2.237ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"25.63ex\" height=\"5.291ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -1349.8 11328.6 2338.6\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><defs><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-I-1D702\" d=\"M21 287Q22 290 23 295T28 317T38 348T53 381T73 411T99 433T132 442Q156 442 175 435T205 417T221 395T229 376L231 369Q231 367 232 367L243 378Q304 442 382 442Q436 442 469 415T503 336V326Q503 302 439 53Q381 -182 377 -189Q364 -216 332 -216Q319 -216 310 -208T299 -186Q299 -177 358 57L420 307Q423 322 423 345Q423 404 379 404H374Q288 404 229 303L222 291L189 157Q156 26 151 16Q138 -11 108 -11Q95 -11 87 -5T76 7T74 17Q74 30 114 189T154 366Q154 405 128 405Q107 405 92 377T68 316T57 280Q55 278 41 278H27Q21 284 21 287Z\"></path><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-N-3D\" d=\"M56 347Q56 360 70 367H707Q722 359 722 347Q722 336 708 328L390 327H72Q56 332 56 347ZM56 153Q56 168 72 173H708Q722 163 722 153Q722 140 707 133H70Q56 140 56 153Z\"></path><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-I-1D45B\" d=\"M21 287Q22 293 24 303T36 341T56 388T89 425T135 442Q171 442 195 424T225 390T231 369Q231 367 232 367L243 378Q304 442 382 442Q436 442 469 415T503 336T465 179T427 52Q427 26 444 26Q450 26 453 27Q482 32 505 65T540 145Q542 153 560 153Q580 153 580 145Q580 144 576 130Q568 101 554 73T508 17T439 -10Q392 -10 371 17T350 73Q350 92 386 193T423 345Q423 404 379 404H374Q288 404 229 303L222 291L189 157Q156 26 151 16Q138 -11 108 -11Q95 -11 87 -5T76 7T74 17Q74 30 112 180T152 343Q153 348 153 366Q153 405 129 405Q91 405 66 305Q60 285 60 284Q58 278 41 278H27Q21 284 21 287Z\"></path><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-I-1D435\" d=\"M231 637Q204 637 199 638T194 649Q194 676 205 682Q206 683 335 683Q594 683 608 681Q671 671 713 636T756 544Q756 480 698 429T565 360L555 357Q619 348 660 311T702 219Q702 146 630 78T453 1Q446 0 242 0Q42 0 39 2Q35 5 35 10Q35 17 37 24Q42 43 47 45Q51 46 62 46H68Q95 46 128 49Q142 52 147 61Q150 65 219 339T288 628Q288 635 231 637ZM649 544Q649 574 634 600T585 634Q578 636 493 637Q473 637 451 637T416 636H403Q388 635 384 626Q382 622 352 506Q352 503 351 500L320 374H401Q482 374 494 376Q554 386 601 434T649 544ZM595 229Q595 273 572 302T512 336Q506 337 429 337Q311 337 310 336Q310 334 293 263T258 122L240 52