><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-N-32\" d=\"M109 429Q82 429 66 447T50 491Q50 562 103 614T235 666Q326 666 387 610T449 465Q449 422 429 383T381 315T301 241Q265 210 201 149L142 93L218 92Q375 92 385 97Q392 99 409 186V189H449V186Q448 183 436 95T421 3V0H50V19V31Q50 38 56 46T86 81Q115 113 136 137Q145 147 170 174T204 211T233 244T261 278T284 308T305 340T320 369T333 401T340 431T343 464Q343 527 309 573T212 619Q179 619 154 602T119 569T109 550Q109 549 114 549Q132 549 151 535T170 489Q170 464 154 447T109 429Z\"></path><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-N-2264\" d=\"M674 636Q682 636 688 630T694 615T687 601Q686 600 417 472L151 346L399 228Q687 92 691 87Q694 81 694 76Q694 58 676 56H670L382 192Q92 329 90 331Q83 336 83 348Q84 359 96 365Q104 369 382 500T665 634Q669 636 674 636ZM84 -118Q84 -108 99 -98H678Q694 -104 694 -118Q694 -130 679 -138H98Q84 -131 84 -118Z\"></path></defs><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(0 -0.5)\"><use data-c=\"7C\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-7C\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(278,0)\"><use data-c=\"27E8\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-27E8\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(667,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D719\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-I-1D719\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1263,0) translate(0 -0.5)\"><use data-c=\"7C\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-7C\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(1541,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D713\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-I-1D713\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(2192,0)\"><use data-c=\"27E9\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-27E9\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"msup\" transform=\"translate(2581,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(0 -0.5)\"><use data-c=\"7C\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-7C\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(311,413) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(3573.3,0)\"><use data-c=\"2264\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-2264\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(4629.1,0)\"><use data-c=\"27E8\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-27E8\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(5018.1,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D719\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-I-1D719\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(5614.1,0) translate(0 -0.5)\"><use data-c=\"7C\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-7C\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(5892.1,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D719\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-I-1D719\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(6488.1,0)\"><use data-c=\"27E9\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-27E9\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(6877.1,0)\"><use data-c=\"27E8\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-27E8\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(7266.1,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D713\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-I-1D713\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(7917.1,0) translate(0 -0.5)\"><use data-c=\"7C\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-7C\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(8195.1,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D713\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-I-1D713\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(8846.1,0)\"><use data-c=\"27E9\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-27E9\"></use></g></g></g></svg>','[]','[]','[\"standard-bound-37b64d8c\",\"heisenberg-link-3a87bdfe\",\"saturation-2c7b6f4e\",\"probability-guard-8576c685\"]'),
(2010633,'square-integrability','hilbert-space','Square-Integrability','<p>Square-Integrability is the physical and mathematical requirement that the absolute square of a <strong>Wave Function</strong> must have a finite integral over its entire domain. In university-level physics, square-integrability defines the \"Membership\" in the 4D <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/hilbert-space\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Hilbert Space</strong></a>. It is the 4D geometric expression of the <strong>Conservation</strong> of mass and probability, ensuring that every  remains <strong>Localizable</strong> within the .</p>\n\n                    <h3>1. The Physical Existential Condition</h3>\n                    <p>For a wave function \\( \\psi(\\mathbf{r}) \\) to represent a real particle, the <strong>Born Interpretation</strong> requires:\n                    \\[ \\int_{\\text{All Space}} |\\psi(\\mathbf{r})|^2 d\\tau = 1 \\]\n                    If the function is not square-integrable (i.e., the integral diverges), the particle would have an infinite probability of being found, which is physically impossible. This condition \"Filters\" out mathematical functions that do not represent <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/scientific-realism\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Scientific Realism</strong></a> in the 4D <strong>Block Universe</strong>.</p>\n\n                    <h3>2. Hilbert Space Membership (L^2)</h3>\n                    <p>Square-integrable functions form the <strong>Infinite-Dimensional</strong> vector space \\( L^2 \\). This space is the natural home for the <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/hamiltonian-operator\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Hamiltonian Operator</strong></a> and <strong>Momentum Operator</strong>. Because \\( L^2 \\) is a <strong>Complete Space</strong>, we are guaranteed that any physical interaction (like 4D scattering) will result in a new state that is also square-integrable, preserving <strong>Physical Causality</strong>.</p>\n\n                    <h3>3. Boundaries and Decay</h3>\n                    <p>For a function to be square-integrable on an infinite domain, it must \"Decay\" to zero at infinity faster than \\( 1/\\sqrt{r} \\) in 1D. This 4D geometric requirement is what dictates the <strong>Boundary Conditions</strong> for atoms. It explains why the electron in a hydrogen atom has \"Bound States\" with discrete <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/energy-eigenvalues\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Energy Eigenvalues</strong></a>, linking <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/potential-theory\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Potential Theory</strong></a> to the subatomic scale.</p>\n\n                    <h3>4. Non-Square-Integrable States (Plane Waves)</h3>\n                    <p>A university-level nuance is the use of \"Plane Waves\" (\\( e^{ipx/\\hbar} \\)), which are <em>not</em> square-integrable. These states represent particles with perfectly defined momentum but zero 4D localization. In <strong>Relativistic Quantum Field Theory</strong>, we treat these as \"Idealized\" limits in a <strong>Rigged Hilbert Space</strong>, using them as an <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/orthonormal-basis\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Orthonormal Basis</strong></a> to construct real, square-integrable wave packets.</p>\n\n                    <h3>5. Plancherel\'s Theorem and Momentum</h3>\n                    <p>Square-integrability is preserved under the Fourier Transform. This means that if a particle\'s position wave function is \\( L^2 \\), its <strong>Momentum Representation</strong> wave function is also \\( L^2 \\). This 4D <strong>Symmetry</strong> ensures that <strong>Information Density</strong> is conserved whether we look at where a particle is or how fast it is moving.</p>\n\n                    <h3>6. Epistemic Status: The Identity of a Particle</h3>\n                    <p>Square-integrability is an <strong>Ontological</strong> definition of a particle. It tells us that a particle is a \"Packet\" of energy that is localized in space and time. By restricting our 4D physics to \\( L^2 \\) functions, we anchor our <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/scientific-realism\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Scientific Realism</strong></a> in the belief that the universe is made of finite, countable excitations of the  rather than infinite, continuous flows.</p>','Square-Integrability is the physical and mathematical requirement that the absolute square of a Wave Function must have a finite integral over its entire domain. In university-level physics, square-integrability defines the \"Membership\" in the 4D Hilbert Space. It is the 4D geometric expression of the Conservation of mass and probability, ensuring that every remains Localizable within the.','Square-Integrability is the physical and mathematical requirement that the absolute square of a Wave Function must have a finite integral over its entire domain. In university-level physics, square-integrability defines the \"Membership\" in the 4D Hilbert Space. It is the 4D geometric expression of the Conservation of mass and probability, ensuring that every  remains Localizable within the .','<svg style=\"color: #FFD700; vertical-align: -2.338ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"21.357ex\" height=\"5.417ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -1361 9439.8 2394.5\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><defs><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-LO-222B\" d=\"M114 -798Q132 -824 165 -824H167Q195 -824 223 -764T275 -600T320 -391T362 -164Q365 -143 367 -133Q439 292 523 655T645 1127Q651 1145 655 1157T672 1201T699 1257T733 1306T777 1346T828 1360Q884 1360 912 1325T944 1245Q944 1220 932 1205T909 1186T887 1183Q866 1183 849 1198T832 1239Q832 1287 885 1296L882 1300Q879 1303 874 1307T866 1313Q851 1323 833 1323Q819 1323 807 1311T775 1255T736 1139T689 936T633 628Q574 293 510 -5T410 -437T355 -629Q278 -862 165 -862Q125 -862 92 -831T55 -746Q55 -711 74 -698T112 -685Q133 -685 150 -700T167 -741Q167 -789 114 -798Z\"></path><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-N-41\" d