></use></g></g></g></svg>). This university-level abstraction moves beyond mere coordinate grids to treat the state space as a topological object where position and momentum are inextricably linked by a global geometric structure, providing the necessary framework for both General Relativity and Quantum Field Theory. A symplectic manifold is an even-dimensional smooth manifold equipped with a Symplectic Form (<svg style=\"color: #FFD700; vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.407ex\" height=\"1.027ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -443 622 454\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><defs><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-I-1D714\" d=\"M495 384Q495 406 514 424T555 443Q574 443 589 425T604 364Q604 334 592 278T555 155T483 38T377 -11Q297 -11 267 66Q266 68 260 61Q201 -11 125 -11Q15 -11 15 139Q15 230 56 325T123 434Q135 441 147 436Q160 429 160 418Q160 406 140 379T94 306T62 208Q61 202 61 187Q61 124 85 100T143 76Q201 76 245 129L253 137V156Q258 297 317 297Q348 297 348 261Q348 243 338 213T318 158L308 135Q309 133 310 129T318 115T334 97T358 83T393 76Q456 76 501 148T546 274Q546 305 533 325T508 357T495 384Z\"></path></defs><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D714\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-I-1D714\"></use></g></g></g></svg>)—a differential 2-form that is both Closed (<svg style=\"color: #FFD700; vertical-align: -0.186ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"6.732ex\" height=\"1.756ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -694 2975.6 776\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><defs><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-I-1D451\" d=\"M366 683Q367 683 438 688T511 694Q523 694 523 686Q523 679 450 384T375 83T374 68Q374 26 402 26Q411 27 422 35Q443 55 463 131Q469 151 473 152Q475 153 483 153H487H491Q506 153 506 145Q506 140 503 129Q490 79 473 48T445 8T417 -8Q409 -10 393 -10Q359 -10 336 5T306 36L300 51Q299 52 296 50Q