><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-I-1D45E\" d=\"M33 157Q33 258 109 349T280 441Q340 441 372 389Q373 390 377 395T388 406T404 418Q438 442 450 442Q454 442 457 439T460 434Q460 425 391 149Q320 -135 320 -139Q320 -147 365 -148H390Q396 -156 396 -157T393 -175Q389 -188 383 -194H370Q339 -192 262 -192Q234 -192 211 -192T174 -192T157 -193Q143 -193 143 -185Q143 -182 145 -170Q149 -154 152 -151T172 -148Q220 -148 230 -141Q238 -136 258 -53T279 32Q279 33 272 29Q224 -10 172 -10Q117 -10 75 30T33 157ZM352 326Q329 405 277 405Q242 405 210 374T160 293Q131 214 119 129Q119 126 119 118T118 106Q118 61 136 44T179 26Q233 26 290 98L298 109L352 326Z\"></path><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-N-2227\" d=\"M318 591Q325 598 333 598Q344 598 348 591Q349 590 414 445T545 151T611 -4Q609 -22 591 -22Q588 -22 586 -21T581 -20T577 -17T575 -13T572 -9T570 -4L333 528L96 -4Q87 -20 80 -21Q78 -22 75 -22Q57 -22 55 -4Q55 2 120 150T251 444T318 591Z\"></path><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-I-1D45D\" d=\"M23 287Q24 290 25 295T30 317T40 348T55 381T75 411T101 433T134 442Q209 442 230 378L240 387Q302 442 358 442Q423 442 460 395T497 281Q497 173 421 82T249 -10Q227 -10 210 -4Q199 1 187 11T168 28L161 36Q160 35 139 -51T118 -138Q118 -144 126 -145T163 -148H188Q194 -155 194 -157T191 -175Q188 -187 185 -190T172 -194Q170 -194 161 -194T127 -193T65 -192Q-5 -192 -24 -194H-32Q-39 -187 -39 -183Q-37 -156 -26 -148H-6Q28 -147 33 -136Q36 -130 94 103T155 350Q156 355 156 364Q156 405 131 405Q109 405 94 377T71 316T59 280Q57 278 43 278H29Q23 284 23 287ZM178 102Q200 26 252 26Q282 26 310 49T356 107Q374 141 392 215T411 325V331Q411 405 350 405Q339 405 328 402T306 393T286 380T269 365T254 350T243 336T235 326L232 322Q232 321 229 308T218 264T204 212Q178 106 178 102Z\"></path></defs><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D714\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-I-1D714\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(899.8,0)\"><use data-c=\"3D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-3D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"munder\" transform=\"translate(1955.6,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2211\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-LO-2211\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(600,-1084.4) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"1D456\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-I-1D456\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(3566.2,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D451\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-I-1D451\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"msub\" transform=\"translate(4086.2,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D45E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-I-1D45E\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(479,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"1D456\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-I-1D456\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(5081.4,0)\"><use data-c=\"2227\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-2227\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(5970.6,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D451\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-I-1D451\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"msub\" transform=\"translate(6490.6,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D45D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-I-1D45D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(536,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"1D456\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-I-1D456\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg>','[]','[]','[\"geometric-metric-a888626a\",\"incompressibility-74b430ae\",\"area-quantization-103507df\",\"deterministic-path-edc8bb30\"]'),
(2010724,'hamiltonian-mechanics','theoretical-physics','Hamiltonian Mechanics and Phase Space','<p>Hamiltonian mechanics is a powerful refinement of analytical dynamics that shifts the focus from configuration space to <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/phase-space\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Phase Space</strong></a>. By treating position and momentum as independent variables, it reveals the deep <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/symplectic-geometry\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Symplectic Geometry</strong></a> of the physical world and provides the mathematical language for statistical mechanics and quantum theory.</p>\n\n                    <h3>1. The Legendre Transformation and Canonical Variables</h3>\n                    <p>The transition from <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/lagrangian\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Lagrangian</strong></a> to <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/hamiltonian\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Hamiltonian</strong></a> mechanics is achieved via a <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/legendre-transformation\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Legendre Transformation</strong></a>. This transformation replaces the generalized velocity (\\( \\dot{q} \\)) with the <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/conjugate-momentum\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Conjugate Momentum</strong></a> (\\( p_i = \\partial L / \\partial \\dot{q}_i \\)). The <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/hamiltonian\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Hamiltonian</strong></a> function (\\( H \\)) is then constructed as:\n                    \\[ H(q, p, t) = \\sum_i p_i \\dot{q}_i - L(q, \\dot{q}, t) \\]\n                    In this framework, the state of a system with \\( n \\) degrees of freedom is represented as a single point in a \\( 2n \\)-dimensional manifold, allowing dynamics to be analyzed as a flow in phase space.</p>\n\n                    <h3>2. Hamilton\'s Canonical Equations</h3>\n                    <p>The evolution of the system is governed by a symmetric pair of first-order differential equations known as <strong>Hamilton\'s Equations</strong>:\n                    \\[ \\dot{q}_i = \\frac{\\partial H}{\\partial p_i}, \\quad \\dot{p}_i = -\\frac{\\partial H}{\\partial q_i} \\]\n                    These equations demonstrate that the \"flow\" of a physical system is always perpendicular to the gradient of its energy, ensuring that trajectories remain on surfaces of constant energy (for time-independent systems).</p>\n\n                    <h3>3. Poisson Brackets and Symplectic Algebra</h3>\n                    <p>The algebraic structure of <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/hamiltonian\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Hamiltonian</strong></a> mechanics is defined by the <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/poisson-bracket\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Poisson Bracket</strong></a> (\\( \\{f, g\\} \\)). This operation satisfies the properties of a <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/lie-algebra\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Lie Algebra</strong></a>, including antisymmetry and the Jacobi identity. The time-evolution of any physical observable \\( A \\) is given by:\n                    \\[ \\frac{dA}{dt} = \\{A, H\\} + \\frac{\\partial A}{\\partial t} \\]\n                    This formulation proves that a quantity is conserved if its Poisson bracket with the <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/hamiltonian\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Hamiltonian</strong></a> vanishes, providing a direct classical precursor to the Heisenberg equation of motion in quantum mechanics.</p>\n\n                    <h3>4. Liouville\'s Theorem and Statistical Flow</h3>\n                    <p>A fundamental result of <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/hamiltonian\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Hamiltonian</strong></a> dynamics is <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/liouvilles-theorem\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Liouville\'s Theorem</strong></a>, which states that the <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/phase-space-volume\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Phase Space Volume</strong></a> of a collection of systems is invariant under <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/hamiltonian\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Hamiltonian</strong></a> evolution (\\( d\\rho/dt = 0 \\)). This implies that the distribution of states behaves like an <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/incompressible-fluid-phase-space\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Incompressible Fluid</strong></a>. This theorem is the bedrock of statistical mechanics, allowing for the definition of stable equilibrium ensembles (like the Gibbs distribution) in complex many-body systems.</p>\n\n                    <h3>5. Hamilton-Jacobi Theory</h3>\n                    <p>At the highest level of classical dynamics, <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/hamilton-jacobi-theory\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Hamilton-Jacobi Theory</strong></a> seeks a canonical transformation that renders the <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/hamiltonian\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Hamiltonian</strong></a> identically zero. This leads to the <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/hamilton-jacobi-equation\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Hamilton-Jacobi Equation</strong></a>, a first-order non-linear PDE for the <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/principal-function\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Principal Function</strong></a> (\\( S \\)):\n                    \\[ H\\left(q, \\frac{\\partial S}{\\partial q}, t\\right) + \\frac{\\partial S}{\\partial t} = 0 \\]\n                    Solving this equation provides a complete set of constants of motion (action-angle variables). Moreover, the principal function \\( S \\) acts as the phase of the quantum wave function in the eikonal limit, providing the formal link between classical trajectories and quantum waves.</p>','Hamiltonian mechanics is a powerful refinement of analytical dynamics that shifts the focus from configuration space to Phase Space. By treating position and momentum as independent variables, it reveals the deep Symplectic Geometry of the physical world and provides the mathematical language for statistical mechanics and quantum theory. The transition from Lagrangian to Hamiltonian mechanics is achieved via a Legendre Transformation.','Hamiltonian mechanics is a powerful refinement of analytical dynamics that shifts the focus from configuration space to Phase Space. By treating position and momentum as independent variables, it reveals the deep Symplectic Geometry of the physical world and provides the mathematical language for statistical mechanics and quantum theory. The transition from Lagrangian to Hamiltonian mechanics is achieved via a Legendre Transformation.','<svg style=\"color: #FFD700; vertical-align: -2.697ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"30.041ex\" height=\"4.847ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -950 13278.2 2142.2\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><defs><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-I-1D43B\" d=\"M228 637Q194 637 192 641Q191 643 191 649Q191 673 202 682Q204 683 219 683Q260 681 355 681Q389 681 418 681T463 682T483 682Q499 682 499 672Q499 670 497 658Q492 641 487 638H485Q483 638 480 638T473 638T464 637T455 637Q416 636 405 634T387 623Q384 619 355 500Q348 474 340 442T328 395L324 380Q324 378 469 378H614L615 381Q615 384 646 504Q674 619 674 627T617 637Q594 637 587 639T580 648Q580 650 582 660Q586 677 588 679T604 682Q609 682 646 681T740 680Q802 680 835 681T871 682Q888 682 888 672Q888 645 876 638H874Q872 638 869 638T862 638T853 637T844 637Q805 636 794 634T776 623Q773 618 704 340T634 58Q634 51 638 51Q646 48 692 46H723Q729 38 729 37T726 19Q722 6 716 0H701Q664 2 567 2Q533 2 504 2T458 2T437 1Q420 1 420 10Q420 15 423 24Q428 43 433 45Q437 46 448 46H454Q481 46 514 49Q520 50 522 50T528 55T534 64T540 82T547 110T558 153Q565 181 569 198Q602 330 602 331T457 332H312L279 197Q245 63 245 58Q245 51 253 49T303 46H334Q340 38 340 37T337 19Q333 6 327 0H312Q275 2 178 2Q144 2 115 2T69 2T48 1Q31 1 31 10Q31 12 34 24Q39 43 44 45Q48 46 59 46H65Q92 46 125 49Q139 52 144 61Q147 65 216 339T285 628Q285 635 228 637Z\"></path><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-N-28\" d=\"M94 250Q94 319 104 3