321 597Z\"></path><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-N-36\" d=\"M42 313Q42 476 123 571T303 666Q372 666 402 630T432 550Q432 525 418 510T379 495Q356 495 341 509T326 548Q326 592 373 601Q351 623 311 626Q240 626 194 566Q147 500 147 364L148 360Q153 366 156 373Q197 433 263 433H267Q313 433 348 414Q372 400 396 374T435 317Q456 268 456 210V192Q456 169 451 149Q440 90 387 34T253 -22Q225 -22 199 -14T143 16T92 75T56 172T42 313ZM257 397Q227 397 205 380T171 335T154 278T148 216Q148 133 160 97T198 39Q222 21 251 21Q302 21 329 59Q342 77 347 104T352 209Q352 289 347 316T329 361Q302 397 257 397Z\"></path></defs><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"223C\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-223C\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"msup\" transform=\"translate(1055.8,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\"><use data-c=\"31\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-31\"></use><use data-c=\"30\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-30\" transform=\"translate(500,0)\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" transform=\"translate(1033,393.1) scale(0.707)\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\"><use data-c=\"31\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-31\"></use><use data-c=\"36\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-N-36\" transform=\"translate(500,0)\"></use></g></g></g></g></g></svg>','[]','[]','[\"a-href-physics-subtopic-renormalization-group-class-subtopic-link-renormalization-group-a-2889d62b\",\"a-href-physics-subtopic-fermion-unification-class-subtopic-link-fermion-unification-a-a694834c\",\"a-href-physics-subtopic-unification-energy-class-subtopic-link-unification-energy-a-8178cea6\",\"a-href-physics-subtopic-b-violation-class-subtopic-link-b-violation-a-02c398e6\"]'),
(2010739,'string-theory','theoretical-physics','String Theory and M-Theory','<p>String Theory is a revolutionary mathematical framework that replaces zero-dimensional point particles with one-dimensional <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/extended-objects\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Extended Objects</strong></a> called strings. In university-level theoretical physics, it is the primary candidate for a <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/theory-of-everything\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Theory of Everything (ToE)</strong></a>, providing a UV-finite quantum description of gravity that naturally unifies with the gauge interactions of the Standard Model.</p>\n\n                    <h3>1. Worldsheet Dynamics: Nambu-Goto and Polyakov Actions</h3>\n                    <p>The motion of a relativistic string is described by the <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/worldsheet\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Worldsheet</strong></a>, the 2D surface it sweeps through spacetime. Dynamics are governed by the <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/nambu-goto-action\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Nambu-Goto Action</strong></a>, proportional to the worldsheet area. However, for quantization, the <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/polyakov-action\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Polyakov Action</strong></a> is preferred:\n                    \\[ S_P = -\\frac{T}{2} \\int d^2\\sigma \\sqrt{-h} h^{\\alpha\\beta} \\partial_\\alpha X^\\mu \\partial_\\beta X^\\nu \\eta_{\\mu\\nu} \\]\n                    This formulation introduces an auxiliary metric \\( h_{\\alpha\\beta} \\) and possesses <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/weyl-invariance\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Weyl Invariance</strong></a> (local scale invariance). In the critical dimension (\\( D=10 \\) for superstrings), the Weyl anomaly vanishes, ensuring the consistency of the quantum theory.</p>\n\n                    <h3>2. The Five Superstring Theories and M-Theory</h3>\n                    <p>There are five consistent 10-dimensional superstring theories: <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/superstring-theories\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Type I, Type IIA, Type IIB, Heterotic SO(32), and Heterotic \\( E_8 \\times E_8 \\)</strong></a>. The \"Second Superstring Revolution\" revealed that these are non-perturbative limits of a single 11-dimensional framework known as <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/m-theory\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>M-Theory</strong></a>. While strings are the fundamental objects in 10D, M-Theory is governed by higher-dimensional membranes (<a href=\"/physics/subtopic/m2-m5-branes\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>M2 and M5-branes</strong></a>) and its low-energy limit is 11D Supergravity.</p>\n\n                    <h3>3. Dualities: The Web of Connectivity</h3>\n                    <p>Dualities prove that seemingly distinct string theories describe the same physical reality:\n                        <ul>\n                            <li><a href=\"/physics/subtopic/t-duality\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>T-Duality</strong></a>: Relates a theory on a circle of radius \\( R \\) to one on radius \\( 1/R \\), exchanging momentum and winding modes (e.g., IIA \\(\\leftrightarrow\\) IIB).</li>\n                            <li><a href=\"/physics/subtopic/s-duality\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>S-Duality</strong></a>: Relates the strong-coupling limit of one theory to the weak-coupling limit of another (e.g., Type I \\(\\leftrightarrow\\) Heterotic SO(32)), providing a tool to probe non-perturbative regimes.</li>\n                        </ul>\n                    </p>\n\n                    <h3>4. D-Branes and AdS/CFT Correspondence</h3>\n                    <p><a href=\"/physics/subtopic/d-branes\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>D-Branes</strong></a> are dynamical hypersurfaces where open strings end. They carry non-Abelian gauge fields and are essential for constructing realistic particle physics models. A major breakthrough is the <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/ads-cft\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>AdS/CFT Correspondence</strong></a> (Holography), which conjectures an exact equivalence between string theory in <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/anti-de-sitter\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Anti-de Sitter (AdS)</strong></a> space and a <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/conformal-field-theory\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Conformal Field Theory (CFT)</strong></a> on its boundary. This allows for the study of strongly coupled quantum systems via classical gravity.</p>\n\n                    <h3>5. Compactification and the Swampland</h3>\n                    <p>To recover 4D physics, the 6 extra dimensions are compactified on <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/calabi-yau-manifolds\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Calabi-Yau Manifolds</strong></a>—Ricci-flat Kähler manifolds with \\( SU(3) \\) holonomy. The manifold\'s topology determines the number of particle generations. The vast number of possible vacua (\\( \\sim 10^{500} \\)) is called the <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/landscape\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Landscape</strong></a>. Conversely, the <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/swampland\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Swampland</strong></a> refers to the set of seemingly consistent field theories that <em>cannot</em> be consistently coupled to quantum gravity, leading to conjectures like the <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/weak-gravity-conjecture\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Weak Gravity Conjecture</strong></a>.</p>','String Theory is a revolutionary mathematical framework that replaces zero-dimensional point particles with one-dimensional Extended Objects called strings. In university-level theoretical physics, it is the primary candidate for a Theory of Everything (ToE), providing a UV-finite quantum description of gravity that naturally unifies with the gauge interactions of the Standard Model. The motion of a relativistic string is described by the Worldsheet, the 2D surface it sweeps through spacetime.','String Theory is a revolutionary mathematical framework that replaces zero-dimensional point particles with one-dimensional Extended Objects called strings. In university-level theoretical physics, it is the primary candidate for a Theory of Everything (ToE), providing a UV-finite quantum description of gravity that naturally unifies with the gauge interactions of the Standard Model. The motion of a relativistic string is described by the Worldsheet, the 2D surface it sweeps through spacetime.','<svg style=\"color: #FFD700; vertical-align: -1.948ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"39.386ex\" height=\"5.027ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -1361 17408.7 2222\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><defs><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-I-1D446\" d=\"M308 24Q367 24 416 76T466 197Q466 260 414 284Q308 311 278 321T236 341Q176 383 176 462Q176 523 208 573T273 648Q302 673 343 688T407 704H418H425Q521 704 564 640Q565 640 577 653T603 682T623 704Q624 704 627 704T632 705Q645 705 645 698T617 577T585 459T569 456Q549 456 549 465Q549 471 550 475Q550 478 551 494T553 520Q553 554 544 579T526 616T501 641Q465 662 419 662Q362 662 313 616T263 510Q263 480 278 458T319 427Q323 425 389 408T456 390Q490 379 522 342T554 242Q554 216 546 186Q541 164 528 137T492 78T426 18T332 -20Q320 -22 298 -22Q199 -22 144 33L134 44L106 13Q83 -14 78 -18T65 -22Q52 -22 52 -14Q52 -11 110 221Q112 227 130 227H143Q149 221 149 216Q149 214 148 207T144 186T142 153Q144 114 160 87T203 47T255 29T308 24Z\"></path><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-I-1D443\" d=\"M287 628Q287 635 230 637Q206 637 199 638T192 648Q192 649 194 659Q200 679 203 681T397 683Q587 682 600 680Q664 669 707 631T751 530Q751 453 685 389Q616 321 507 303Q500 302 402 301H307L277 182Q247 66 247 59Q247 55 248 54T255 50T272 48T305 46H336Q342 37 342 35Q342 19 335 5Q330 0 319 0Q316 0 282 1T182 2Q120 2 87 2T51 1Q33 1 33 11Q33 13 36 25Q40 41 44 43T67 46Q94 46 127 49Q141 52 146 61Q149 65 218 339T287 628ZM645 554Q645 567 643 575T634 597T609 619T560 635Q553 636 480 637Q463 637 445 637T416 636T404 636Q391 635 386