mi\"><use data-c=\"1D44B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-I-1D44B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(936.2,413) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"1D708\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-I-1D708\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"msub\" transform=\"translate(16027.6,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D702\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-I-1D702\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" transform=\"translate(530,-150) scale(0.707)\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D707\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-I-1D707\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(603,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D708\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-1-TEX-I-1D708\"></use></g></g></g></g></g></svg>','[]','[]','[\"string-dynamics-c7f093b6\",\"geometric-duality-8302add6\",\"coupling-duality-21f159be\",\"topological-generations-b47c92b8\"]'),
(2010740,'loop-quantum-gravity','theoretical-physics','Loop Quantum Gravity (LQG)','<p>Loop <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/quantum-gravity\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Quantum Gravity</strong></a> (LQG) is a non-perturbative, background-independent framework for quantizing <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/general-relativity\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>General Relativity</strong></a>. Unlike string theory, which assumes a pre-existing spacetime, LQG derives the geometry of the universe from first principles, describing space as a discrete, \"atomic\" fabric of <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/quantum-states-of-geometry\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Quantum States of Geometry</strong></a>.</p>\n\n                    <h3>1. Ashtekar Variables and the Connection Representation</h3>\n                    <p>The foundation of LQG lies in Abhay Ashtekar\'s reformulation of <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/general-relativity\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>General Relativity</strong></a> using variables similar to those in gauge theory. The state of the gravitational field is described by the <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/ashtekar-barbero-connection\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Ashtekar-Barbero Connection</strong></a> (\\( A_a^i \\))—an \\( SU(2) \\) gauge field—and its conjugate momentum, the <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/densitized-triad\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Densitized Triad</strong></a> (\\( E^a_i \\)), which represents the gravitational flux through a surface. This formulation includes the <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/immirzi-parameter\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Immirzi Parameter</strong></a> (\\( \\gamma \\)), a fundamental constant that scales the discrete units of area and volume.</p>\n\n                    <h3>2. Holonomy-Flux Algebra and Spin Networks</h3>\n                    <p>To achieve a mathematically well-defined quantization, LQG utilizes <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/holonomies\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Holonomies</strong></a> (parallel transport of the connection along edges) and <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/fluxes\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Fluxes</strong></a> (integrals of the triad over surfaces). The basis states of theory are <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/spin-networks\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Spin Networks</strong></a>—graphs where edges are labeled by spins (\\( j \\)) and vertices by <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/intertwiners\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Intertwiners</strong></a>. In this view, space is not a container for these networks; space <em>is</em> the spin network itself, with the nodes representing quanta of volume and the edges representing quanta of area.</p>\n\n                    <h3>3. The Discrete Spectra of Geometry</h3>\n                    <p>One of the most striking predictions of LQG is that geometry is <strong>Quantized</strong>. The <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/area-operator\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Area Operator</strong></a> (\\( \\hat{A} \\)) and <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/volume-operator\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Volume Operator</strong></a> (\\( \\hat{V} \\)) possess discrete spectra, meaning that space cannot be infinitely divided.\n                    \\[ A_j = 8\\pi \\ell_P^2 \\gamma \\sqrt{j(j+1)} \\]\n                    This discreteness provides a natural \"cutoff\" for the ultraviolet infinities that plague traditional quantum gravity, and it allows for a microscopic derivation of <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/black-hole-entropy\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Black Hole Entropy</strong></a> by counting the number of spin network states that form an isolated horizon.</p>\n\n                    <h3>4. Dynamics and Spin Foams</h3>\n                    <p>While spin networks describe the state of space at a fixed time, the time-evolution of these states is described by <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/spin-foams\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Spin Foams</strong></a>. A spin foam is a 2D complex that represents a \"history\" of spin networks, where the vertices represent the interaction and branching of space itself. This provides a covariant, path-integral-like approach to quantum gravity, allowing for the calculation of transition amplitudes between different geometric states.</p>\n\n                    <h3>5. Loop <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/quantum-cosmology\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Quantum Cosmology</strong></a> and the Big Bounce</h3>\n                    <p>Applying LQG to the early universe leads to <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/loop-quantum-cosmology-lqc\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Loop <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/quantum-cosmology\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Quantum Cosmology</strong></a> (LQC)</strong></a>. Theory predicts that as the universe contracts toward a singularity, the discrete nature of space creates a repulsive <a href=\"/physics/subtopic/quantum-force\" class=\"subtopic-link\"><strong>Quantum Force</strong></a> that becomes dominant at the Planck density. This results in a <strong>Big Bounce</strong>, where the universe transitions from a previous contracting phase to our current expansion, effectively resolving the classical Big Bang singularity.</p>\n\n<h3>Related Theoretical Frameworks</h3><p>The study of Loop Quantum Gravity (LQG) is intrinsically linked to the <strong><a href=\"/physics/subtopic/quantized\" class=\"subtopic-link\">Quantized Geometry</a></strong>, which provides the necessary analytical depth for understanding the underlying physical manifold.</p>','Loop Quantum Gravity (LQG) is a non-perturbative, background-independent framework for quantizing General Relativity. Unlike string theory, which assumes a pre-existing spacetime, LQG derives the geometry of the universe from first principles, describing space as a discrete, \"atomic\" fabric of Quantum States of Geometry. The foundation of LQG lies in Abhay Ashtekar\'s reformulation of General Relativity using variables similar to those in gauge theory.','Loop Quantum Gravity (LQG) is a non-perturbative, background-independent framework for quantizing General Relativity. Unlike string theory, which assumes a pre-existing spacetime, LQG derives the geometry of the universe from first principles, describing space as a discrete, \"atomic\" fabric of Quantum States of Geometry. The foundation of LQG lies in Abhay Ashtekar\'s reformulation of General Relativity using variables similar to those in gauge theory.','<svg style=\"color: #FFD700; vertical-align: -1.21ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"21.372ex\" height=\"4.208ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -1325.3 9446.4 1860\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><defs><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-I-1D434\" d=\"M208 74Q208 50 254 46Q272 46 272 35Q272 34 270 22Q267 8 264 4T251 0Q249 0 239 0T205 1T141 2Q70 2 50 0H42Q35 7 35 11Q37 38 48 46H62Q132 49 164 96Q170 102 345 401T523 704Q530 716 547 716H555H572Q578 707 578 706L606 383Q634 60 636 57Q641 46 701 46Q726 46 726 36Q726 34 723 22Q720 7 718 4T704 0Q701 0 690 0T651 1T578 2Q484 2 455 0H443Q437 6 437 9T439 27Q443 40 445 43L449 46H469Q523 49 533 63L521 213H283L249 155Q208 86 208 74ZM516 260Q516 271 504 416T490 562L463 519Q447 492 400 412L310 260L413 259Q516 259 516 260Z\"></path><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-I-1D457\" d=\"M297 596Q297 627 318 644T361 661Q378 661 389 651T403 623Q403 595 384 576T340 557Q322 557 310 567T297 596ZM288 376Q288 405 262 405Q240 405 220 393T185 362T161 325T144 293L137 279Q135 278 121 278H107Q101 284 101 286T105 299Q126 348 164 391T252 441Q253 441 260 441T272 442Q296 441 316 432Q341 418 354 401T367 348V332L318 133Q267 -67 264 -75Q246 -125 194 -164T75 -204Q25 -204 7 -183T-12 -137Q-12 -110 7 -91T53 -71Q70 -71 82 -81T95 -112Q95 -148 63 -167Q69 -168 77 -168Q111 -168 139 -140T182 -74L193 -32Q204 11 219 72T251 197T278 308T289 365Q289 372 288 376Z\"></path><path id=\"MJX-1-TEX-N-3D\" d=\"M56 347Q56 360 70 367H707Q722 359 722 347Q722 336 708 328L390 327H72Q56 332 56 347ZM56 153Q56 168 72 173H708Q722 163 722 153